'','none'),(4546,_binary 'Contains a list of log entries.','','none'),(4547,_binary 'WID','','11.2.5'),(4548,_binary 'The user on which the log entry as written.','','none'),(4549,_binary 'The actual message of the log entry.','','none'),(4550,_binary 'The variables of the log entry in a serialized format.','','none'),(4551,_binary 'Operation links for the event.','','none'),(4552,_binary 'URL of the previous page.','','none'),(4553,_binary 'Date when the event occurred.','','none'),(4554,_binary 'Replace variables','','none'),(4555,_binary 'One file only.Maximum @count files.','','none'),(4556,_binary 'Configure language support for content.','','11.2.5'),(4557,_binary 'Managing and displaying link fields','','none'),(4558,_binary 'Adding link text','','none'),(4559,_binary 'In the field settings you can define additional link text to be <em>optional</em> or <em>required</em> in any link field.','','none'),(4560,_binary 'Displaying link text','','none'),(4561,_binary 'If link text has been submitted for a URL, then by default this link text is displayed as a link to the URL. If you want to display both the link text <em>and</em> the URL, choose the appropriate link format from the drop-down menu in the <em>Manage display</em> page. If you only want to display the URL even if link text has been submitted, choose <em>Link</em> as the format, and then change its <em>Format settings</em> to display <em>URL only</em>.','','none'),(4562,_binary 'Adding attributes to links','','none'),(4563,_binary 'You can add attributes to links, by changing the <em>Format settings</em> in the <em>Manage display</em> page. Adding <em>rel=\"nofollow\"</em> notifies search engines that links should not be followed.','','none'),(4564,_binary 'Validating URLs','','none'),(4565,_binary 'Number (decimal)','','none'),(4566,_binary 'Number (float)','','none'),(4567,_binary 'Number (integer)','','none'),(4568,_binary 'Alias for @id','','none'),(4569,_binary 'Raw output for @id','','none'),(4570,_binary 'The Serialization module provides a service for serializing and deserializing data to and from formats such as JSON and XML.','','none'),(4571,_binary 'Serialization is the process of converting data structures like arrays and objects into a string. This allows the data to be represented in a way that is easy to exchange and store (for example, for transmission over the Internet or for storage in a local file system). These representations can then be deserialized to get back to the original data structures.','','none'),(4572,_binary 'The serializer splits this process into two parts. Normalization converts an object to a normalized array structure. Encoding takes that array and converts it to a string.','','none'),(4573,_binary 'The uninstall process removes all data related to a module.','','none'),(4574,_binary 'The date the term was last updated.','','none'),(4575,_binary 'The time that the term was last edited.','','none'),(4576,_binary 'Managing and displaying telephone fields','','none'),(4577,_binary 'Displaying telephone numbers as links','','none'),(4578,_binary 'The user account %name cannot be canceled.','','none'),(4579,_binary 'The handler for this item is broken or missing. The following details are available:','','none'),(4580,_binary 'Default actions','','none'),(4581,_binary 'Grouping @id','','none'),(4582,_binary 'Columns for @field','','none'),(4583,_binary 'Sortable for @field','','none'),(4584,_binary 'Default sort order for @field','','none'),(4585,_binary 'Default sort for @field','','none'),(4586,_binary 'Alignment for @field','','none'),(4587,_binary 'Separator for @field','','none'),(4588,_binary 'Hide empty column for @field','','none'),(4589,_binary 'Responsive setting for @field','','none'),(4590,_binary 'No default sort','','none'),(4591,_binary 'Page display settings','','none'),(4592,_binary 'Block display settings','','none'),(4593,_binary 'View basic information','','none'),(4594,_binary 'Allow embedded displays','','none'),(4595,_binary 'Embedded displays can be used in code via views_embed_view().','','none'),(4596,_binary 'Show SQL query','','none'),(4597,_binary 'Remove @title','','none'),(4598,_binary 'Weight for @id','','none'),(4599,_binary 'Group for @id','','none'),(4600,_binary 'Remove @id','','none'),(4601,_binary 'PHP date format','','none'),(4602,_binary '@group: @title','','none'),(4603,_binary 'Registering module','','11.2.5'),(4604,_binary 'Media types','','none'),(4605,_binary 'Not fully protected','','none'),(4606,_binary 'Reset your password','','none'),(4607,_binary 'Number of new comments','','none'),(4608,_binary 'Lists (Views)','','11.2.5'),(4609,_binary 'Simple configuration','','11.2.5'),(4610,_binary 'Configuration type','','none'),(4611,_binary 'Here is your configuration:','','none'),(4612,_binary 'Are you sure you want to update the %name @type?','','none'),(4613,_binary 'Missing ID key \"@id_key\" for this @entity_type import.','','none'),(4614,_binary 'An entity with this machine name already exists but the import did not specify a UUID.','','none'),(4615,_binary 'An entity with this machine name already exists but the UUID does not match.','','none'),(4616,_binary 'An entity with this UUID already exists but the machine name does not match.','','none'),(4617,_binary 'Fallback date format','','11.2.5'),(4618,_binary 'Configuration translation','','none'),(4619,_binary 'Translate the configuration.','','none'),(4620,_binary '@label fields','','none'),(4621,_binary 'Enter block, theme or category','','none'),(4622,_binary 'Enter a part of the block, theme or category to filter by.','','none'),(4623,_binary 'Translations for %label','','none'),(4624,_binary '@language (original)','','none'),(4625,_binary 'Enter label','','none'),(4626,_binary 'Enter a part of the label or description to filter by.','','none'),(4627,_binary 'Enter field or @bundle','','none'),(4628,_binary 'Add @language translation for %label','','none'),(4629,_binary 'Successfully saved @language translation.','','none'),(4630,_binary '@language translation of %label was deleted','','none'),(4631,_binary 'Edit @language translation for %label','','none'),(4632,_binary 'Successfully updated @language translation.','','none'),(4633,_binary '(Empty)','','none'),(4634,_binary 'About text formats','','11.2.5'),(4635,_binary 'Are you sure you want to apply the updated %name image effect to all images?','','none'),(4636,_binary 'This operation does not change the original images but the copies created for this style will be recreated.','','none'),(4637,_binary 'The image style %name has been flushed.','','none'),(4638,_binary 'Image to be shown if no image is uploaded.','','none'),(4639,_binary 'Action title','','none'),(4640,_binary 'The title shown above the actions dropdown.','','none'),(4641,_binary 'The machine-readable name must be unique, and can only contain lowercase letters, numbers, and underscores. Additionally, it can not be the reserved word \"custom\".','','none'),(4642,_binary '- Restricted access -','','none'),(4643,_binary 'Workflow type','','none'),(4644,_binary 'Sample content','','none'),(4645,_binary 'Display block title','','none'),(4646,_binary 'List of items','','none'),(4647,_binary 'Placing and moving blocks','','none'),(4648,_binary 'Demonstrating block regions for a theme','','none'),(4649,_binary 'Toggling between different themes','','none'),(4650,_binary 'Configuring block settings','','none'),(4651,_binary 'You can control the visibility of a block by restricting it to specific pages, content types, and/or roles by setting the appropriate options under <em>Visibility settings</em> of the block configuration.','','none'),(4652,_binary 'Unless you\'re experiencing problems with pagers related to this field, you should leave this at 0. If using multiple pagers on one page you may need to set this number to a higher value so as not to conflict within the ?page= array. Large values will add a lot of commas to your URLs, so avoid if possible.','','none'),(4653,_binary 'Pager ID: @id','','none'),(4654,_binary 'Enter the name of the configuration file without the <em>.yml</em> extension. (e.g. <em>system.site</em>)','','none'),(4655,_binary 'The sender\'s email','','none'),(4656,_binary 'The email of the person that is sending the contact message.','','none'),(4657,_binary 'Relate file entities to their usage.','','none'),(4658,_binary 'Managing and displaying file fields','','none'),(4659,_binary 'Allowing file extensions','','none'),(4660,_binary 'In the field settings, you can define the allowed file extensions (for example <em>pdf docx psd</em>) for the files that will be uploaded with the file field.','','none'),(4661,_binary 'Restricting the maximum file size','','none'),(4662,_binary 'The maximum file size that users can upload is limited by PHP settings of the server, but you can restrict by entering the desired value as the <em>Maximum upload size</em> setting. The maximum file size is automatically displayed to users in the help text of the file field.','','none'),(4663,_binary 'Displaying files and descriptions','','none'),(4664,_binary 'In the field settings, you can allow users to toggle whether individual files are displayed. In the display settings, you can then choose one of the following formats: <ul><li><em>Generic file</em> displays links to the files and adds icons that symbolize the file extensions. If <em>descriptions</em> are enabled and have been submitted, then the description is displayed instead of the file name.</li><li><em>URL to file</em> displays the full path to the file as plain text.</li><li><em>Table of files</em> lists links to the files and the file sizes in a table.</li><li><em>RSS enclosure</em> only displays the first file, and only in a RSS feed, formatted according to the RSS 2.0 syntax for enclosures.</li></ul> A file can still be linked to directly by its URI even if it is not displayed.','','none'),(4665,_binary 'Flag to control whether this file should be displayed when viewing content','','none'),(4666,_binary 'The log entry explaining the changes in this revision.','','11.2.5'),(4667,_binary 'At least one authentication provider must be defined for resource @id','','none'),(4668,_binary 'At least one format must be defined for resource @id','','none'),(4669,_binary 'The ID of the shortcut.','','none'),(4670,_binary 'The UUID of the shortcut.','','none'),(4671,_binary 'The bundle of the shortcut.','','none'),(4672,_binary 'Weight among shortcuts in the same shortcut set.','','none'),(4673,_binary 'Route name','','none'),(4674,_binary 'The language code of the shortcut.','','none'),(4675,_binary 'Shortcut link','','none'),(4676,_binary 'Rebuild access','','none'),(4677,_binary 'The rebuild_access setting is enabled in settings.php. It is recommended to have this setting disabled unless you are performing a rebuild.','','none'),(4678,_binary 'Relate nodes to taxonomy terms, specifying which vocabulary or vocabularies to use. This relationship will cause duplicated records if there are multiple terms.','','none'),(4679,_binary 'Taxonomy term ID','','none'),(4680,_binary 'Taxonomy term name','','none'),(4681,_binary 'Return to site content','','11.2.5'),(4682,_binary 'Preferred admin language code','','none'),(4683,_binary 'The user\'s preferred language code for receiving emails and viewing the site.','','none'),(4684,_binary 'Preferred language code','','none'),(4685,_binary 'The user\'s preferred language code for viewing administration pages.','','none'),(4686,_binary 'The name of this user.','','none'),(4687,_binary 'The password of this user (hashed).','','none'),(4688,_binary 'The email of this user.','','none'),(4689,_binary 'The timezone of this user.','','none'),(4690,_binary 'The time that the user was created.','','none'),(4691,_binary 'Initial email','','none'),(4692,_binary 'User ID from route context','','none'),(4693,_binary 'The Views module provides a back end to fetch information from content, user accounts, taxonomy terms, and other entities from the database and present it to the user as a grid, HTML list, table, unformatted list, etc. The resulting displays are known generally as <em>views</em>.','','none'),(4694,_binary 'Adding functionality to administrative pages','','none'),(4695,_binary 'The Views module adds functionality to some core administration pages. For example, <em>admin/content</em> uses Views to filter and sort content. With Views uninstalled, <em>admin/content</em> is more limited.','','none'),(4696,_binary 'Expanding Views functionality','','none'),(4697,_binary 'Changing the title here means it cannot be dynamically altered anymore.','','none'),(4698,_binary 'Validate @label','','none'),(4699,_binary 'Validate user has access to the %name','','none'),(4700,_binary 'Multiple arguments','','none'),(4701,_binary 'Single ID','','none'),(4702,_binary 'One or more IDs separated by , or +','','none'),(4703,_binary 'Tag based','','none'),(4704,_binary 'Tag based caching of data. Caches will persist until any related cache tags are invalidated.','','none'),(4705,_binary 'Name and description','','none'),(4706,_binary 'Administrative tags','','none'),(4707,_binary 'Enter a comma-separated list of words to describe your view.','','none'),(4708,_binary 'Click <em>Save</em>.','','11.2.5'),(4709,_binary 'Defines a field type for telephone numbers.','','none'),(4710,_binary 'simple configuration','','none'),(4711,_binary 'The staged configuration cannot be imported, because it originates from a different site than this site. You can only synchronize configuration between cloned instances of this site.','','none'),(4712,_binary 'The date the file created.','','none'),(4713,_binary 'The timestamp that the file was created.','','none'),(4714,_binary 'The timestamp that the file was last changed.','','none'),(4715,_binary 'Language based on a selected language.','','none'),(4716,_binary 'Menu links with lower weights are displayed before links with higher weights.','','none'),(4717,_binary 'The name of the user role.','','none'),(4718,_binary 'Influence','','none'),(4719,_binary 'Influence is a numeric multiplier used in ordering search results. A higher number means the corresponding factor has more influence on search results; zero means the factor is ignored. Changing these numbers does not require the search index to be rebuilt. Changes take effect immediately.','','none'),(4720,_binary 'Search page type','','none'),(4721,_binary '- Choose page type -','','none'),(4722,_binary 'No search pages have been configured.','','none'),(4723,_binary 'You must select the new search page type.','','none'),(4724,_binary 'Edit %label search page','','none'),(4725,_binary 'The %label search page has been enabled.','','none'),(4726,_binary 'The %label search page has been disabled.','','none'),(4727,_binary 'The default search page is now %label. Be sure to check the ordering of your search pages.','','none'),(4728,_binary 'The %label search page has been added.','','none'),(4729,_binary 'Save search page','','none'),(4730,_binary 'The %label search page has been updated.','','none'),(4731,_binary 'The label for this search page.','','none'),(4732,_binary 'The search page path must be unique.','','none'),(4733,_binary 'Managing and displaying text fields','','none'),(4734,_binary 'Creating short text fields','','none'),(4735,_binary 'Creating long text fields','','none'),(4736,_binary 'Trimming the text length','','none'),(4737,_binary 'On the <em>Manage display</em> page you can choose to display a trimmed version of the text, and if so, where to cut off the text.','','none'),(4738,_binary 'Displaying summaries instead of trimmed text','','none'),(4739,_binary 'Using text formats and editors','','none'),(4740,_binary 'Left','Text alignment','none'),(4741,_binary 'Center','Text alignment','none'),(4742,_binary 'Right','Text alignment','none'),(4743,_binary 'State label','','none'),(4744,_binary '%name: may not be longer than @max characters.','','11.2.5'),(4745,_binary 'A breakpoint separates the height or width of viewports (screens, printers, and other media output types) into steps. For instance, a width breakpoint of 40em creates two steps: one for widths up to 40em and one for widths above 40em. Breakpoints can be used to define when layouts should shift from one form to another, when images should be resized, and other changes that need to respond to changes in viewport height or width.','','none'),(4746,_binary 'Resolution multiplier','','none'),(4747,_binary 'Resolution multipliers are a measure of the viewport\'s device resolution, defined to be the ratio between the physical pixel size of the active device and the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Device_independent_pixel\">device-independent pixel</a> size. The Breakpoint module defines multipliers of 1, 1.5, and 2; when defining breakpoints, modules and themes can define which multipliers apply to each breakpoint.','','11.2.5'),(4748,_binary 'Defining breakpoints and breakpoint groups','','none'),(4749,_binary 'Modules and themes can use the API provided by the Breakpoint module to define breakpoints and breakpoint groups, and to assign resolution multipliers to breakpoints.','','none'),(4750,_binary 'Comment author name','Validation','none'),(4751,_binary 'Changing the text format to %text_format will permanently remove content that is not allowed in that text format.<br><br>Save your changes before switching the text format to avoid losing data.','','11.2.5'),(4752,_binary 'Entity view display','','11.2.5'),(4753,_binary 'Managing and displaying entity reference fields','','none'),(4754,_binary 'Selecting reference type','','none'),(4755,_binary 'In the field settings you can select which entity type you want to create a reference to.','','none'),(4756,_binary 'Filtering and sorting reference fields','','none'),(4757,_binary 'Depending on the chosen entity type, additional filtering and sorting options are available for the list of entities that can be referred to, in the field settings. For example, the list of users can be filtered by role and sorted by name or ID.','','none'),(4758,_binary 'Displaying a reference','','none'),(4759,_binary 'An entity reference can be displayed as a simple label with or without a link to the entity. Alternatively, the referenced entity can be displayed as a teaser (or any other available view mode) inside the referencing entity.','','none'),(4760,_binary 'Managing text formats','','none'),(4761,_binary 'Assigning roles to text formats','','none'),(4762,_binary 'Selecting filters','','none'),(4763,_binary 'Each filter can have additional configuration options. For example, for the \"Limit allowed HTML tags\" filter you need to define the list of HTML tags that the filter leaves in the text.','','none'),(4764,_binary 'When creating or editing data in a field that has text formats enabled, users can select the format under the field from the Text format select list.','','none'),(4765,_binary 'Import behavior','','none'),(4766,_binary 'The keywords to search for.','','none'),(4767,_binary 'Managing and displaying list fields','','none'),(4768,_binary 'Defining option keys and labels','','none'),(4769,_binary 'When you define the list options you can define a key and a label for each option in the list. The label will be shown to the users while the key gets stored in the database.','','none'),(4770,_binary 'Choosing list field type','','none'),(4771,_binary 'There are three types of list fields, which store different types of data: <em>float</em>, <em>integer</em> or, <em>text</em>. The <em>float</em> type allows storing approximate decimal values. The <em>integer</em> type allows storing whole numbers, such as years (for example, 2012) or values (for example, 1, 2, 5, 305). The <em>text</em> list field type allows storing text values. No matter which type of list field you choose, you can define whatever labels you wish for data entry.','','none'),(4772,_binary 'Dependency of required module @module','','none'),(4773,_binary 'Some of the pending updates cannot be applied because their dependencies were not met.','','none'),(4774,_binary 'The vocabulary to which the term is assigned.','','none'),(4775,_binary 'Managing user account fields','','none'),(4776,_binary 'The date the taxonomy was most recently updated.','','none'),(4777,_binary 'An entity field containing a UNIX timestamp of when the entity has been last updated.','','none'),(4778,_binary 'An entity field containing a UNIX timestamp of when the entity has been created.','','none'),(4779,_binary 'An entity field for storing a serialized array of values.','','none'),(4780,_binary 'Timestamp value','','none'),(4781,_binary 'Sends the message as plain text, using PHP\'s native mail() function.','','none'),(4782,_binary 'Mail collector','','none'),(4783,_binary 'Does not send the message, but stores it in Drupal within the state system. Used for testing.','','none'),(4784,_binary 'Synchronizing configuration','','none'),(4785,_binary 'Starting configuration synchronization.','','none'),(4786,_binary 'Configuration synchronization has encountered an error.','','none'),(4787,_binary 'Nothing to export.','','none'),(4788,_binary 'Administer responsive images','','none'),(4789,_binary 'Defined on the Appearance or Theme Settings page. You do not have the appropriate permissions to change the site logo.','','none'),(4790,_binary 'Defined on the Site Information page. You do not have the appropriate permissions to change the site logo.','','none'),(4791,_binary 'Toggle branding elements','','none'),(4792,_binary 'Choose which branding elements you want to show in this block instance.','','none'),(4793,_binary 'Site branding','','11.2.5'),(4794,_binary 'Rendering language','','none'),(4795,_binary 'Save and configure','','11.2.5'),(4796,_binary 'The \"@name\" option must contain a valid value. You may either leave the text field empty or enter a string li