dual error messages next to the form elements themselves. For more information, see the <a href=\":inline_form_error\">online documentation for the Inline Form Errors module</a>.','','none'),(7076,_binary 'Displaying error messages','','none'),(7077,_binary 'When a form is not filled in correctly (for example, if a required field is left blank), a warning message is displayed at the top of the form. This message links to the affected form elements, and individual error messages are displayed next to each form element.','','none'),(7078,_binary 'Displaying error messages in browsers with HTML5 form validation','','none'),(7079,_binary 'In browsers that support HTML5 form validation, users will first see the error messages generated by their browser. In this case, the inline form error messages are only displayed after the HTML5 validation errors have been resolved.','','none'),(7080,_binary 'Places error messages adjacent to form inputs, for improved usability and accessibility.','','none'),(7081,_binary 'Language format settings','','none'),(7082,_binary 'Include locked languages','','none'),(7083,_binary 'Creating media items','','none'),(7084,_binary 'When a new media item is created, the Media module records basic information about it, including the author, date of creation, and the <a href=\":media-type\">media type</a>. It also manages the <em>publishing options</em>, which define whether or not the item is published. Default settings can be configured for each type of media on your site.','','none'),(7085,_binary 'Creating custom media types','','none'),(7086,_binary 'The Media module gives users with the <em>Administer media types</em> permission the ability to <a href=\":media-new\">create new media types</a> in addition to the default ones already configured. Each media type has an associated media source (such as the image source) which support thumbnail generation and metadata extraction. Fields managed by the <a href=\":field\">Field module</a> may be added for storing that metadata, such as width and height, as well as any other associated values.','','none'),(7087,_binary 'The Media module also enables you to create multiple versions of any media item, and revert to older versions using the <em>Revision information</em> settings.','','none'),(7088,_binary 'The Media module makes a number of permissions available, which can be set by role on the <a href=\":permissions\">permissions page</a>.','','none'),(7089,_binary 'Add media type','','none'),(7090,_binary 'Manage media types.','','none'),(7091,_binary 'Administer media types','','none'),(7092,_binary 'Update own media','','none'),(7093,_binary 'Delete own media','','none'),(7094,_binary 'View all media revisions','','none'),(7095,_binary 'To view a revision, you also need permission to view the media item.','','none'),(7096,_binary 'Full URI to a folder where the media icons will be installed','','none'),(7097,_binary 'Whether the thumbnail downloads should be queued','','none'),(7098,_binary 'Media source settings','','none'),(7099,_binary '\"File\" media source configuration','','none'),(7100,_binary '\"Image\" media source configuration','','none'),(7101,_binary 'Edit %type_label @label','','none'),(7102,_binary '@type %label has been created.','','none'),(7103,_binary '@type %label has been updated.','','none'),(7104,_binary '@type: added %label.','','none'),(7105,_binary '@type: updated %label.','','none'),(7106,_binary '- Create -','','none'),(7107,_binary 'Select the field that will store essential information about the media item. If \"Create\" is selected a new field will be automatically created.','','none'),(7108,_binary '%field_type field will be automatically created on this type to store the essential information about the media item.','','none'),(7109,_binary '%field_name field is used to store the essential information about the media item.','','none'),(7110,_binary 'Media source that is responsible for additional logic related to this media type.','','none'),(7111,_binary 'Media source configuration','','none'),(7112,_binary 'Media sources can provide metadata fields such as title, caption, size information, credits, etc. Media can automatically save this metadata information to entity fields, which can be configured below. Information will only be mapped if the entity field is empty.','','none'),(7113,_binary 'Media will be automatically published when created.','','none'),(7114,_binary 'Automatically create new revisions. Users with the \"Administer media\" permission will be able to override this option.','','none'),(7115,_binary 'Download thumbnails via a queue. When using remote media sources, the thumbnail generation could be a slow process. Using a queue allows for this process to be handled in the background.','','none'),(7116,_binary 'The media type %name has been updated.','','none'),(7117,_binary 'The media type %name has been added.','','none'),(7118,_binary 'Added media type %name.','','none'),(7119,_binary 'No media types available. <a href=\":url\">Add media type</a>.','','none'),(7120,_binary 'The thumbnail of the media item.','','none'),(7121,_binary 'The time the media item was created.','','none'),(7122,_binary 'The time the media item was last edited.','','none'),(7123,_binary 'media type','','none'),(7124,_binary 'media types','','none'),(7125,_binary '%type is used by @count media item on your site. You can not remove this media type until you have removed all of the %type media items.%type is used by @count media items on your site. You can not remove this media type until you have removed all of the %type media items.','','none'),(7126,_binary 'Linked to media item','','none'),(7127,_binary 'Use local files for reusable media.','','none'),(7128,_binary 'Use local images for reusable media.','','none'),(7129,_binary 'Menu settings.','Validation','none'),(7130,_binary 'You can only change the menu settings for the <em>published</em> version of this content.','','none'),(7131,_binary 'To view a revision, you also need permission to view the content item.','','11.2.5'),(7132,_binary 'To revert a revision, you also need permission to edit the content item.','','11.2.5'),(7133,_binary 'To delete a revision, you also need permission to delete the content item.','','11.2.5'),(7134,_binary 'Path alias.','Validation','none'),(7135,_binary 'You can only change the URL alias for the <em>published</em> version of this content.','','none'),(7136,_binary 'REST support for content types (provided by the <a href=\":node\">Node</a> module) is enabled by default. To enable support for other content entity types, you can use a <a href=\":config\" target=\"blank\">process based on configuration editing</a> or the contributed <a href=\":restui\">REST UI module</a>.','','none'),(7137,_binary 'Limited date range','','none'),(7138,_binary 'Your PHP installation has a limited date range.','','none'),(7139,_binary 'You are running on a system where PHP is compiled or limited to using 32-bit integers. This will limit the range of dates and timestamps to the years 1901-2038. Read about the <a href=\":url\">limitations of 32-bit PHP</a>.','','none'),(7140,_binary 'A client error happened','','none'),(7141,_binary 'To run cron from outside the site, go to <a href=\":cron\" class=\"system-cron-settings__link\">@cron</a>','','none'),(7142,_binary 'Run times of individual cron jobs will be written to watchdog','','none'),(7143,_binary 'Delete temporary files after','','none'),(7144,_binary 'Temporary files are not referenced, but are in the file system and therefore may show up in administrative lists. <strong>Warning:</strong> If enabled, temporary files will be permanently deleted and may not be recoverable.','','none'),(7145,_binary 'This workflow is in use. You cannot remove this workflow until you have removed all content using it.','','none'),(7146,_binary 'Edit %label workflow','','none'),(7147,_binary 'This workflow state is in use. You cannot remove this workflow state until you have removed all content using it.','','none'),(7148,_binary 'Find and manage comments.','','11.2.5'),(7149,_binary 'The approved comments listing.','','11.2.5'),(7150,_binary 'Comments published','','11.2.5'),(7151,_binary 'The unapproved comments listing.','','11.2.5'),(7152,_binary 'Comments unapproved','','11.2.5'),(7153,_binary '{{ message }}','','11.2.5'),(7154,_binary 'Entity reference selection handler settings','','none'),(7155,_binary 'Default selection handler settings','','none'),(7156,_binary 'The field instance ID.','','none'),(7157,_binary 'The field instance data.','','none'),(7158,_binary 'The field type','','none'),(7159,_binary 'The field definition.','','none'),(7160,_binary 'The formatter settings.','','none'),(7161,_binary 'File selection handler settings','','none'),(7162,_binary 'Source module not found for @migration_id.','','none'),(7163,_binary 'Destination module not found for @migration_id.','','none'),(7164,_binary 'User selection handler settings','','none'),(7165,_binary 'Views selection handler settings','','none'),(7166,_binary 'Czechia','','none'),(7167,_binary 'Go to page @key','','none'),(7168,_binary '%workflow workflow: Use %transition transition.','','none'),(7169,_binary 'Offset must be a number greater than or equal to 0.','','none'),(7170,_binary 'Are you sure you want to remove the %label block?','','none'),(7171,_binary 'Select the @entity_type types for the @workflow workflow','','none'),(7172,_binary 'Select the @entity_type_plural_label for the @workflow workflow','','none'),(7173,_binary 'Make sure that <strong>access to the database</strong> for the old site is available from this new site.','','none'),(7174,_binary '<strong>If the old site has private files</strong>, a copy of its files directory must also be accessible on the host of this new site.','','none'),(7175,_binary '<strong>Do not add any content to the new site</strong> before upgrading. Any existing content is likely to be overwritten by the upgrade process. See <a href=\":url\">the upgrade preparation guide</a>.','','none'),(7176,_binary 'The upgrade can take a long time. It is better to upgrade from a local copy of your site instead of directly from your live site.','','none'),(7177,_binary '\"Audio\" media source configuration','','none'),(7178,_binary 'Access media overview','','none'),(7179,_binary 'Users with this permission can access the media overview page.','','none'),(7180,_binary '\"Video\" media source configuration','','none'),(7181,_binary 'Set default value','','11.2.5'),(7182,_binary 'Upgrade analysis report','','none'),(7183,_binary 'Page Actions','','none'),(7184,_binary 'Requires the \"View any unpublished content\" or \"View own unpublished content\" permission','','none'),(7185,_binary 'The %field_name entity reference field (entity_type: %entity_type, bundle: %bundle) no longer has any valid bundle it can reference. The field is not working correctly anymore and has to be adjusted.','','none'),(7186,_binary 'Compatible','','none'),(7187,_binary 'Moderation state filter','','none'),(7188,_binary 'Response failed validation.\nResponse:\n@data\n\nErrors:\n@errors','','none'),(7189,_binary 'Cannot change the install profile from %profile to %new_profile once Drupal is installed.','','none'),(7190,_binary 'Disclaimer block','','none'),(7191,_binary 'Entity action','','none'),(7192,_binary 'Use field label instead of the \"On\" label as the label.','','none'),(7193,_binary 'There is no moderated @label yet. Only pending versions of @label, such as drafts, are listed here.','','none'),(7194,_binary 'The image file is invalid or the image type is not allowed. Allowed types: %types','','none'),(7195,_binary 'The image was resized to fit within the maximum allowed dimensions of %dimensions pixels. The new dimensions of the resized image are %new_widthx%new_height pixels.','','none'),(7196,_binary 'The image was resized to fit within the maximum allowed height of %height pixels. The new dimensions of the resized image are %new_widthx%new_height pixels.','','none'),(7197,_binary 'The image was resized to fit within the maximum allowed width of %width pixels. The new dimensions of the resized image are %new_widthx%new_height pixels.','','none'),(7198,_binary 'One or more files could not be uploaded.','','none'),(7199,_binary 'Media display format settings','','none'),(7200,_binary 'Show playback controls','','none'),(7201,_binary 'Audio file display format settings','','none'),(7202,_binary 'Video file display format settings','','none'),(7203,_binary 'Replace the file name by its description when available','','none'),(7204,_binary 'Use description as link text','','none'),(7205,_binary 'Display the file using an HTML5 audio tag.','','none'),(7206,_binary 'Playback controls: %controls','','none'),(7207,_binary 'Multiple file display: Multiple HTML tags','','none'),(7208,_binary 'Multiple file display: One HTML tag with multiple sources','','none'),(7209,_binary 'Display the file using an HTML5 video tag.','','none'),(7210,_binary 'Root-relative file URL','','none'),(7211,_binary 'An entity field containing a file URI, and a computed root-relative file URL.','','none'),(7212,_binary '@title field is required if there is @uri input.','','none'),(7213,_binary 'The Media module manages the creation, editing, deletion, settings, and display of media. Items are typically images, documents, slideshows, YouTube videos, tweets, Instagram photos, etc. You can reference media items from any other content on your site. For more information, see the <a href=\":media\">online documentation for the Media module</a>.','','none'),(7214,_binary 'Listing media items','','none'),(7215,_binary 'Media items are listed at the <a href=\":media-collection\">media administration page</a>.','','none'),(7216,_binary 'Adding media to other content','','none'),(7217,_binary 'Users with permission to administer content types can add media support by adding a media reference field to the content type on the content type administration page. (The same is true of block types, taxonomy terms, user profiles, and other content that supports fields.) A media reference field can refer to any configured media type. It is possible to allow multiple media types in the same field.','','none'),(7218,_binary '<em>Media</em> reference fields offer several advantages over basic <em>File</em> and <em>Image</em> references:','','none'),(7219,_binary 'Media reference fields can reference multiple media types in the same field.','','none'),(7220,_binary 'Fields can also be added to media types themselves, which means that custom metadata like descriptions and taxonomy tags can be added for the referenced media. (Basic file and image fields do not support this.)','','none'),(7221,_binary 'Media types for audio and video files are provided by default, so there is no need for additional configuration to upload these media.','','none'),(7222,_binary 'Contributed or custom projects can provide additional media sources (such as third-party websites, Twitter, etc.).','','none'),(7223,_binary 'Existing media items can be reused on any other content items with a media reference field.','','none'),(7224,_binary 'For more information, see the <a href=\"@help_url\">Media help page</a>.','','none'),(7225,_binary 'Media Name','','none'),(7226,_binary '%type_name: Create new media','','none'),(7227,_binary '%type_name: Edit own media','','none'),(7228,_binary '%type_name: Edit any media','','none'),(7229,_binary '%type_name: Delete own media','','none'),(7230,_binary '%type_name: Delete any media','','none'),(7231,_binary '<em>The media source cannot be changed after the media type is created.</em>','','none'),(7232,_binary 'Use audio files for reusable media.','','none'),(7233,_binary 'Use video files for reusable media.','','none'),(7234,_binary 'The destination system contains data which was not created by a migration.','','none'),(7235,_binary 'Migrate Drupal settings','','none'),(7236,_binary 'source_module enforcement tags','','none'),(7237,_binary 'Old site','','none'),(7238,_binary 'The site you want to upgrade.','','none'),(7239,_binary 'New site','','none'),(7240,_binary 'Preparation steps','','none'),(7241,_binary 'WARNING: Content may be overwritten on your new site.','','none'),(7242,_binary 'I acknowledge I may lose data. Continue anyway.','','none'),(7243,_binary 'There is conflicting content of these types:','','none'),(7244,_binary 'On the <a href=\":cache-settings\">Performance page</a>, you can configure how long browsers and proxies may cache pages based on the Cache-Control header; this setting is ignored by the Internal Page Cache module, which caches pages permanently until invalidation, unless they carry an Expires header. There is no other configuration.','','none'),(7245,_binary 'The Settings Tray module allows users with the <a href=\":administer_block_permission\">Administer blocks</a> and <a href=\":contextual_permission\">Use contextual links</a> permissions to edit blocks without visiting a separate page. For more information, see the <a href=\":handbook_url\">online documentation for the Settings Tray module</a>.','','none'),(7246,_binary 'Editing blocks in place','','none'),(7247,_binary 'To edit blocks in place, either click the <strong>Edit</strong> button in the toolbar and then click on the block, or choose \"Quick edit\" from the block\'s contextual link. (See the <a href=\":contextual\">Contextual Links module help</a> for more information about how to use contextual links.)','','none'),(7248,_binary 'The Settings Tray for the block will open in a sidebar, with a compact form for configuring what the block shows.','','none'),(7249,_binary 'Save the form and the changes will be immediately visible on the page.','','none'),(7250,_binary 'Specify the format of the syslog entry. Available variables are: <dl><dt><code>!base_url</code></dt><dd>Base URL of the site.</dd><dt><code>!timestamp</code></dt><dd>Unix timestamp of the log entry.</dd><dt><code>!type</code></dt><dd>The category to which this message belongs.</dd><dt><code>!ip</code></dt><dd>IP address of the user triggering the message.</dd><dt><code>!request_uri</code></dt><dd>The requested URI.</dd><dt><code>!referer</code></dt><dd>HTTP Referer if available.</dd><dt><code>!severity</code></dt><dd>The severity level of the event; ranges from 0 (Emergency) to 7 (Debug).</dd><dt><code>!uid</code></dt><dd>User ID.</dd><dt><code>!link</code></dt><dd>A link to associate with the message.</dd><dt><code>!message</code></dt><dd>The message to store in the log.</dd></dl>','','none'),(7251,_binary 'Either the path \'%path\' is invalid or you do not have access to it.','','none'),(7252,_binary '%capital_name contains the following terms.','','none'),(7253,_binary '%capital_name contains terms grouped under parent terms','','none'),(7254,_binary '%capital_name contains terms with multiple parents.','','none'),(7255,_binary 'Access the taxonomy vocabulary overview page','','11.2.5'),(7256,_binary 'Get an overview of all taxonomy vocabularies.','','11.2.5'),(7257,_binary '%vocabulary: Create terms','','11.2.5'),(7258,_binary '%vocabulary: Delete terms','','11.2.5'),(7259,_binary '%vocabulary: Edit terms','','11.2.5'),(7260,_binary 'Output the URL as text','','none'),(7261,_binary 'Output an absolute link','','none'),(7262,_binary 'Min placeholder','','none'),(7263,_binary 'Max placeholder','','none'),(7264,_binary 'Enable this option to output an absolute link. Required if you want to use the path as a link destination.','','none'),(7265,_binary 'Enforce a <code>destination</code> parameter in the link to return the user to the original view upon completing the link action. Most operations include a destination by default and this setting is no longer needed.','','none'),(7266,_binary 'Hint text that appears inside the Min field when empty.','','none'),(7267,_binary 'Hint text that appears inside the Max field when empty.','','none'),(7268,_binary 'Hint text that appears inside the field when empty.','','none'),(7269,_binary 'There are no workflow types available. In order to create workflows you need to install a module that provides a workflow type. For example, the <a href=\":content-moderation\">Content Moderation</a> module provides a workflow type that enables workflows for content entities.','','none'),(7270,_binary 'Transition label','','none'),(7271,_binary 'Find and moderate content.','','none'),(7272,_binary 'No moderated content available. Only pending versions of content, such as drafts, are listed here.','','none'),(7273,_binary 'No front page content has been created yet.<br/>Follow the <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/user_guide/en/index.html\">User Guide</a> to start building your site.','','11.2.5'),(7274,_binary 'A locally hosted audio file.','','none'),(7275,_binary 'A locally hosted video file.','','none'),(7276,_binary 'Workspace name','','none'),(7277,_binary 'Name (A-Z)','','none'),(7278,_binary 'Name (Z-A)','','none'),(7279,_binary 'A flag indicating whether this was a default revision when it was saved.','','none'),(7280,_binary 'Entity untranslatable fields','Validation','none'),(7281,_binary 'The Content Moderation module allows you to expand on Drupal\'s \"unpublished\" and \"published\" states for content. It allows you to have a published version that is live, but have a separate working copy that is undergoing review before it is published. This is achieved by using <a href=\":workflows\">Workflows</a> to apply different states and transitions to entities as needed. For more information, see the <a href=\":content_moderation\">online documentation for the Content Moderation module</a>.','','none'),(7282,_binary 'Applying workflows','','none'),(7283,_binary 'Moderating content','','none'),(7284,_binary 'You can view a list of content awaiting moderation on the <a href=\":moderated\">moderated content page</a>. This will show any content in an unpublished state, such as Draft or Archived, to help surface content that requires more work from content editors.','','none'),(7285,_binary 'Each transition is exposed as a permission. If a user has the permission for a transition, they can use the transition to change the state of the content item, from Draft to Published.','','none'),(7286,_binary 'Hide non translatable fields on translation forms','','none'),(7287,_binary 'Content translation bundle settings','','none'),(7288,_binary 'Bundle settings values','','none'),(7289,_binary 'Fields that apply to all languages are hidden to avoid conflicting changes. <a href=\":url\">Edit them on the original language form</a>.','','none'),(7290,_binary 'Content translation synchronized fields','Validation','none'),(7291,_binary 'Non-translatable field elements can only be changed when updating the current revision.','','none'),(7292,_binary 'Non-translatable field elements can only be changed when updating the original language.','','none'),(7293,_binary 'The node language.','','none'),(7294,_binary 'This layout builder tool allows you to configure the layout of the main content area.','','none'),(7295,_binary 'To manage other areas of the page, use the <a href=\"@block-ui\">block administration page</a>.','','none'),(7296,_binary 'To manage other areas of the page, use the block administration page.','','none'),(7297,_binary 'For more information, see the <a href=\":layout-builder-documentation\">online documentation for the Layout Builder module</a>.','','none'),(7298,_binary 'Configure any layout','','none'),(7299,_binary 'Configure section','','none'),(7300,_binary 'Per-view-mode Layout Builder settings','','none'),(7301,_binary 'Allow a customized layout','','none'),(7302,_binary 'Layout section','','none'),(7303,_binary 'Edit layout for %label','','none'),(7304,_binary 'The layout override has been saved.','','none'),(7305,_binary 'The changes to the layout have been discarded.','','none'),(7306,_bin