href=\":docs\">Learn more about securing your site with JSON:API.</a>','','none'),(7809,_binary 'i18n language','','none'),(7810,_binary 'i18n mode','','none'),(7811,_binary 'Add section <span class=\"visually-hidden\">at end of layout</span>','','none'),(7812,_binary 'Add section <span class=\"visually-hidden\">at start of layout</span>','','none'),(7813,_binary 'Add section <span class=\"visually-hidden\">between @first and @second</span>','','none'),(7814,_binary 'Add block <span class=\"visually-hidden\">in @section, @region region</span>','','none'),(7815,_binary '@region region in @section','','none'),(7816,_binary 'Remove @section','','none'),(7817,_binary 'Configure @section','','none'),(7818,_binary '@section, Region: @region','','none'),(7819,_binary 'Block label','','none'),(7820,_binary 'Are you sure you want to remove @section?','','none'),(7821,_binary 'The %media-embed-filter-label filter requires <code>&lt;drupal-media&gt;</code> among the allowed HTML tags.','','none'),(7822,_binary 'The <code>&lt;drupal-media&gt;</code> tag in the allowed HTML tags is missing the following attributes: <code>%list</code>.','','none'),(7823,_binary 'The %media-embed-filter-label filter needs to be placed after the %filter filter.The %media-embed-filter-label filter needs to be placed after the following filters: %filters.','','none'),(7824,_binary 'If you would like to change this, <a href=\":display\">add an image style to the %field_name field</a>.','','none'),(7825,_binary 'The default display for the %type media type is not currently using an image style on the %field_name field. Not using an image style can lead to much larger file downloads. @action_item','','none'),(7826,_binary 'The view mode that is used by default','','none'),(7827,_binary 'Media types selectable in the Media Library','','none'),(7828,_binary 'View modes selectable in the \"Edit media\" dialog','','none'),(7829,_binary 'Filters out unpublished media if the current user cannot view it.','','none'),(7830,_binary 'The view mode that an embedded media item should be displayed in by default. This can be overridden using the <code>data-view-mode</code> attribute.','','none'),(7831,_binary 'If none are selected, all will be allowed.','','none'),(7832,_binary 'View modes selectable in the \'Edit media\' dialog','','none'),(7833,_binary 'If two or more view modes are selected, users will be able to update the view mode that an embedded media item should be displayed in after it has been embedded.  If less than two view modes are selected, media will be embedded using the default view mode and no view mode options will appear after a media item has been embedded.','','none'),(7834,_binary 'The referenced media source is missing and needs to be re-embedded.','','none'),(7835,_binary '\n      <p>You can embed media items:</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li>Choose which media item to embed: <code>&lt;drupal-media data-entity-uuid=\"07bf3a2e-1941-4a44-9b02-2d1d7a41ec0e\" /&gt;</code></li>\n        <li>Optionally also choose a view mode: <code>data-view-mode=\"tiny_embed\"</code>, otherwise the default view mode is used.</li>\n        <li>The <code>data-entity-type=\"media\"</code> attribute is required for consistency.</li>\n      </ul>','','none'),(7836,_binary 'You can embed media items (using the <code>&lt;drupal-media&gt;</code> tag).','','none'),(7837,_binary 'During rendering of embedded media: recursive rendering detected for %entity_id. Aborting rendering.','','none'),(7838,_binary 'During rendering of embedded media: the media item with UUID \"@uuid\" does not exist.','','none'),(7839,_binary 'During rendering of embedded media: the view mode \"@view-mode-id\" does not exist.','','none'),(7840,_binary 'Embeds media items using a custom tag, <code>&lt;drupal-media&gt;</code>. If used in conjunction with the \'Align/Caption\' filters, make sure this filter is configured to run after them.','','none'),(7841,_binary 'The Media Library module provides a rich, visual interface for managing media, and allows media to be reused in entity reference fields or embedded into text content. It overrides the <a href=\":media-collection\">media administration page</a>, allowing users to toggle between the existing table-style interface and a new grid-style interface for browsing and performing administrative operations on media.','','none'),(7842,_binary 'To learn more about media management, begin by reviewing the <a href=\":media-help\">documentation for the Media module</a>. For more information about the media library and related functionality, see the <a href=\":media-library-handbook\">online documentation for the Media Library module</a>.','','none'),(7843,_binary 'Selection dialog','','none'),(7844,_binary 'When selecting media for an entity reference field or a text editor, Media Library opens a modal dialog to help users easily find and select media. The modal dialog can toggle between a grid-style and table-style interface, and new media items can be uploaded directly into it.','','none'),(7845,_binary 'Within the dialog, media items are divided up by type. If more than one media type can be selected by the user, the available types will be displayed as a set of vertical tabs. To users who have appropriate permissions, each media type may also present a short form allowing you to upload or create new media items of that type.','','none'),(7846,_binary 'Grid-style vs. table-style interface','','none'),(7847,_binary 'The Media Library module provides a new grid-style interface for the media administration page that displays media as thumbnails, with minimal textual information, allowing users to visually browse media in their site. The existing table-style interface is better suited to displaying additional information about media items, in addition to being more accessible to users with assistive technology.','','none'),(7848,_binary 'Reusing media in entity reference fields','','none'),(7849,_binary 'Any entity reference field that references media can use the media library. To enable, configure the form display for the field to use the \"Media library\" widget.','','none'),(7850,_binary 'Embedding media in text content','','none'),(7851,_binary 'To use the media library within CKEditor, you must add the \"Insert from Media Library\" button to the CKEditor toolbar, and enable the \"Embed media\" filter in the text format associated with the text editor.','','none'),(7852,_binary 'Both the table-style and grid-style interfaces are regular views and can be customized via the Views UI, including sorting and filtering. This is the case for both the administration page and the modal dialog.','','none'),(7853,_binary 'Media Library settings','','none'),(7854,_binary 'Manage Media Library settings.','','none'),(7855,_binary 'Media library settings','','none'),(7856,_binary 'Enable advanced UI','','none'),(7857,_binary 'A path alias set for a specific language will always be used when displaying this page in that language, and takes precedence over path aliases set as <em>- Not specified -</em>.','','none'),(7858,_binary 'No path aliases available. <a href=\":link\">Add URL alias</a>.','','none'),(7859,_binary 'The search page that the form submits to, or Default for the default search page.','','none'),(7860,_binary 'Experimental themes found: %theme_list. Experimental themes are provided for testing purposes only. Use at your own risk.','','none'),(7861,_binary 'Configuration sync directory','','11.2.5'),(7862,_binary 'Your %file file must define the %setting setting as a string containing the directory in which configuration files can be found.','','none'),(7863,_binary 'experimental theme','','none'),(7864,_binary 'A local file system path where temporary files will be stored. This directory should not be accessible over the web. This must be changed in settings.php.','','none'),(7865,_binary 'Are you sure you wish to install an experimental theme?','','none'),(7866,_binary 'Experimental themes are provided for testing purposes only. Use at your own risk.','','none'),(7867,_binary 'The following themes are experimental: @themes','','none'),(7868,_binary 'Internationalization mode.','','none'),(7869,_binary 'Language from the taxonomy_vocabulary table.','','none'),(7870,_binary 'Translation of either the name or the description.','','none'),(7871,_binary 'Language code from locales_target table','','none'),(7872,_binary 'Require summary','','11.2.5'),(7873,_binary 'Always show summary','','none'),(7874,_binary 'The summary will also be visible when marked as required.','','11.2.5'),(7875,_binary 'The summary field is required for @name','','none'),(7876,_binary 'Always show the summary field','','none'),(7877,_binary 'Summary field will always be visible','','none'),(7878,_binary 'Too many password recovery requests from your IP address. It is temporarily blocked. Try again later or contact the site administrator.','','none'),(7879,_binary 'Limit the available operators','','none'),(7880,_binary 'List of available operators','','none'),(7881,_binary 'Limit the available operators to be shown on the exposed filter.','','none'),(7882,_binary 'Restrict operators to','','none'),(7883,_binary 'Selecting none will make all of them available.','','none'),(7884,_binary 'You selected the \"@operator\" operator as the default value but is not included in the list of limited operators.','','none'),(7885,_binary 'Provides an interface to create workflows with transitions between different states (for example publication or user status) provided by other modules.','','none'),(7886,_binary 'Indicates the workspace that this revision belongs to.','','none'),(7887,_binary 'Switch to Live','','none'),(7888,_binary 'Would you like to switch to the live version of the site?','','none'),(7889,_binary 'Switch to the live version of the site.','','none'),(7890,_binary 'You are now viewing the live version of the site.','','none'),(7891,_binary 'Media Library thumbnail (220×220)','','none'),(7892,_binary 'Delete {{ name }}','','none'),(7893,_binary 'An uploaded file or document, such as a PDF.','','none'),(7894,_binary 'Viewing help topics','','none'),(7895,_binary 'The top-level help topics are listed on the main <a href=\":help_page\">Help page</a>. Links to other topics, including non-top-level help topics, can be found under the \"Related\" heading when viewing a topic page.','','none'),(7896,_binary 'Providing help topics','','none'),(7897,_binary 'Translating help topics','','none'),(7898,_binary 'The title and body text of help topics provided by contributed modules and themes are translatable using the <a href=\":locale_help\">Interface Translation module</a>. Topics provided by custom modules and themes are also translatable if they have been viewed at least once in a non-English language, which triggers putting their translatable text into the translation database.','','none'),(7899,_binary 'Configuring help search','','11.2.5'),(7900,_binary 'See the <a href=\":help_page\">Help page</a> for more topics.','','none'),(7901,_binary 'Help search','','none'),(7902,_binary 'Configure the settings of a block that was previously placed in a region of a theme.','','11.2.5'),(7903,_binary 'Click the name of the theme that contains the block.','','11.2.5'),(7904,_binary 'Optionally, click <em>Demonstrate block regions</em> to see the regions of the theme.','','11.2.5'),(7905,_binary 'If you only want to change the region where a block is located, or the ordering of blocks within a region, drag blocks to their desired positions and click <em>Save blocks</em>.','','11.2.5'),(7906,_binary 'If you want to change additional settings, find the region where the block you want to update is currently located, and click <em>Configure</em> in the line of the block description.','','11.2.5'),(7907,_binary 'Edit the block\'s settings. The available settings vary depending on the module that provides the block, but for all blocks you can change:','','11.2.5'),(7908,_binary '<em>Block title</em>: The heading for the block on your site -- for some blocks, you will need to check the <em>Override title</em> checkbox in order to enter a title','','11.2.5'),(7909,_binary '<em>Display title</em>: Check the box if you want the title displayed','','11.2.5'),(7910,_binary '<em>Visibility</em>: Add conditions for when the block should be displayed','','11.2.5'),(7911,_binary '<em>Region</em>: Change the theme region the block is displayed in','','11.2.5'),(7912,_binary 'Click <em>Save block</em>.','','11.2.5'),(7913,_binary 'What are blocks?','','11.2.5'),(7914,_binary 'Blocks are boxes of content rendered into an area, or region, of a web page of your site. Blocks are placed and configured specifically for each theme.','','11.2.5'),(7915,_binary 'What is the block description?','','11.2.5'),(7916,_binary 'The block description is an identification name for a block, which is shown in the administrative interface. It is not displayed on the site.','','11.2.5'),(7917,_binary 'What is the block title?','','11.2.5'),(7918,_binary 'The block title is the heading that is optionally shown to site visitors when the block is placed in a region.','','11.2.5'),(7919,_binary 'Place a block into a theme\'s region.','','11.2.5'),(7920,_binary 'Click the name of the theme that you want to place the block in.','','11.2.5'),(7921,_binary 'Find the region where you want the block, and click <em>Place block</em> in that region. A modal dialog will pop up.','','11.2.5'),(7922,_binary 'Find the block you want to place and click <em>Place block</em>. A <em>Configure block</em> modal dialog will pop up.','','11.2.5'),(7923,_binary 'Enter a description of your block (to be shown to administrators) and the body text for your block.','','11.2.5'),(7924,_binary 'Enter a label for this block type (shown in the administrative interface). Optionally, edit the automatically-generated machine name or the description.','','11.2.5'),(7925,_binary 'Click <em>Save</em>. You will be returned to the <em>Block types</em> page.','','11.2.5'),(7926,_binary 'Click <em>Manage fields</em> in the row of your new block type, and add the desired fields to your block type.','','11.2.5'),(7927,_binary 'Optionally, click <em>Manage form display</em> or <em>Manage display</em> to change the editing form or field display for your block type.','','11.2.5'),(7928,_binary 'Use contextual links to access administrative tasks without navigating the administrative menu.','','11.2.5'),(7929,_binary 'What are contextual links?','','11.2.5'),(7930,_binary '<em>Contextual links</em> give users with the <em>Use contextual links</em> permission quick access to administrative tasks related to areas of non-administrative pages. For example, if a page on your site displays a block, the block would have a contextual link that would allow users with permission to configure the block. If the block contains a menu or a view, it would also have a contextual link for editing the menu links or the view. Clicking a contextual link takes you to the related administrative page directly, without needing to navigate through the administrative menu system.','','11.2.5'),(7931,_binary 'Make sure that the core Contextual Links module is installed, and that you have a role with the <em>Use contextual links</em> permission. Optionally, make sure that a toolbar module is installed (either the core Toolbar module or a contributed module replacement).','','11.2.5'),(7932,_binary 'Visit a non-administrative page on your site, such as the home page.','','11.2.5'),(7933,_binary 'Locate a block or another area on the page that you want to edit or configure.','','11.2.5'),(7934,_binary 'Make the contextual links button visible by hovering your mouse over that area in the page. In most themes, this button looks like a pencil and is placed in the upper right corner of the page area (upper left for right-to-left languages), and hovering will also temporarily outline the affected area. Alternatively, click the contextual links toggle button on the right end of the toolbar (left end for right-to-left languages), which will make all contextual link buttons on the page visible until it is clicked again.','','11.2.5'),(7935,_binary 'While the contextual links button for the area of interest is visible, click the button to display the list of links for that area. Click a link in the list to visit the corresponding administrative page.','','11.2.5'),(7936,_binary 'Complete your administrative task and save your settings, or cancel the action. You should be returned to the page you started from.','','11.2.5'),(7937,_binary 'What are security updates?','','11.2.5'),(7938,_binary 'Any software occasionally has bugs, and sometimes these bugs have security implications. When security bugs are fixed in the core software, modules, or themes that your site uses, they are released in a <em>security update</em>. You will need to apply security updates in order to keep your site secure.','','11.2.5'),(7939,_binary 'Security tasks','','11.2.5'),(7940,_binary 'Keeping track of updates, updating the core software, and updating contributed modules and/or themes are all part of keeping your site secure. See the related topics listed below for specific tasks.','','11.2.5'),(7941,_binary 'Overview of accessibility','','11.2.5'),(7942,_binary 'The default drag-and-drop user interface for ordering tables in the administrative interface presents a challenge for some users, including keyboard-only users and users of screen readers and other assistive technology. The drag-and-drop interface can be disabled in a table by clicking a link labeled <em>Show row weights</em> above the table. The replacement interface allows users to order the table by choosing numerical weights (with increasing numbers) instead of dragging table rows.','','11.2.5'),(7943,_binary 'Administrative interface overview','','11.2.5'),(7944,_binary 'A menu system, which you can navigate to find pages for administrative tasks. The core Toolbar module displays this menu on the top or left side of the page (right side in right-to-left languages). There are also contributed module replacements for the core Toolbar module, with additional features, such as the <a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/project/admin_toolbar\">Admin Toolbar module</a>.','','11.2.5'),(7945,_binary 'The core Shortcuts module enhances the toolbar with a configurable list of links to commonly-used tasks.','','11.2.5'),(7946,_binary 'If you install the core Contextual Links module, non-administrative pages will contain links leading to related administrative tasks.','','11.2.5'),(7947,_binary 'The core Help module displays help topics, and provides a Help block that can be placed on administrative pages to provide an overview of their functionality.','','11.2.5'),(7948,_binary 'See the related topics listed below for specific tasks.','','11.2.5'),(7949,_binary 'Set up your site so that users can search for help.','','11.2.5'),(7950,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Search and metadata</em> &gt; <em>Search pages</em>.','','11.2.5'),(7951,_binary 'Verify that a Help search page is listed in the <em>Search pages</em> section. If not, add a new page of type <em>Help</em>.','','11.2.5'),(7952,_binary 'Create, view, and use a set of shortcuts to access administrative pages.','','11.2.5'),(7953,_binary 'What are shortcuts?','','11.2.5'),(7954,_binary '<em>Shortcuts</em> are quick links to administrative pages; they are managed by the core Shortcut module. A site can have one or more <em>shortcut sets</em>, which can be shared by one or more users (by default, there is only one set shared by all users); each set contains a limited number of shortcuts. Users need <em>Use shortcuts</em> permission to view shortcuts; <em>Edit current shortcut set</em> permission to add, delete, or edit the shortcuts in the set assigned to them; and <em>Select any shortcut set</em> permission to select a different shortcut set when editing their user profile. There is also an <em>Administer shortcuts</em> permission, which allows an administrator to do any of these actions, as well as select shortcut sets for other users.','','11.2.5'),(7955,_binary 'Navigate to an administrative page that you want in your shortcut list.','','11.2.5'),(7956,_binary 'Repeat until all the desired links have been added to your shortcut set.','','11.2.5'),(7957,_binary 'Click <em>Shortcuts</em> in the toolbar to display your shortcuts, and verify that the list is complete.','','11.2.5'),(7958,_binary 'Optionally, click <em>Edit shortcuts</em> at the right end of the shortcut list (left end in right-to-left languages), to remove links or change their order.','','11.2.5'),(7959,_binary 'Click any link in the shortcut bar to go directly to the administrative page.','','11.2.5'),(7960,_binary 'Configure the basic settings of your site, including the site name, slogan, main email address, default time zone, default country, and the date formats to use.','','11.2.5'),(7961,_binary 'Enter the site name, slogan, and main email address for your site.','','11.2.5'),(7962,_binary 'Click <em>Save configuration</em>. You should see a message indicating that the settings were saved.','','11.2.5'),(7963,_binary 'Select the default country and default time zone for your site.','','11.2.5'),(7964,_binary 'Look at the <em>Patterns</em> for the Default long, medium, and short date formats. If any of them does not match the date format you want to use on your site, click <em>Edit</em> in that row to edit the format.','','11.2.5'),(7965,_binary 'Adjust the <em>Format string</em> until the <em>Displayed</em> format matches what you want. (Date format strings are composed of PHP date format codes.)','','11.2.5'),(7966,_binary 'Click <em>Save format</em>. You should see a message indicating that the format was saved.','','11.2.5'),(7967,_binary 'Repeat the previous three steps for any other date formats that need to be changed.','','11.2.5'),(7968,_binary 'Set up your site to respond appropriately to site errors, including 403 and 404 page responses.','','11.2.5'),(7969,_binary 'What are 403 and 404 responses?','','11.2.5'),(7970,_binary 'When a user visits a web page, the web server sends a response code in addition to the page content. A normal, non-error response has code 200. If the page does not exist on the site, the response code is 404. If the page exists, but the user is not authorized to visit the page, the response code is 403. The core software provides default responses for both 403 and 404 codes, but if you prefer, you can create your own pages for each.','','11.2.5'),(7971,_binary 'What other errors can occur?','','11.2.5'),(7972,_binary 'Under some situations, your site can generate error messages. These can be due to user errors (such as entering invalid values in a form, or incorrect configuration), PHP runtime errors, or software bugs. Some errors may result in a <em>white screen of death</em> (a totally blank web page response); less drastic errors will generate error messages. You can configure what happens when an error message is generated.','','11.2.5'),(7973,_binary 'If desired, create pages to use for 403 and 404 responses. Note the URLs for these pages.','','11.2.5'),(7974,_binary 'For a production site, select <em>None</em> under <em>Error messages to display</em>. For a site that is in development, select one of the other options, so that you are more aware of the errors the site is generating.','','11.2.5'),(7975,_binary 'Configure settings related to how user accounts are created and deleted.','','11.2.5'),(7976,_binary 'What are the settings related to user account creation and deletion?','','11.2.5'),(7977,_binary 'You can make it possible for new users to register themselves for accounts, with or without email verification or administrative approval. Or, you can make it so only administrators with <em>Administer users</em> permission can register new users.','','11.2.5'),(7978,_binary 'You can configure what happens to content that a user created, if their account is <em>canceled</em> (deleted).','','11.2.5'),(7979,_binary 'You can edit the email messages that are sent to users when their accounts are pending, approved, created, blocked, or canceled, or when they request a password reset.','','11.2.5'),(7980,_binary 'What are variables in email message text?','','11.2.5'),(7981,_binary '<em>Variables</em> are short text strings, enclosed in square brackets [], that you can insert into configured email message text. When an individual message is generated, data from your site is substituted for the variables. Some commonly-used variables are:','','11.2.5'),(7982,_binary '[site:login-url]: The URL where users can log in to your site.','','11.2.5'),(7983,_binary '[user:display-name]: The user\'s displayed name.','','11.2.5'),(7984,_binary '[user:mail]: The user\'s email alias.','','11.2.5'),(7985,_binary '[user:one-time-login-url]: An expiring URL that a user can use to log in once, if they need to reset their password.','','11.2.5'),(7986,_binary 'Select the method you want to use for creating user accounts, and check or uncheck the box that requires email verification, to match the settings you want for your site.','','11.2.5'),(7987,_binary 'Select the desired option for what happens to content that a user created if their account is canceled.','','11.2.5'),(7988,_binary 'Optionally, edit the text of email messages related to user accounts.','','11.2.5'),(7989,_binary 'Verify that the other settings are correct.','','11.2.5'),(7990,_binary 'Topics can be provided by modules or themes. Top-level help topics on your site:','','none'),(7991,_binary 'Both the table-style and grid-style interfaces are regular views and can be customized via the <a href=\":views-ui\">Views UI</a>, including sorting and filtering. This is the case for both the administration page and the modal dialog.','','none'),(7992,_binary 'In the grid-style interface, the fields that are displayed (including which image style is used for images) can be customized by configuring the \"Media library\" view mode for each of your <a href=\":media-types\">media types</a>. The thumbnail images in the grid-style interface can be customized by configuring the \"Media Library thumbnail (220×220)\" image style.','','none'),(7993,_binary 'When adding new media items within the modal dialog, the fields that are displayed can be customized by configuring the \"Media library\" form mode for each of your <a href=\":media-types\">media types</a>.','','none'),(7994,_binary 'Provides the API allowing to rename URLs.','','none'),(7995,_binary 'The parent workspace.','','none'),(7996,_binary 'Merge workspace','','none'),(7997,_binary 'Only top-level workspaces can be published.','','none'),(7998,_binary 'Merge into @target_label','','none'),(7999,_binary 'The %label workspace can not be deleted because it has child workspaces.','','none'),(8000,_binary 'There are no changes that can be merged from %source_label to %target_label.','','none'),(8001,_binary 'Would you like to merge the contents of the %source_label workspace into %target_label?','','none'),(8002,_binary 'Merge workspace contents.','','none'),(8003,_binary 'The contents of the %source_label workspace have been merged into %target_label.','','none'),(8004,_binary 'There is @count item that can be merged from %source_label to %target_labelThere are @count items that can be merged from %source_label to %target_label','','none'),(8005,_binary 'Workspace selection','','none'),(8006,_binary 'Medium 8:7','','none'),(8007,_binary 'Responsive 3x2','','none'),(8008,_binary 'The field that is going to be used as the RSS item link for each row. This must either be an internal unprocessed path like \"node/123\" or a processed, root-relative URL as produced by fields like \"Link to content\".','','none'),(8009,_binary 'Recursive rendering detected when rendering entity %entity_type: %entity_id, using the %field_name field on the %parent_entity_type:%parent_bundle %parent_entity_id entity. Aborting rendering.','','none'),(8010,_binary 'Response status','','11.2.5'),(8011,_binary 'Directory \"@temp\" has insufficient space. There must be at least @space megabytes free.','','none'),(8012,_binary 'Width: %width pixels','','none'),(8013,_binary 'Height: %height pixels','','none'),(8014,_binary 'Heading type','','none'),(8015,_binary '@interval hence','','11.2.5'),(8016,_binary 'The @drupal installer requires that the %default-file file must not be deleted or modified from the original download.','','none'),(8017,_binary 'Drupal 9 no longer uses the $settings[\'install_profile\'] value in settings.php and it should be removed.','','none'),(8018,_binary '@low_version_number to @high_version_number','','none'),(8019,_binary 'Drupal core security coverage','','11.2.5'),(8020,_binary 'Visit the <a href=\":url\">release cycle overview</a> for more information on supported releases.','','none'),(8021,_binary 'Manage workspace','','none'),(8022,_binary 'Other workspaces:','','none'),(8023,_binary 'View all workspaces','','none'),(8024,_binary 'Not compatible','','none'),(8025,_binary 'Requires Drupal core:','','11.2.5'),(8026,_binary 'Covered until @end_version','','none'),(8027,_binary 'Coverage has ended','','none'),(8028,_binary '<a href=\":update_status_report\">Update to @next_minor or higher</a> soon to continue receiving security updates.','','none'),(8029,_binary 'Covered until @date','','none'),(8030,_binary '<a href=\":update_status_report\">Update to a supported minor</a> as soon as possible to continue receiving security updates.','','none'),(8031,_binary 'Manages breakpoints and breakpoint groups for responsive designs.','','none'),(8032,_binary 'Allows users to comment on content.','','none'),(8033,_binary 'Allows users to translate configuration text.','','none'),(8034,_binary 'Provides site-wide contact forms and forms to contact individual users.','','none'),(8035,_binary 'Allows users to translate content.','','none'),(8036,_binary 'Provides contextual links to directly access tasks related to page elements.','','none'),(8037,_binary 'Logs system events in the database.','','none'),(8038,_binary 'Caches pages, including those with dynamic content, for all users.','','none'),(8039,_binary 'Provides a user interface for the Field module.','','none'),(8040,_binary 'Defines a field type for image media and provides display configuration tools.','','none'),(8041,_binary 'Allows users to configure available languages.','','none'),(8042,_binary 'Allows users to create menu links.','','none'),(8043,_binary 'Users with sufficient access rights will be able to override these options.','','none'),(8044,_binary 'Caches pages for anonymous users and can be used when external page cache is not available.','','none'),(8045,_binary 'Allows users to create search pages based on plugins provided by other modules.','','none'),(8046,_binary 'PHP APCu caching','','11.2.5'),(8047,_binary 'Enabled (@size)','','none'),(8048,_binary 'Depending on your configuration, Drupal can run with a @apcu_size APCu limit. However, a @apcu_default_size APCu limit (the default) or above is recommended, especially if your site uses additional custom or contributed modules.','','none'),(8049,_binary 'Memory available: @available.','','none'),(8050,_binary 'PHP APCu caching can improve your site\'s performance considerably. It is <strong>highly recommended</strong> to have <a href=\"https://www.php.net/manual/apcu.installation.php\" target=\"_blank\">APCu</a> installed on your server.','','none'),(8051,_binary 'The version of Drupal you are trying to update from is too old','','none'),(8052,_binary 'Unsupported schema version: @module','','none'),(8053,_binary 'The installed version of the %module module is too old to update. Update to an intermediate version first (last removed version: @last_removed_version, installed version: @installed_version).','','none'),(8054,_binary 'Provides a user interface for creating and managing views.','','none'),(8055,_binary '<p class=\"text-align-center\">Explore recipes across every type of occasion, ingredient, and skill level.</p>','','none'),(8056,_binary '<p class=\"text-align-center\">Explore recipes across every type of occasion, ingredient, and skill level</p>','','none'),(8057,_binary '@count place@count places','','11.2.5'),(8058,_binary 'Leave blank for all. Otherwise, the first selected item will be the default instead of \"Any\".','','none'),(8059,_binary 'Select %entity_types','','none'),(8060,_binary 'Select @entity_types','','none'),(8061,_binary 'MariaDB','','none'),(8062,_binary 'MySQL, Percona Server, or equivalent','','none'),(8063,_binary 'Required by the theme: @theme_namesRequired by the themes: @theme_names','','none'),(8064,_binary '@theme','','none'),(8065,_binary '@theme (theme) (<span class=\"admin-disabled\">disabled</span>)','','none'),(8066,_binary 'This theme requires the listed modules to operate correctly.','','none'),(8067,_binary 'Review the <a href=\":url\"> suggestions for resolving this incompatibility</a> to repair your installation, and then re-run update.php.','','none'),(8068,_binary 'Missing updates for: @module','','none'),(8069,_binary 'The following module is installed, but it is incompatible with Drupal @version:The following modules are installed, but they are incompatible with Drupal @version:','','none'),(8070,_binary 'Incompatible moduleIncompatible modules','','none'),(8071,_binary 'The following theme is installed, but it is incompatible with Drupal @version:The following themes are installed, but they are incompatible with Drupal @version:','','none'),(8072,_binary 'Incompatible themeIncompatible themes','','none'),(8073,_binary 'The following module is installed, but it is incompatible with PHP @version:The following modules are installed, but they are incompatible with PHP @version:','','none'),(8074,_binary 'The following theme is installed, but it is incompatible with PHP @version:The following themes are installed, but they are incompatible with PHP @version:','','none'),(8075,_binary 'The following module is marked as installed in the core.extension configuration, but it is missing:The following modules are marked as installed in the core.extension configuration, but they are missing:','','none'),(8076,_binary 'Missing or invalid moduleMissing or invalid modules','','none'),(8077,_binary 'The following theme is marked as installed in the core.extension configuration, but it is missing:The following themes are marked as installed in the core.extension configuration, but they are missing:','','none'),(8078,_binary 'Missing or invalid themeMissing or invalid themes','','none'),(8079,_binary 'The installed version of the %module module is too old to update. Update to a version prior to @versions first (missing updates: @missing_updates).The installed version of the %module module is too old to update. Update first to a version prior to all of the following: @versions (missing updates: @missing_updates).','','none'),(8080,_binary '@module_name (<span class=\"admin-missing\">missing</span>)','','none'),(8081,_binary '@module_name (<span class=\"admin-missing\">incompatible with</span> this version of Drupal core)','','none'),(8082,_binary '@module_name (<span class=\"admin-missing\">incompatible with</span> version @version)','','none'),(8083,_binary '@module_name (<span class=\"admin-disabled\">disabled</span>)','','none'),(8084,_binary 'Unable to install @theme due to missing module dependencies.','','none'),(8085,_binary 'Empty version','','none'),(8086,_binary 'Invalid version: @existing_version','','none'),(8087,_binary 'Stable 9','','none'),(8088,_binary 'A base theme using Drupal 9.0.0\'s core markup and CSS.','','none'),(8089,_binary 'Ban visitors from one or more IP addresses from accessing and viewing your site.','','none'),(8090,_binary 'Enter an <em>IP address</em> and click <em>Add</em>.','','none'),(8091,_binary 'You should see the IP address you entered listed under <em>Banned IP addresses</em>. Repeat the above steps to ban additional IP addresses.','','none'),(8092,_binary 'What types of data does a site have?','','11.2.5'),(8093,_binary 'What is a content entity?','','11.2.5'),(8094,_binary 'What is a field?','','11.2.5'),(8095,_binary 'Within entity items, the data is stored in individual <em>fields</em>, each of which holds one type of data, such as formatted or plain text, images or other files, or dates. Fields can be added by an administrator on entity sub-types, so that all entity items of a given entity sub-type have the same collection of fields available, and they can be single-valued or multiple-valued. When you create or edit entity items, you are specifying the values for the fields on the entity item.','','11.2.5'),(8096,_binary 'What is a reference field?','','11.2.5'),(8097,_binary 'A <em>reference field</em> is a field that stores a relationship between an entity and one or more other entities, which may belong to the same or different entity type. For example, a <em>Content reference</em> field on a content type stores a relationship between one content item and one or more other content items.','','11.2.5'),(8098,_binary 'What field types are available?','','11.2.5'),(8099,_binary 'The following field types are provided by the core system and core modules (many more are provided by contributed modules):','','11.2.5'),(8100,_binary 'Boolean, Number (provided by the core system): Stores true/false values and numbers','','11.2.5'),(8101,_binary 'Comment (provided by the core Comment module): Allows users to add comments to an entity','','11.2.5'),(8102,_binary 'Date, Timestamp (Datetime module): Stores dates and times','','11.2.5'),(8103,_binary 'Email (core system): Stores email addresses','','11.2.5'),(8104,_binary 'Link (Link module): Stores URLs and link text','','11.2.5'),(8105,_binary 'Telephone (Telephone module): Stores telephone numbers','','11.2.5'),(8106,_binary 'What is a formatter?','','11.2.5'),(8107,_binary 'A <em>formatter</em> is a way to display a field; most field types offer several types of formatters, and most formatters have settings that further define how the field is displayed. It is also possible to completely hide a field from display, and you have the option of showing or hiding the field\'s label when it is displayed.','','11.2.5'),(8108,_binary 'What is a widget?','','11.2.5'),(8109,_binary 'A <em>widget</em> is a way to edit a field. Some field types, such as plain text single-line fields, have only one widget available (in this case, a single-line text input field). Other field types offer choices for the widget; for example, single-valued <em>List</em> fields can use a <em>Select</em> or <em>Radio button</em> widget for editing. Many widget types have settings that further define how the field can be edited.','','11.2.5'),(8110,_binary 'Managing content structure overview','','11.2.5'),(8111,_binary 'Besides the field modules listed in the previous section, there are additional core modules that you can use to manage your content structure:','','11.2.5'),(8112,_binary 'Configure your system so that cron will run automatically.','','11.2.5'),(8113,_binary 'What are cron tasks?','','11.2.5'),(8114,_binary 'To ensure that your site and its modules continue to function well, a group of administrative operations should be run periodically. These operations are called <em>cron</em> tasks, and running the tasks is known as <em>running cron</em>. Depending on how often content is updated on your site, you might need to run cron on a schedule ranging from hourly to weekly to keep your site running well.','','11.2.5'),(8115,_binary 'What options are available for running cron?','','11.2.5'),(8116,_binary 'If the core Automated Cron module is installed, your site will run cron periodically, on a schedule you can configure.','','11.2.5'),(8117,_binary 'You can set up a task on your web server to visit the <em> cron URL</em>, which is unique to your site, on a schedule.','','11.2.5'),(8118,_binary 'You can also run cron manually, but this is not the recommended way to make sure it is run periodically.','','11.2.5'),(8119,_binary 'If you want to run cron right now, click <em>Run cron</em> and wait for cron to finish.','','11.2.5'),(8120,_binary 'If you have a way to configure tasks on your web server, copy the link where it says <em>To run cron from outside the site, go to</em>. Set up a task to visit that URL on your desired cron schedule, such as once an hour or once a week. (On Linux-like servers, you can use the <em>wget</em> command to visit a URL.) If you configure an outside task, you should uninstall the Automated Cron module.','','11.2.5'),(8121,_binary 'If you are not configuring an outside task, and you have the core Automated Cron module installed, select a schedule for automated cron runs in <em>Cron settings</em> &gt; <em>Run cron every</em>. Click <em>Save configuration</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8122,_binary 'What is a module?','','11.2.5'),(8123,_binary 'A <em>module</em> is a set of PHP, JavaScript, and/or CSS files that extends site features and adds functionality. A set of <em>Core modules</em> is distributed as part of the core software download. Additional <em>Contributed modules</em> can be downloaded separately from the <a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/project/project_module\">Download &amp; Extend page on drupal.org</a>.','','11.2.5'),(8124,_binary 'What is an Experimental module?','','11.2.5'),(8125,_binary 'An <em>Experimental</em> module is a module that is still in development and is not yet stable. Using Experimental modules on production sites is not recommended.','','11.2.5'),(8126,_binary 'What are installing and uninstalling?','','11.2.5'),(8127,_binary 'Installing a core or downloaded contributed module means turning it on, so that you can use its features and functionality. Uninstalling means turning it off and removing all of its configuration. A module cannot be uninstalled if another installed module depends on it, or if you have created content on your site using the module -- you would need to delete the content and uninstall dependent modules first.','','11.2.5'),(8128,_binary 'Extending overview','','11.2.5'),(8129,_binary 'See the related topics listed below for help performing tasks related to extending the functionality of your site.','','11.2.5'),(8130,_binary 'Maintaining and troubleshooting overview','','11.2.5'),(8131,_binary 'Here are some tasks and hints related to maintaining your site, and troubleshooting problems that may come up on your site. See the related topics below for more information.','','11.2.5'),(8132,_binary 'Configure your site so that cron runs periodically.','','11.2.5'),(8133,_binary 'If your site is not behaving as expected, clear the cache before trying to diagnose the problem.','','11.2.5'),(8134,_binary 'There are several site reports that can help you diagnose problems with your site. There are also two core modules that can be used for error logging: Database Logging and Syslog.','','11.2.5'),(8135,_binary 'Find the particular sub-type that you want to add the field to, and click <em>Manage fields</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8136,_binary 'Click <em>Add field</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8137,_binary 'The <em>Label</em> field should now be visible; enter a label for the field, which is used as the field label for both content editing and content display.','','11.2.5'),(8138,_binary 'Click <em>Save and continue</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8139,_binary 'On the next screen, enter a value for <em>Allowed number of values</em>. You can limit the field to one value per entity item, a set number of values, or set it to have unlimited values. Click <em>Save field settings</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8140,_binary 'On the next screen, optionally edit the settings for the field, which vary depending on what field type you are creating. For all fields, you can edit the <em>Label</em>, <em>Help text</em> (text to be displayed below the field on the content editing page), and <em>Required field</em> (to make it so a value must be entered in order to save the content when editing). You can also configure a default value for the field.','','11.2.5'),(8141,_binary 'Find the particular sub-type that you want to configure the display of, and click <em>Manage display</em> in the <em>Operations</em> list.','','11.2.5'),(8142,_binary 'Use the drag arrows to order the fields in your preferred order.','','11.2.5'),(8143,_binary 'Drag any fields that you do not wish to see in the display to the <em>Disabled</em> section.','','11.2.5'),(8144,_binary 'In the <em>Label</em> column, select the position for each field label in the display, or <em>- Hidden -</em> to hide a label. You can also choose <em>- Visually Hidden-</em> if you want the label\'s text to appear in the HTML page, so that screen readers and search engines can read it, but it will not be visible.','','11.2.5'),(8145,_binary 'In the <em>Format</em> column, select the formatter for displaying each field.','','11.2.5'),(8146,_binary 'After selecting the desired formatters, click the settings gear in each row to change the settings for the formatter.','','11.2.5'),(8147,_binary 'When you are done making changes, click <em>Save</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8148,_binary 'Test the display for your entity sub-type by viewing an entity. If needed, return to these steps to further refine the display.','','11.2.5'),(8149,_binary 'Find the particular sub-type that you want to configure the editing form for, and click <em>Manage form display</em> in the <em>Operations</em> list.','','11.2.5'),(8150,_binary 'Drag any fields that you do not wish to see on the editing form to the <em>Disabled</em> section.','','11.2.5'),(8151,_binary 'In the <em>Widget</em> column, select the widget for editing each field.','','11.2.5'),(8152,_binary 'After selecting the desired widgets, click the settings gear in each row to change the settings for the widget.','','11.2.5'),(8153,_binary 'Test the editing form for your entity sub-type by editing or creating an entity. If needed, return to these steps to further refine the form.','','11.2.5'),(8154,_binary 'In <em>Add a new field</em>, select the type of reference field you want to add. The <em>Reference</em> section of the select list shows the most common types of reference field; choose <em>Other...</em> if the entity type you want to reference is not listed.','','11.2.5'),(8155,_binary 'On the next screen, verify that the type of entity you want to reference is shown in <em>Type of item to reference</em>, or select it if not. Enter a value for <em>Allowed number of values</em>. You can limit the field to one value per entity item, a set number of values, or set it to have unlimited values. Click <em>Save field settings</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8156,_binary 'On the next screen, optionally edit the settings for <em>Label</em>, <em>Help text</em> (text to be displayed below the field on the content editing page), and <em>Required field</em> (to make it so a value must be entered in order to save the content when editing).','','11.2.5'),(8157,_binary 'In the <em>Reference type</em> section, you will usually want to limit the entity sub-types that can be referenced; for example, if you are creating a <em>Content</em> reference, you can check one or two <em>Content type</em> choices. The choices will be easier for content editors to scan if you also choose a sort value (normally the entity title or label field).','','11.2.5'),(8158,_binary 'Clear the data in the site cache.','','11.2.5'),(8159,_binary 'What is the cache?','','11.2.5'),(8160,_binary 'Some of the calculations that are done when your site loads a page take a long time to run. To save time when these calculations would need to be done again, their results can be <em>cached</em> in your site\'s database. There are internal mechanisms to <em>clear</em> cached data when the conditions or assumptions that went into the calculation have changed, but you can also clear cached data manually. When your site is misbehaving, a good first step is to clear the cache and see if the problem goes away.','','11.2.5'),(8161,_binary 'Click <em>Clear all caches</em>. Your site\'s cached data will be cleared.','','11.2.5'),(8162,_binary 'Put your site in maintenance mode to perform maintenance operations, and then return to normal mode when finished.','','11.2.5'),(8163,_binary 'What is maintenance mode?','','11.2.5'),(8164,_binary 'When your site is in maintenance mode, most site visitors will see a simple maintenance mode message page, rather than being able to use the full functionality of the site. Users with <em>Use the site in maintenance mode</em> permission who are already logged in will be able to use the full site, and the log in page at <em>/user</em> will also be accessible to anyone.','','11.2.5'),(8165,_binary 'Check <em>Put site into maintenance mode</em>, optionally change the <em>Message to display when in maintenance mode</em>, and click <em>Save configuration</em>. Your site will be in maintenance mode.','','11.2.5'),(8166,_binary 'Perform your maintenance operations.','','11.2.5'),(8167,_binary 'Uncheck <em>Put site into maintenance mode</em> and click <em>Save configuration</em>. Your site will be back in normal operation mode.','','11.2.5'),(8168,_binary 'Install a core module, or a contributed module that has already been downloaded.','','11.2.5'),(8169,_binary 'Enter a word from the module name or description into the filter box, to make the list of modules smaller. Locate the module you want to install.','','11.2.5'),(8170,_binary 'Check the box next to the name of the module you want to install; you can also check more than one box to install multiple modules at the same time. If the checkbox is disabled for the module you are trying to install, expand the information to see why -- you may need to download an additional module that your module requires.','','11.2.5'),(8171,_binary 'Click <em>Install</em> at the bottom of the page. If you chose to install a module with dependencies that were not already installed, or if you chose an Experimental module, confirm your choice on the next page.','','11.2.5'),(8172,_binary 'Wait for the module (or modules) to be installed. You should be returned to the <em>Extend</em> page with a message saying the module or modules were installed.','','11.2.5'),(8173,_binary 'Enter a word from the module name or description into the filter box, to make the list of modules smaller. Locate the module you want to uninstall.','','11.2.5'),(8174,_binary 'In the <em>Description</em> column, see if there are reasons that this module cannot be uninstalled. For example, you may have created content using this module (which you would need to delete first), or there may be another module installed that requires this module to be installed (you would need to uninstall the other module first).','','11.2.5'),(8175,_binary 'If there are no reasons listed, the module can be uninstalled. Check the box in the <em>Uninstall</em> column, next to the module\'s name.','','11.2.5'),(8176,_binary 'Click <em>Uninstall</em> at the bottom of the page. Verify the list of modules to be uninstalled and configuration to be deleted on the confirmation page, and click <em>Uninstall</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8177,_binary 'Wait for the module to be uninstalled. You should be returned to the <em>Uninstall</em> page with a message saying the module was uninstalled.','','11.2.5'),(8178,_binary 'Run reports to learn about the status and health of your site.','','11.2.5'),(8179,_binary 'If you have the core Database Logging module installed, in the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Reports</em> &gt; <em>Recent log messages</em> to see a report of the error and informational messages your site has generated. You can filter the report by <em>Severity</em> to see only the most critical messages, if desired.','','11.2.5'),(8180,_binary 'Click <em>Add user</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8181,_binary 'Enter the <em>Email address</em>, <em>Username</em>, and <em>Password</em> (twice) for the new user.','','11.2.5'),(8182,_binary 'Verify that the <em>Roles</em> checked for the new user are correct.','','11.2.5'),(8183,_binary 'If you want the new user to receive an email message notifying them of the new account, check <em>Notify user of new account</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8184,_binary 'Optionally, change other settings on the form.','','11.2.5'),(8185,_binary 'Click <em>Create new account</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8186,_binary 'You will be left on the <em>Add user</em> page; repeat these steps if you have more user accounts to create.','','11.2.5'),(8187,_binary 'Create a new role.','','11.2.5'),(8188,_binary 'Click <em>Add role</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8189,_binary 'Enter the desired <em>Role name</em>. If desired, click <em>Edit</em> to change the <em>Machine name</em> for the role.','','11.2.5'),(8190,_binary 'Click <em>Save</em>. You should be returned to the <em>Roles</em> page and your new role should be in the role list.','','11.2.5'),(8191,_binary 'What is a user?','','11.2.5'),(8192,_binary 'A user is anyone accessing or viewing your site. <em>Anonymous</em> users are users who are not logged in, and <em>Authenticated</em> users are users who are logged in.','','11.2.5'),(8193,_binary 'What is a role?','','11.2.5'),(8194,_binary '<em>Roles</em> are used to group and classify users; each user can be assigned one or more roles. There are also special roles for all anonymous and all authenticated users.','','11.2.5'),(8195,_binary 'What is a permission?','','11.2.5'),(8196,_binary 'Granting a <em>permission</em> to a role allows users who have been assigned that role to perform an action on the site, such as viewing content, editing or creating  a particular type of content, administering settings for a particular module, or using a particular function of the site (such as search).','','11.2.5'),(8197,_binary 'Overview of managing user accounts and visitors','','11.2.5'),(8198,_binary 'Modify the permissions for an existing role.','','11.2.5'),(8199,_binary 'Review the permissions for the role, paying particular attention to the permissions marked with <em>Warning: Give to trusted roles only; this permission has security implications.</em> Uncheck permissions that this role should not have, in the row of the permission and the column of the role; check permissions that this role should have.','','11.2.5'),(8200,_binary 'Click <em>Save permissions</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8201,_binary 'Update or delete an existing user account.','','11.2.5'),(8202,_binary 'Enter all or part of the user name or email address of the user account you want to update or delete, and click <em>Filter</em>. A short list of user accounts, including the account of interest, should be shown in the table; if not, modify the filter text until you can find the account of interest.','','11.2.5'),(8203,_binary 'Click <em>Edit</em> in the <em>Operations</em> area of the account of interest.','','11.2.5'),(8204,_binary 'To delete the user account, scroll to the bottom and click <em>Cancel account</em>. Select what you want to happen to the user\'s content on the next screen, and click <em>Cancel account</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8205,_binary 'To update the user account, enter new values in the form and click <em>Save</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8206,_binary 'Selection handler','','none'),(8207,_binary 'Selection handler settings','','none'),(8208,_binary 'Programming languages','','none'),(8209,_binary 'Media has been removed.','','none'),(8210,_binary 'Olivero Utilities','','none'),(8211,_binary 'Enable mobile menu at all widths','','none'),(8212,_binary 'Header site branding background color','','none'),(8213,_binary 'Search by keyword or phrase.','','11.2.5'),(8214,_binary 'Nav Medium','','none'),(8215,_binary 'Grid Medium','','none'),(8216,_binary 'Grid Max','','none'),(8217,_binary 'olivero settings','','none'),(8218,_binary 'Schema information for module %module was missing from the database. You should manually review the module updates and your database to check if any updates have been skipped up to, and including, %last_update_hook.','','none'),(8219,_binary 'Add, remove, or rearrange the fields on personal and site-wide contact forms.','','11.2.5'),(8220,_binary 'What are the fields on contact forms?','','11.2.5'),(8221,_binary 'Click <em>Manage fields</em> for the form you want to change the fields of, and add or remove one or more fields on the form.','','11.2.5'),(8222,_binary 'Click <em>Manage form display</em> to change the order or configuration of the fields on the form.','','11.2.5'),(8223,_binary 'Configure personal contact forms for registered users on the website.','','11.2.5'),(8224,_binary 'In the <em>Contact settings</em> section, check/uncheck the box to enable/disable the contact form for new user accounts.','','11.2.5'),(8225,_binary 'Click <em>Save configuration</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8226,_binary 'Verify that permissions are correct for your site\'s roles, including the generic <em>Anonymous user</em> and <em>Authenticated user</em>. In order to use personal contact forms, users need both <em>View user information</em> (in the <em>User</em> section, which enables them to view user profiles) and <em>Use users\' personal contact forms</em> (in the <em>Contact</em> section, which enables them to use contact forms if they can view user profiles).','','11.2.5'),(8227,_binary 'Create a new site-wide contact form.','','11.2.5'),(8228,_binary 'Click <em>Add contact form</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8229,_binary 'Fill in the <em>Label</em> (title) for the form, <em>Recipients</em>, and optionally the other settings.','','11.2.5'),(8230,_binary 'Click <em>Save</em>. You should see your new contact form in the table, along with a link to view it.','','11.2.5'),(8231,_binary 'What are contact forms?','','11.2.5'),(8232,_binary 'There are two different types of contact forms provided by the core Contact module: personal contact forms, which allow users to contact other users on the site, and site-wide contact forms, which allow users to contact site managers or administrators. A site can have more than one site-wide contact form; each has its own fields to fill out, recipients, and URL; you can also change the fields that are shown on personal contact forms.','','11.2.5'),(8233,_binary 'Site visitors can email registered users on your site by using the personal contact form, without knowing or learning the email address of the recipient. When a user with the correct permissions is viewing another user\'s profile, the viewer will see a <em>Contact</em> tab or link, which leads to the personal contact form if the user whose profile is being viewed has their personal contact form enabled (this is a user account setting).','','11.2.5'),(8234,_binary 'Contact form management tasks','','11.2.5'),(8235,_binary 'See the related topics below for specific tasks.','','11.2.5'),(8236,_binary 'Click <em>Edit</em> for the site-wide form you want to be the default.','','11.2.5'),(8237,_binary 'Check <em>Make this the default form</em> and click <em>Save</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8238,_binary 'Tracking overview','','11.2.5'),(8239,_binary 'The core History module tracks how recently users have viewed content items, and provides a Views field and filter that can be used to show users content that they haven\'t yet seen.','','11.2.5'),(8240,_binary 'If you have one or more tracking modules installed on your site, see the related topics listed below for specific tasks.','','11.2.5'),(8241,_binary 'Click <em>Save settings</em>. You should be returned to the <em>Manage fields</em> page, with your new field in the list.','','11.2.5'),(8242,_binary 'What content visits are tracked?','','11.2.5'),(8243,_binary 'The core History module tracks when each logged-in user has most recently visited each content item page on the site. This allows content to be marked as <em>new</em> or <em>updated</em> for each user, meaning that it was newly created or has been updated since the last time they visited its page. These records are kept for one month, meaning that content older than one month is never marked as new or updated.','','11.2.5'),(8244,_binary 'What options are available for using this tracking information?','','11.2.5'),(8245,_binary 'You can display the new/updated status of content by creating or editing a view. There is a <em>Has new content</em> field for <em>Content</em> views, which displays the new/updated marker. There is also a <em>Has new content</em> filter, which limits the view to new and updated content.','','11.2.5'),(8246,_binary 'Whether to force the output to be an absolute link (beginning with http: or https:)','','none'),(8247,_binary 'Whether to force this URL to point to a secure location (beginning with https:)','','none'),(8248,_binary 'Checked %langcode translation for %project.','','11.2.5'),(8249,_binary 'Downloaded %langcode translation for %project.','','none'),(8250,_binary 'Imported %langcode translation for %project.','','11.2.5'),(8251,_binary 'It looks like you have content on your new site which <strong>may be overwritten</strong> if you continue to run this upgrade. The upgrade should be performed on a clean Drupal @version installation. For more information see the <a target=\"_blank\" href=\":id-conflicts-handbook\">upgrade handbook</a>.','','none'),(8252,_binary 'An upgrade has already been performed on this site. To perform a new migration, create a clean and empty new install of Drupal @version. Rollbacks are not yet supported through the user interface. For more information, see the <a href=\":url\">upgrading handbook</a>.','','none'),(8253,_binary 'Upgrade a site by importing its files and the data from its database into a clean and empty new install of Drupal @version. See the <a href=\":url\">Drupal site upgrades handbook</a> for more information.','','none'),(8254,_binary 'This empty Drupal @version installation you will import the old site to.','','none'),(8255,_binary 'The menu name (= set name) for this shortcut link.','','none'),(8256,_binary 'There are errors with some installed themes. Visit the <a href=\":link\">status report page</a> for more information.','','none'),(8257,_binary 'There are errors with some installed modules. Visit the <a href=\":link\">status report page</a> for more information.','','none'),(8258,_binary 'Display machine name must contain only lowercase letters, numbers, or underscores.','','none'),(8259,_binary 'Module %name has an entry in the system.schema key/value storage, but is missing from your site. <a href=\":url\">More information about this error</a>.','','none'),(8260,_binary 'Module %name has an entry in the system.schema key/value storage, but is not installed. <a href=\":url\">More information about this error</a>.','','none'),(8261,_binary 'Missing required data for configuration: %config','','none'),(8262,_binary 'Search form (narrow)','','11.2.5'),(8263,_binary 'Search form (wide)','','11.2.5'),(8264,_binary 'What are breakpoints?','','11.2.5'),(8265,_binary 'Breakpoints are the point at which your site\'s content will respond to provide the user with the best possible layout to consume the information. A breakpoint separates the height or width of viewports (screens, printers, and other media output types) into steps. For instance, a width breakpoint of 40em creates two steps: one for widths up to 40em and one for widths above 40em. Breakpoints can be used to define when layouts should shift from one form to another, when images should be resized, and other changes that need to respond to changes in viewport height or width.','','11.2.5'),(8266,_binary 'What are media queries?','','11.2.5'),(8267,_binary 'Media  queries are a formal way to encode breakpoints. For instance, a width breakpoint at 40em would be written as the media query \"(min-width: 40em)\". Breakpoints are really just media queries with some additional meta-data, such as a name and multiplier information.','','11.2.5'),(8268,_binary 'What are resolution multipliers?','','11.2.5'),(8269,_binary 'What is a breakpoint group?','','11.2.5'),(8270,_binary 'Managing breakpoints and breakpoint groups overview','','11.2.5'),(8271,_binary 'The <em>Breakpoint</em> module allows you to define breakpoints and breakpoint groups in YAML files. Modules and themes can use the API provided by the <em>Breakpoint</em> module to define breakpoints and breakpoint groups, and to assign resolution multipliers to breakpoints.','','11.2.5'),(8272,_binary 'W3C standards for media queries','','11.2.5'),(8273,_binary 'What is a theme?','','11.2.5'),(8274,_binary 'A <em>theme</em> is a set of files that define the visual look and feel of your site. The core software and modules that run on your site determine which content (including HTML text and other data stored in the database, uploaded images, and any other asset files) is displayed on the pages of your site. The theme determines the HTML markup and CSS styling that wraps the content. Several basic themes are supplied with the core software; additional <em>contributed themes</em> can be downloaded separately from the <a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/project/project_theme\">Download &amp; Extend page on drupal.org</a>, or you can create your own theme.','','11.2.5'),(8275,_binary 'What is a base theme?','','11.2.5'),(8276,_binary 'What is a layout?','','11.2.5'),(8277,_binary 'Changing site appearance overview','','11.2.5'),(8278,_binary 'The core Field UI module provides a user interface for managing fields and their display on entities.','','11.2.5'),(8279,_binary 'The core Layout Builder module provides a more flexible user interface for configuring the display of entities.','','11.2.5'),(8280,_binary 'What is site performance?','','11.2.5'),(8281,_binary 'Site performance, in this context, refers to speed factors such as the page load time and the response time after a user action on a page.','','11.2.5'),(8282,_binary 'What is caching?','','11.2.5'),(8283,_binary 'Caching is saving already-rendered HTML output and other calculated data for later use the first time it is needed. This saves time, because the next time the same data is needed it can be quickly retrieved instead of recalculated. Automatic caching systems also include mechanisms to delete cached calculations or mark them as no longer valid when the underlying data changes. To facilitate that, cached data has a <em>lifetime</em>, which is the maximum time before the data will be deleted from the cache (forcing recalculation).','','11.2.5'),(8284,_binary 'What is file aggregation?','','11.2.5'),(8285,_binary 'Aggregation is when CSS and JavaScript files are merged together and compressed into a format that is much smaller than the original. This allows for faster transmission and faster rendering on the other end.','','11.2.5'),(8286,_binary 'What can I do to improve my site\'s performance?','','11.2.5'),(8287,_binary 'Internal Page Cache module','','11.2.5'),(8288,_binary 'Caches pages requested by users who are not logged in (anonymous users). Do not use if your site needs to send different output to different anonymous users.','','11.2.5'),(8289,_binary 'Internal Dynamic Page Cache module','','11.2.5'),(8290,_binary 'Caches data for both authenticated and anonymous users, with non-cacheable data in the page converted to placeholders and calculated when the page is requested.','','11.2.5'),(8291,_binary 'Big Pipe module','','11.2.5'),(8292,_binary 'Changes the way pages are sent to users, so that cacheable parts are sent out first with placeholders, and the uncacheable or personalized parts of the page are streamed afterwards. This allows the browser to render the bulk of the page quickly and fill in the details later.','','11.2.5'),(8293,_binary 'Performance page settings','','11.2.5'),(8294,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, if you navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Development</em> &gt; <em>Performance</em>, you will find a setting for the maximum cache lifetime, as well as the ability to turn on CSS and JavaScript file aggregation.','','11.2.5'),(8295,_binary 'Online documentation for the Internal Page Cache module','','11.2.5'),(8296,_binary 'Online documentation for the Internal Dynamic Page Cache module','','11.2.5'),(8297,_binary 'Online documentation for the BigPipe module','','11.2.5'),(8298,_binary 'What are the parts of a layout?','','none'),(8299,_binary 'Find the particular sub-type that you want to create a layout for, and click <em>Manage display</em> in the <em>Operations</em> list.','','none'),(8300,_binary 'Under <em>Layout options</em>, check <em>Use Layout Builder</em>. You can also check the box below to allow each entity item to have its layout individually customized (if it is left unchecked, the site will use the same layout for all items of this entity sub-type).','','none'),(8301,_binary 'Click <em>Save</em>. You will be returned to the <em>Manage display</em> page, but you will no longer see the table of fields of the classic display manager.','','none'),(8302,_binary 'Click <em>Manage layout</em> to enter layout management view. A default layout will be set up for you, with a single one-column section containing the fields on your entity sub-type.','','none'),(8303,_binary 'To remove the default section and start from an empty layout, find and click the <em>Remove</em> button for the default section, which looks like an X. Confirm by clicking <em>Remove</em> in the pop-up dialog.','','none'),(8304,_binary 'Add new sections, each with one to four columns, to your layout. For instance, you might want a one-column section at the top, a two-column section in the middle, and then a one-column section at the bottom. To add a section, click <em>Add section</em> and click the desired number of columns. For multi-column sections, set the column width percentages and click <em>Add section</em> in the pop-up dialog.','','none'),(8305,_binary 'In each section, click <em>Add block</em> to add a block. You will see a list of the blocks available on your site, plus a section called <em>Content fields</em> with a block for each field on your content item. Each block can be configured, if desired, with a <em>Title</em>, and for content field blocks, you can also configure the field formatter. Continue to add blocks to your sections until all the desired blocks and fields are displayed.','','none'),(8306,_binary 'Verify your layout. You can check <em>Show content preview</em> to show a preview of what your layout will look like, or uncheck it to see the names of the fields and blocks in each section.','','none'),(8307,_binary 'If needed, reorder the blocks by dragging them to new locations. If you hover over a block, a contextual menu will appear that will let you change the configuration of the block, remove the block, or <em>Move</em> blocks within the section using a more compact interface.','','none'),(8308,_binary 'When you are satisfied with your layout, click <em>Save layout</em>.','','none'),(8309,_binary 'Creating layout defaults','','none'),(8310,_binary 'Building Layouts Using the Layout Builder UI','','none'),(8311,_binary 'Install a core theme, or a contributed theme that has already been downloaded. Choose the default themes to use for the site and for administrative pages.','','11.2.5'),(8312,_binary 'Locate the themes that you want to use as the site default theme and for administrative pages.','','11.2.5'),(8313,_binary 'For each of these themes, if the theme is in the <em>Uninstalled themes</em> section, click the <em>Install</em> link to install the theme. Wait for the theme to be installed (translations might be downloaded). You should be returned to the <em>Appearance</em> page.','','11.2.5'),(8314,_binary 'Locate the theme that you want to be your default theme, which should now be in the <em>Installed themes</em> section. If it is not already labeled as the <em>default theme</em>, click the <em>Set as default</em> link.','','11.2.5'),(8315,_binary 'At the bottom of the page, select the <em>Administration theme</em> that you want to use on administrative pages. Click <em>Save configuration</em> if you selected a new theme.','','11.2.5'),(8316,_binary 'If you changed the default theme for your site, visit the site home page or another page on the non-administration part of your site and verify that the site is using the new theme. If you changed the administration theme, verify that the new theme is used on administrative pages.','','11.2.5'),(8317,_binary 'Uninstall a theme that was previously installed, but is no longer being used on the site.','','11.2.5'),(8318,_binary 'Locate the theme that you want to uninstall, in the <em>Installed themes</em> section.','','11.2.5'),(8319,_binary 'The form has become outdated. Press the back button, copy any unsaved work in the form, and then reload the page.','','none'),(8320,_binary 'Deployment identifier','','none'),(8321,_binary 'Configure one or more search pages.','','11.2.5'),(8322,_binary 'Scroll down to the <em>Search pages</em> section. You will see a list of the already-configured search pages on your site.','','11.2.5'),(8323,_binary 'To configure an existing search page, click <em>Edit</em>. Or, to add a new search page, select the <em>Search page type</em> and click <em>Add search page</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8324,_binary 'Enter the desired <em>Label</em> name and URL <em>Path</em> for the search page.','','11.2.5'),(8325,_binary 'For <em>Content</em> search pages, select the desired level of influence in ranking search results of the available <em>Content ranking</em> factors.','','11.2.5'),(8326,_binary 'Click <em>Save</em>. You will be returned to the <em>Search pages</em> page.','','11.2.5'),(8327,_binary 'Verify that the correct search page is listed as <em>Default</em> in the <em>Status</em> column. If not, click <em>Set as default</em> in the <em>Operations</em> list for the correct search page.','','11.2.5'),(8328,_binary 'Optionally, disable or delete any search pages that you do not want to have available on the site (disabling is temporary, while deleting is permanent).','','11.2.5'),(8329,_binary 'Manage the search index, and make sure that the site is fully indexed for searching.','','11.2.5'),(8330,_binary 'What is the search index?','','11.2.5'),(8331,_binary 'Under <em>Indexing throttle</em>, select the <em>Number of items to index per cron run</em>. A smaller number will make cron faster and reduce the possibility of timeout; a larger number will make sure more of your site is indexed in fewer cron runs.','','11.2.5'),(8332,_binary 'Under <em>Default indexing settings</em>, enter the desired <em>Minimum word length to index</em>. Words smaller than this length will be dropped from both keywords when searching and content when indexing.','','11.2.5'),(8333,_binary 'If your site uses Chinese, Japanese, or Korean languages, optionally check <em>Simple CJK handling</em> under <em>Default indexing settings</em> to provide some support for these languages.','','11.2.5'),(8334,_binary 'Click <em>Save configuration</em>, and you should be returned to the <em>Search pages</em> page.','','11.2.5'),(8335,_binary 'Click <em>Re-index site</em> if you have changed the indexing configuration, or later on, if you believe that the search index has been corrupted.','','11.2.5'),(8336,_binary 'After waiting for cron to run several times, verify that the content has been fully indexed for searching. The overall status is listed under <em>Indexing progress</em>, and the status for each search page is shown in the <em>Indexing progress</em> column of the <em>Search pages</em> section.','','11.2.5'),(8337,_binary 'What are search pages?','','11.2.5'),(8338,_binary 'The core Search module organizes site search into <em>pages</em>. Each page allows users to search a particular type of content with a particular configuration. The configuration includes specifying a URL that starts with <em>search</em>, a name for the page, and additional options for some search page types.','','11.2.5'),(8339,_binary 'What modules provide site search?','','11.2.5'),(8340,_binary 'The core Search module provides the ability to configure search pages; search page types are provided by both core and contributed modules. The core modules that provide search page types are:','','11.2.5'),(8341,_binary 'The Node module, for searching content pages','','11.2.5'),(8342,_binary 'The User module, for searching user profiles','','11.2.5'),(8343,_binary 'The Help module, for searching help topics','','11.2.5'),(8344,_binary 'As an alternative to the core Search module\'s system of search pages, you can use contributed modules to provide site search. For example, the <a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/project/apachesolr\">Apache Solr</a> and <a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/project/sphinx\">Sphinx</a> contributed modules use third-party technology to provide site search.','','11.2.5'),(8345,_binary 'What are the limitations of the core Search module?','','11.2.5'),(8346,_binary 'There are two main limitations of the core Search module. First, it is not appropriate for very large sites -- if you have a large site, look into other search technologies like Apache Solr. Second, the Node search page type only supports exact keyword matching, which is not the behavior that most users will expect. You can improve this by installing a language-specific stemming module for your language (such as <a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/project/porterstemmer\">Porter Stemmer</a> for American English), which makes it so that, for example, a search for the word walk would match pages containing the words walk, walking, and walked.','','11.2.5'),(8347,_binary 'What are the search permissions?','','11.2.5'),(8348,_binary 'Users with <em>Use search</em> permission can use the <em>Search form</em> block and <em>Search</em> page; this permission is required for any search configured in the core Search module.','','11.2.5'),(8349,_binary 'In addition to <em>Use search</em>, <em>View user information</em> permission is needed for searching users.','','11.2.5'),(8350,_binary 'In addition to <em>Use search</em>, <em>View published content</em> permission is needed for searching content.','','11.2.5'),(8351,_binary 'Users with <em>Use advanced search</em> permission can use more complex search filtering when performing content searches.','','11.2.5'),(8352,_binary 'Configuring site search overview','','11.2.5'),(8353,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/documentation/modules/search\">Online documentation for the Search module</a>','','11.2.5'),(8354,_binary 'Document root for files','','none'),(8355,_binary 'Document root for public files','','none'),(8356,_binary 'Document root for private files','','none'),(8357,_binary 'Enables the mobile menu toggle at all widths.','','none'),(8358,_binary 'Configuring a previously-placed block','','11.2.5'),(8359,_binary 'Managing blocks','','11.2.5'),(8360,_binary 'Placing a block','','11.2.5'),(8361,_binary 'Managing height, width, and resolution breakpoints','','11.2.5'),(8362,_binary 'Managing the fields of contact forms','','11.2.5'),(8363,_binary 'Configuring personal contact forms','','11.2.5'),(8364,_binary 'Creating a new contact form','','11.2.5'),(8365,_binary 'Managing contact forms','','11.2.5'),(8366,_binary 'Setting a default contact form','','11.2.5'),(8367,_binary 'Using contextual links','','11.2.5'),(8368,_binary 'Changing the appearance of your site','','11.2.5'),(8369,_binary 'Managing content structure','','11.2.5'),(8370,_binary 'Running and configuring cron','','11.2.5'),(8371,_binary 'Extending and modifying your site functionality','','11.2.5'),(8372,_binary 'Maintaining and troubleshooting your site','','11.2.5'),(8373,_binary 'Optimizing site performance','','11.2.5'),(8374,_binary 'Making your site secure','','11.2.5'),(8375,_binary 'Tracking the content of your website','','11.2.5'),(8376,_binary 'Accessibility of the administrative interface','','11.2.5'),(8377,_binary 'Using the administrative interface','','11.2.5'),(8378,_binary 'Adding a field to an entity sub-type','','11.2.5'),(8379,_binary 'Configuring field display for an entity sub-type','','11.2.5'),(8380,_binary 'Configuring the edit form for an entity sub-type','','11.2.5'),(8381,_binary 'Adding a reference field to an entity sub-type','','11.2.5'),(8382,_binary 'Tracking which content a user has visited','','11.2.5'),(8383,_binary 'Changing the layout for an entity','','none'),(8384,_binary 'Configuring site search','','11.2.5'),(8385,_binary 'Creating and using shortcut administrative links','','11.2.5'),(8386,_binary 'Clearing the site cache','','11.2.5'),(8387,_binary 'Changing basic site settings','','11.2.5'),(8388,_binary 'Configuring error responses, including 403/404 pages','','11.2.5'),(8389,_binary 'Enabling and disabling maintenance mode','','11.2.5'),(8390,_binary 'Installing a module','','11.2.5'),(8391,_binary 'Uninstalling a module','','11.2.5'),(8392,_binary 'Running reports on your site','','11.2.5'),(8393,_binary 'Installing a theme and setting default themes','','11.2.5'),(8394,_binary 'Uninstalling an unused theme','','11.2.5'),(8395,_binary 'Creating a user account','','11.2.5'),(8396,_binary 'Adding a new role','','11.2.5'),(8397,_binary 'Managing user accounts and site visitors','','11.2.5'),(8398,_binary 'Modifying the permissions for a role','','11.2.5'),(8399,_binary 'Configuring how user accounts are created and deleted','','11.2.5'),(8400,_binary 'Modifying or deleting a user account','','11.2.5'),(8401,_binary 'Module Link','','none'),(8402,_binary 'Mobile menu all widths','','none'),(8403,_binary 'Site branding background color','','none'),(8404,_binary '<em>You haven’t created any frontpage content yet.</em>','','11.2.5'),(8405,_binary 'Drupal is an open source platform for building amazing digital experiences. It’s made, used, taught, documented, and marketed by the <a href=\"@drupal_community\">Drupal community</a>. Our community is made up of people from around the world with a shared set of <a href=\"@drupal_values\">values</a>, collaborating together in a respectful manner. As we like to say:','','11.2.5'),(8406,_binary 'Come for the code, stay for the community.','','11.2.5'),(8407,_binary 'There are a few ways to get started with Drupal:','','11.2.5'),(8408,_binary '<a href=\"@drupal_user_guide\">User Guide:</a> Includes installing, administering, site building, and maintaining the content of a Drupal website.','','11.2.5'),(8409,_binary '<a href=\"@create_content\">Create Content:</a> Want to get right to work? Start adding content. <strong>Note:</strong> the information on this page will go away once you add content to your site. Read on and bookmark resources of interest.','','11.2.5'),(8410,_binary '<a href=\"@drupal_extend\">Extend Drupal:</a> Drupal’s core software can be extended and customized in remarkable ways. Install additional functionality and change the look of your site using addons contributed by our community.','','11.2.5'),(8411,_binary 'Bookmark these links to our active Drupal community groups and support resources.','','11.2.5'),(8412,_binary '<a href=\"@drupal_events\">Upcoming Events:</a> Learn and connect with others at conferences and events held around the world.','','11.2.5'),(8413,_binary '<a href=\"@drupal_community\">Community Page:</a> List of key Drupal community groups with their own content.','','11.2.5'),(8414,_binary 'Migration failed with source plugin exception: @e in @file line @line','','none'),(8415,_binary 'Display %display has set node/% as path. This will not produce what you want. If you want to have multiple versions of the node view, use Layout Builder.','','none'),(8416,_binary 'A user-defined date format. See the <a href=\"https://www.php.net/manual/datetime.format.php#refsect1-datetime.format-parameters\">PHP manual</a> for available options.','','none'),(8417,_binary 'Manage translations for any entity that the user can edit','','none'),(8418,_binary 'The Filter module allows administrators to configure text formats. Text formats change how HTML tags and other text will be <em>processed and displayed</em> in the site. They are used to transform text, and also help to defend your website against potentially damaging input from malicious users. Visual text editors can be associated with text formats by using the <a href=\":editor_help\">Text Editor module</a>. For more information, see the <a href=\":filter_do\">online documentation for the Filter module</a>.','','none'),(8419,_binary 'There are four main types of data. <em>Content</em> is the information (text, images, etc.) meant to be displayed to website visitors. <em>Configuration</em> is data that defines how the content is displayed; some configuration (such as field labels) may also be visible to site visitors. <em>State</em> is temporary data about the state of your site, such as the last time the system <em>cron</em> jobs ran. <em>Session</em> is a subset of State information, related to users\' interactions with the site, such as site cookies and whether or not they are logged in.','','11.2.5'),(8420,_binary 'List (Options module): Stores values chosen from pre-defined lists, where the values can be numbers or text; see section below for more on list fields.','','11.2.5'),(8421,_binary 'Reference (core system): Stores entity references; see section above','','11.2.5'),(8422,_binary 'Text (Text module): Stores formatted and unformatted text; see section below for more on text fields.','','11.2.5'),(8423,_binary 'What settings are available for List field types?','','11.2.5'),(8424,_binary 'List fields associate pre-defined <em>keys</em> (or value codes) with <em>labels</em> that the user sees. For example, you might define a list field that shows the user the names of several locations, while behind the scenes a location code is stored in the database. Each list field type corresponds to one type of stored key. For example, a <em>List (integer)</em> field stores integers, while the <em>List (text)</em> field stores text strings. Once you have chosen the field type, the main setting for a list field is the <em>Allowed values</em> list, which associates the keys with the labels.','','11.2.5'),(8425,_binary 'What types of Text fields are available?','','11.2.5'),(8426,_binary 'There are several types of text fields, with different characteristics. Text fields can be either <em>plain</em> or <em>formatted</em>: plain text fields do not contain HTML, while formatted fields can contain HTML and are processed through <em>text filters</em> (these are provided by the core Filter module; if you have that module enabled, see the related topic below on filters for more information). Text fields can also be regular-length (with a limit of 255 characters) or <em>long</em> (with a very large character limit), and long formatted text fields can include a <em>summary</em> attribute. All possible combinations of these characteristics exist as text field types; for example, <em>Text (plain)</em> and <em>Text (formatted, long, with summary)</em> are two examples of text field types.','','11.2.5'),(8427,_binary 'What is a menu?','','11.2.5'),(8428,_binary 'A menu is a collection of <em>menu links</em> used to navigate a web site. Menus and menu links can be provided by modules or site administrators.','','11.2.5'),(8429,_binary 'Managing menus overview','','11.2.5'),(8430,_binary 'The core Menu UI module provides a user interface for managing menus, including creating new menus, reordering menu links, and disabling links provided by modules. It also provides the ability for links to content items to be added to menus while editing, if configured on the content type. The core Custom Menu Links module provides the ability to add custom links to menus. Each menu can be displayed by placing a block in a theme region; some themes also can display a menu outside of the block system. See the related topics listed below for specific tasks.','','11.2.5'),(8431,_binary 'Enabling web services','','11.2.5'),(8432,_binary 'What is a web service?','','11.2.5'),(8433,_binary 'A web service allows your site to provide its content and data to other web sites and applications. Typically, the data is transported via <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hypertext_Transfer_Protocol\">HTTP</a> in a serialized machine-readable format.','','11.2.5'),(8434,_binary 'What is serialization?','','11.2.5'),(8435,_binary 'Serialization is the process of converting complex data structures into text strings, so that they can be exchanged and stored. The reverse process is called <em>deserialization</em>. JSON and XML are the two most-commonly-used data serialization formats for web services.','','11.2.5'),(8436,_binary 'What is HTTP Basic authentication?','','11.2.5'),(8437,_binary '<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basic_access_authentication\">HTTP Basic authentication</a> is a method for authenticating requests by sending a user name and password along with the request.','','11.2.5'),(8438,_binary 'What modules provide web services?','','11.2.5'),(8439,_binary 'JSON:API module','','11.2.5'),(8440,_binary 'RESTful Web Services module','','11.2.5'),(8441,_binary 'Serialization module','','11.2.5'),(8442,_binary 'Provides a framework for adding specific serialization formats for other modules to use.','','11.2.5'),(8443,_binary 'HTTP Basic Authentication module','','11.2.5'),(8444,_binary 'There are also contributed modules that provide web services.','','11.2.5'),(8445,_binary 'Online documentation for the RESTful Web Services module','','11.2.5'),(8446,_binary 'Online documentation for the JSON:API module','','11.2.5'),(8447,_binary 'Comparison of the RESTFul Web Services and JSON:API modules','','11.2.5'),(8448,_binary 'Connecting text editors to text formats','','11.2.5'),(8449,_binary 'What is a text editor?','','11.2.5'),(8450,_binary 'Managing text filters and text formats','','11.2.5'),(8451,_binary 'Configure text formats on the site.','','11.2.5'),(8452,_binary 'What are text filters and text formats?','','11.2.5'),(8453,_binary 'A text filter is a processing step that can be applied to text, either to transform it in some way (such as converting URLs in the text into HTML links), or to defend against potentially-dangerous input from site users. A text format is an ordered sequence of text filters. Text filters are provided by modules; text formats are managed by the core Filter module.','','11.2.5'),(8454,_binary 'Text fields that have \"formatted\" in the field type name, such as <em>Text (formatted)</em>, use text formats. Users choose the text format when editing the field text; when the field text is shown on the site, it is processed by the chosen text format. Administrators can configure text formats and assign permissions for who can use each format. If the core Text Editor module is enabled, administrators can also associate visual editors with text formats.','','11.2.5'),(8455,_binary 'What text filters are available?','','11.2.5'),(8456,_binary 'Some of the more commonly used text filters are:','','11.2.5'),(8457,_binary 'Limits which HTML tags can be used; useful both for site security and enforcing site design.','','11.2.5'),(8458,_binary 'Line breaks in HTML source are displayed as horizontal spaces. This filter converts line breaks into HTML paragraph and line break tags.','','11.2.5'),(8459,_binary 'Takes plain URLs in text and turns them into HTML links.','','11.2.5'),(8460,_binary 'For text formats that allow HTML image tags, restricts images to URLs within this site.','','11.2.5'),(8461,_binary 'Click <em>Configure</em> to configure an existing text format, or <em>+ Add text format</em> to create a new text format.','','11.2.5'),(8462,_binary 'Enter the desired <em>Name</em> for the text format.','','11.2.5'),(8463,_binary 'Check the <em>Roles</em> that can use this text format. Some HTML tags allow users to embed malicious links or scripts in text. To ensure security, anonymous and untrusted users should only have access to text formats that restrict them to either plain text or a safe set of HTML tags. <strong>Improper text format configuration is a security risk.</strong>','','11.2.5'),(8464,_binary 'If the core Text Editor module is installed, see the related topic to connect a text editor to this text format.','','11.2.5'),(8465,_binary 'Under <em>Enabled filters</em>, check the text filters that you want to use.','','11.2.5'),(8466,_binary 'Under <em>Filter processing order</em>, drag the filters to the correct order. Choose the order carefully; for example, if you have a filter that results in a particular HTML tag being added to the text, that should run after a filter that restricts HTML tags, to avoid deleting the new tags the first filter added.','','11.2.5'),(8467,_binary 'Under <em>Filter settings</em>, verify and adjust the settings for each active filter that has configuration options.','','11.2.5'),(8468,_binary 'Click <em>Save configuration</em>, which will return you to the <em>Text formats and editors</em> page.','','11.2.5'),(8469,_binary 'Repeat these steps if you have additional text formats to configure.','','11.2.5'),(8470,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; <em>Block layout</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8471,_binary 'Configure menu settings for a content type','','11.2.5'),(8472,_binary 'For an existing content type, configure the available menus that will be shown as options on content editing screens; links to content items of this type can be added to these menus during editing.','','11.2.5'),(8473,_binary 'Locate the content type you want to configure, and click <em>Edit</em> in the <em>Operations</em> list.','','11.2.5'),(8474,_binary 'Under <em>Menu settings</em>, check the menus that you want to be available when editing a content item of this type.','','11.2.5'),(8475,_binary 'Optionally, select the <em>Default parent item</em>, to put links to content items under a default location in the menu structure.','','11.2.5'),(8476,_binary 'Adding a link to a menu','','11.2.5'),(8477,_binary 'Add a link to a menu. Note that you can also add a link to a menu from the content edit page if menu settings have been configured for the content type.','','11.2.5'),(8478,_binary 'Locate the desired menu and click <em>Add link</em> in the <em>Operations</em> list.','','11.2.5'),(8479,_binary 'Enter the <em>Menu link title</em> to be displayed.','','11.2.5'),(8480,_binary 'Enter the <em>Link</em>, one of the following:','','11.2.5'),(8481,_binary 'An internal path, such as <em>/node/add</em>','','11.2.5'),(8482,_binary 'A full external URL','','11.2.5'),(8483,_binary 'Start typing the title of a content item and select it when the full title comes up','','11.2.5'),(8484,_binary '<em>&lt;nolink&gt;</em> to display the <em>Menu link title</em> as plain text without a link','','11.2.5'),(8485,_binary '<em>&lt;front&gt;</em> to link to the front page of your site','','11.2.5'),(8486,_binary 'Make sure that <em>Enabled</em> is checked; if not, the menu link will not be displayed.','','11.2.5'),(8487,_binary 'Optionally, enter a <em>Description</em>, which will be displayed when a user hovers over the link.','','11.2.5'),(8488,_binary 'Optionally, check <em>Show as expanded</em> to automatically show the children of this link (if any) when this link is shown.','','11.2.5'),(8489,_binary 'Optionally, select the <em>Parent link</em>, if this menu link should be a child of another menu link.','','11.2.5'),(8490,_binary 'Click <em>Save</em>. You will be returned to the <em>Add link</em> page to add another link.','','11.2.5'),(8491,_binary 'Locate the menu you just added a link to and click <em>Edit</em> in the <em>Operations</em> list.','','11.2.5'),(8492,_binary 'Verify that the order of links is correct. If it is not, drag menu links until the order is correct, and click <em>Save</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8493,_binary 'Creating a menu','','11.2.5'),(8494,_binary 'Create a new menu.','','11.2.5'),(8495,_binary 'Click <em>Add menu</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8496,_binary 'Enter the title for the menu, which is used as the default block title if the menu is displayed as a block. If desired, also edit the machine name of the menu, which is by default derived from the title.','','11.2.5'),(8497,_binary 'Enter an administrative summary, which is displayed on the <em>Menus</em> page.','','11.2.5'),(8498,_binary 'If your site has more than one language, choose the language for the menu.','','11.2.5'),(8499,_binary 'Click <em>Save</em>. You will be on the menu editing page, ready to add links to the menu if the core Custom Menu Links module is installed; see related topics for further tasks.','','11.2.5'),(8500,_binary 'Reordering and disabling menu links','','11.2.5'),(8501,_binary 'Disable menu links or change the order and hierarchy of menu links.','','11.2.5'),(8502,_binary 'Click <em>Edit menu</em> for the menu that you want to edit.','','11.2.5'),(8503,_binary 'Drag menu links into a new order, or check/uncheck <em>Enabled</em> to enable or disable menu links.','','11.2.5'),(8504,_binary 'Click <em>Save</em> to save your changes.','','11.2.5'),(8505,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.php.net/manual/datetime.format.php#refsect1-datetime.format-parameters\">PHP date format codes reference</a>','','11.2.5'),(8506,_binary '[site:name]: The name of your website.','','11.2.5'),(8507,_binary '[site:url]: The URL of your website.','','11.2.5'),(8508,_binary 'Managing content listings (views)','','11.2.5'),(8509,_binary 'What is a view?','','11.2.5'),(8510,_binary 'A <em>view</em> is a listing of items on your site; for example, a block showing the most recent comments, a page listing news items, or a list of registered users. The listings can be formatted in a table, grid, list, calendar, RSS feed, and other formats (some output formats may require you to install additional contributed modules).','','11.2.5'),(8511,_binary 'What are the components of a view?','','11.2.5'),(8512,_binary 'When you first create a view, you will specify what type of <em>base data</em> is being displayed in the view, which cannot be changed. After choosing a base data type, you can edit the following components, which allow you to specify which data to output, in what order, and in what format:','','11.2.5'),(8513,_binary '<em>Displays</em>: whether the output goes to a page, block, feed, etc.; a single view can have multiple displays, each with different settings.','','11.2.5'),(8514,_binary '<em>Format</em>: the output style for each display, such as content item, grid, table, or HTML list.','','11.2.5'),(8515,_binary '<em>Fields</em>: if the Format allows, the particular fields to display.','','11.2.5'),(8516,_binary '<em>Filter criteria</em>: criteria to limit the data to output, such as whether the content is published, the type of content, etc. Filters can be <em>exposed</em> to let users choose how to filter the data.','','11.2.5'),(8517,_binary '<em>Sort criteria</em>: how to order the data. Sorting can also be exposed to users.','','11.2.5'),(8518,_binary '<em>Header</em> and <em>Footer</em>: content to display at the top or bottom of the view display.','','11.2.5'),(8519,_binary '<em>No results behavior</em>: what to do if the filter criteria result in having no data to display.','','11.2.5'),(8520,_binary '<em>Pager</em>: how many items to display, and how to paginate if there are additional items to display.','','11.2.5'),(8521,_binary '<em>Advanced</em> &gt; <em>Contextual filters</em>: like regular filters, except the criteria come from the <em>context</em>, such as the current date, page the view is displayed on, etc.','','11.2.5'),(8522,_binary '<em>Advanced</em> &gt; <em>Relationships</em>: additional data to pull in and display, related in some way to the base data of the view (such as data about the user who created the content item).','','11.2.5'),(8523,_binary '<em>Advanced</em> &gt; <em>Exposed form</em>: if you have exposed filters or sorts, how to display the form to the user.','','11.2.5'),(8524,_binary 'Managing views overview','','11.2.5'),(8525,_binary 'The core Views module handles the display of views, and the core Views UI module allows you to create, edit, and delete views in the administrative interface. See the related topics listed below for specific tasks (if the Views UI module is installed).','','11.2.5'),(8526,_binary 'Adding a new display to an existing view','','11.2.5'),(8527,_binary 'Add a new display to an existing view. This will allow you to display similar data to an existing view, using similar settings, in a new block, page, feed, etc.','','11.2.5'),(8528,_binary 'Under <em>Displays</em>, click <em>Add</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8529,_binary 'In the pop-up list, click the link for the type of display you want to add; the most common types are <em>Page</em> and <em>Block</em>. The new display will be added to your view, and you will be editing that display.','','11.2.5'),(8530,_binary 'Optionally, click the link next to <em>Display name</em> and enter a new name to be shown for this display in the administrative interface.','','11.2.5'),(8531,_binary 'Creating a new view','','11.2.5'),(8532,_binary 'Create a new view to list content or other items on your site.','','11.2.5'),(8533,_binary 'Click <em>Add view</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8534,_binary 'In the <em>View name</em> field, enter a name for the view, which is how it will be listed in the administrative interface.','','11.2.5'),(8535,_binary 'In <em>View settings</em> &gt; <em>Show</em>, select the base data type to display in your view. This cannot be changed later.','','11.2.5'),(8536,_binary 'Optionally, select or enter filtering, sorting, and page/block display settings; these can be added or changed later.','','11.2.5'),(8537,_binary 'Click <em>Save and edit</em>. Your view will be created; edit it following the steps in the related topics below.','','11.2.5'),(8538,_binary 'Editing an existing view display','','11.2.5'),(8539,_binary 'Edit an existing view display, to modify what data is displayed or how it is displayed.','','11.2.5'),(8540,_binary 'Under <em>Displays</em>, click the display you want to edit.','','11.2.5'),(8541,_binary 'For sections containing lists (such as <em>Fields</em> and <em>Filter criteria</em>), to modify or delete an existing item, click the name of the item. To add a new item, click <em>Add</em> in the drop-down list. To change the order of items, click <em>Rearrange</em> in the drop-down list.','','11.2.5'),(8542,_binary 'For sections containing individual settings (such as <em>Title</em> and <em>Format</em>), there are often two links for each setting. The first link shows the current value; click that link to change the value. If there is a second link called <em>Settings</em>, click that link to change the settings details. For example, if your <em>Format</em> is currently shown as <em>Unformatted list</em>, click <em>Unformatted list</em> to switch to using a <em>Grid</em> or <em>Table</em> format. Click <em>Settings</em> next to your format type to change the settings for your chosen format.','','11.2.5'),(8543,_binary 'When you have finished changing all the settings, verify that the display is correct by clicking <em>Update preview</em>. Return to editing settings if necessary.','','11.2.5'),(8544,_binary 'When you have verified the display, click <em>Save</em>. Alternatively, if you have made mistakes and want to discard your changes, click <em>Cancel</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8545,_binary 'For accessibility and search engine optimization, all images that convey meaning on websites should have alternate text. Drupal also allows entry of title text for images, but it can lead to confusion for screen reader users and its use is not recommended. Image fields can be configured so that alternate and title text fields are enabled or disabled; if enabled, the fields can be set to be required. The recommended setting is to enable and require alternate text and disable title text.','','none'),(8546,_binary 'This must be an internal path such as %add-node. You can also start typing the title of a piece of content to select it. Enter %front to link to the front page. Enter %nolink to display link text only. Enter %button to display keyboard-accessible link text only.','','none'),(8547,_binary 'Start typing the title of a piece of content to select it. You can also enter an internal path such as %add-node or an external URL such as %url. Enter %front to link to the front page. Enter %nolink to display link text only. Enter %button to display keyboard-accessible link text only.','','none'),(8548,_binary 'It is potentially insecure to display oEmbed content in a frame that is served from the same domain as your main Drupal site, as this may allow execution of third-party code. Refer to <a href=\"https://oembed.com/#section3\">oEmbed Security Considerations</a>.','','none'),(8549,_binary 'It is potentially insecure to display oEmbed content in a frame that is served from the same domain as your main Drupal site, as this may allow execution of third-party code. <a href=\":url\">You can specify a different domain for serving oEmbed content in the Media settings</a>.','','none'),(8550,_binary 'If checked, users creating new media items in the media library will see a summary of their selected media items, and they will be able to insert their selection directly into the media field or text editor.','','none'),(8551,_binary 'A flag for whether the link should be rendered in menus. (1 = a disabled menu link that may be shown on admin screens, -1 = a menu callback, 0 = a normal, visible link)','','none'),(8552,_binary 'Menu link language code.','','none'),(8553,_binary 'Translation set id.','','none'),(8554,_binary 'Menu link ID of the source language menu link.','','none'),(8555,_binary 'Users with the <em>Administer menus and menu links</em> permission can add, edit, and delete custom menus on the <a href=\":menu\">Menus page</a>. Custom menus can be special site menus, menus of external links, or any combination of internal and external links. You may create an unlimited number of additional menus, each of which will automatically have an associated block (if you have the <a href=\":block_help\">Block module</a> installed). By selecting <em>Edit menu</em>, you can add, edit, or delete links for a given menu. The links listing page provides a drag-and-drop interface for controlling the order of links, and creating a hierarchy within the menu.','','none'),(8556,_binary 'Default parent link','','none'),(8557,_binary 'Choose the menu link to be the default parent for a new link in the content authoring form.','','none'),(8558,_binary 'The selected menu link is not under one of the selected menus.','','none'),(8559,_binary '<strong>Warning:</strong> There is currently 1 menu link in %title. It will be deleted (system-defined links will be reset).<strong>Warning:</strong> There are currently @count menu links in %title. They will be deleted (system-defined links will be reset).','','none'),(8560,_binary 'Drupal @version module name','','none'),(8561,_binary 'Drupal @version machine name','','none'),(8562,_binary 'The human-readable name of the mapping','','none'),(8563,_binary 'The machine name of the mapping','','none'),(8564,_binary 'The group this mapping belongs to','','none'),(8565,_binary 'The mappings linked to the breakpoints group','','none'),(8566,_binary 'About searching','','none'),(8567,_binary 'You can display your shortcuts by enabling the <em>Shortcuts</em> block on the <a href=\":blocks\">Blocks administration page</a>. Certain administrative modules also display your shortcuts; for example, the core <a href=\":toolbar-help\">Toolbar module</a> provides a corresponding menu link.','','none'),(8568,_binary 'The new set is created by copying links from your default shortcut set.','','none'),(8569,_binary 'The new set is created by copying links from the %default set.','','none'),(8570,_binary 'The menu.mlid primary key for this menu link (= shortcut link).','','none'),(8571,_binary 'Administer menus and menu links','','11.2.5'),(8572,_binary 'The menu is only visible if the menu link for the current page is at this level or below it. Use level 1 to always display this menu.','','none'),(8573,_binary 'Menu language.','','none'),(8574,_binary 'Menu i18n mode.','','none'),(8575,_binary 'Administer roles and permissions','','11.2.5'),(8576,_binary 'Flood control blocked login attempt for uid %uid from %ip','','none'),(8577,_binary 'Flood control blocked login attempt for uid %uid','','none'),(8578,_binary 'Flood control blocked login attempt from %ip','','none'),(8579,_binary 'Menu link entry','','none'),(8580,_binary 'When providing a menu link as a tab, Drupal needs to know what the parent menu link of that tab will be. Sometimes the parent will already exist, but other times you will need to have one created. The path of a parent link will always be the same path with the last part left off. i.e, if the path to this view is <em>foo/bar/baz</em>, the parent path would be <em>foo/bar</em>.','','none'),(8581,_binary 'Normal menu link','','none'),(8582,_binary 'If creating a parent menu link, enter the title of the link.','','none'),(8583,_binary 'If creating a parent menu link, enter the description of the link.','','none'),(8584,_binary 'If the parent menu link is a tab, enter the weight of the tab. Heavier tabs will sink and the lighter tabs will be positioned nearer to the first menu link.','','none'),(8585,_binary 'Views cannot create normal menu links for paths with a % in them.','','none'),(8586,_binary 'If \"Custom\", see <a href=\"https://www.php.net/manual/datetime.format.php#refsect1-datetime.format-parameters\" target=\"_blank\">the PHP docs</a> for date formats. Otherwise, enter the number of different time units to display, which defaults to 2.','','none'),(8587,_binary 'Primary Branding Color','','none'),(8588,_binary 'A clean, accessible, and flexible Drupal front-end theme.','','none'),(8589,_binary 'Wide (1090)','','11.2.5'),(8590,_binary 'Olivero Medium','','11.2.5'),(8591,_binary 'Content blocks','','11.2.5'),(8592,_binary 'Failed to fetch available update data:','','none'),(8593,_binary 'See <a href=\"@url\">PHP OpenSSL requirements</a> in the Drupal.org handbook for possible reasons this could happen and what you can do to resolve them.','','none'),(8594,_binary 'Check <a href=\"@url\">your local system logs</a> for additional error messages.','','none'),(8595,_binary 'Check your local system logs for additional error messages.','','none'),(8596,_binary 'Drupal update settings','','none'),(8597,_binary 'For security reasons, your upload has been rejected.','','none'),(8598,_binary 'Exporting your complete site configuration','','11.2.5'),(8599,_binary 'Click <em>Export</em> and save the archive file.','','11.2.5'),(8600,_binary 'Select the <em>Configuration type</em> that you want to export, and then select the specific <em>Configuration name</em> to export.','','11.2.5'),(8601,_binary 'Use your browser to copy the text in the box marked <em>Here is your configuration</em> to the clipboard.','','11.2.5'),(8602,_binary 'Paste the copied text into a plain-text editor on your computer or other device, and save it using the suggested file name below the text box.','','11.2.5'),(8603,_binary 'Importing your complete site configuration','','11.2.5'),(8604,_binary 'Browse to find the <em>Configuration archive</em> that you want to import.','','11.2.5'),(8605,_binary 'Click <em>Upload</em>. Your configuration archive will be unpacked and placed in the configuration synchronization directory, and you will be redirected to the <em>Synchronize</em> page.','','11.2.5'),(8606,_binary 'Review the differences between your uploaded configuration and the active configuration, if any, and click <em>Import all</em> to import the changes.','','11.2.5'),(8607,_binary 'Select the <em>Configuration type</em> that you want to import.','','11.2.5'),(8608,_binary 'On your computer or other device, copy the YAML-format configuration that you want to import to the clipboard.','','11.2.5'),(8609,_binary 'Paste the clipboard text into the box labeled <em>Paste your configuration here</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8610,_binary 'Click <em>Import</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8611,_binary 'Managing and deploying configuration','','11.2.5'),(8612,_binary 'What is the configuration system?','','11.2.5'),(8613,_binary 'The configuration system provides the ability for administrators to customize the site, and to move and synchronize configuration changes between development sites and the live site. It does this in 2 ways:','','11.2.5'),(8614,_binary 'Providing storage for configuration','','11.2.5'),(8615,_binary 'Providing a process in which configuration changes can be imported and exported between instances of the same site; for example, from \"dev\" to \"staging\" to \"live\"','','11.2.5'),(8616,_binary 'Configuration data describes settings that define how your site behaves or is displayed. For example, when a site administrator updates settings using an administrative form, these settings are stored as configuration data. Configuration data describes settings as simple as a site name and as complex as a view or image style.','','11.2.5'),(8617,_binary 'What kinds of configuration are there?','','11.2.5'),(8618,_binary 'Active configuration','','11.2.5'),(8619,_binary 'Active configuration is the current working configuration of a site. Storage of active configuration is defined by the site, and resides in the database by default.','','11.2.5'),(8620,_binary 'A simple configuration item is a group of settings, such as the settings for a module or theme. Each simple configuration item has its own unique structure.','','11.2.5'),(8621,_binary 'Configuration entities are user-defined configuration items grouped by type, such as views, image styles, and content types. Each configuration entity within a type has a similar structure.','','11.2.5'),(8622,_binary 'Default configuration can be defined by a module, theme, or installation profile in its <em>config/install</em> or <em>config/optional</em> directories. Configuration is provided in YAML files (file extension .yml); YAML is a human-readable data serialization standard that is used by the core software for several purposes. Once the default configuration has been imported into the site\'s active configuration (through installing the extension), that configuration is owned by the site, not the extension. This means that future updates of the extension will not override the site\'s active configuration for that extension.','','11.2.5'),(8623,_binary 'What is configuration synchronization?','','11.2.5'),(8624,_binary 'Configuration synchronization is the process of exporting and importing configuration to keep configuration synchronized between different versions of a site; for example, between a development site and the live site.','','11.2.5'),(8625,_binary 'Each site has unique identifier, also called a <em>UUID</em>, which identifies the site to the system in any instance of the site, as long as the site instances have been reproduced as clones (cloning is when the codebase and database are copied to create a new site instance). When site instances are cloned, a \"dev\" instance of the site has the same UUID as the \"live\" instance. When site instances share the same UUID, configuration can be exported from one instance to another.','','11.2.5'),(8626,_binary 'The following list contains terms and concepts related to configuration synchronization:','','11.2.5'),(8627,_binary 'Exported configuration','','11.2.5'),(8628,_binary 'When configuration is exported, the active configuration is exported as a set of files in YAML format. When using the <em>Configuration synchronization</em> administrative UI, configuration can be exported as a full-export or single-item archive. This archive can then be imported into the destination site instance.','','11.2.5'),(8629,_binary 'Imported configuration','','11.2.5'),(8630,_binary 'Imported configuration is configuration that has been exported from another instance of the site (the \"source\") and is now being imported into another site instance (the \"destination\"), thereby updating its active configuration to match the imported configuration data set.','','11.2.5'),(8631,_binary 'The configuration sync directory location is set in the site\'s <em>settings.php</em> file. When configuration is exported, the active configuration is exported and described in YAML files which are stored in the configuration sync directory. After the first export, the system compares the site\'s active configuration with the configuration data in the sync directory and will only export active configuration items that are different than their counterparts in the sync directory.','','11.2.5'),(8632,_binary 'Managing configuration overview','','11.2.5'),(8633,_binary 'Configuration management tasks, such as exporting or importing configuration and synchronizing configuration, can be done either through the administrative UI provided by the core Configuration Manager module or a command-line interface (CLI) tool. Defining a configuration sync directory path other than the default value requires read/write access to the site\'s <em>settings.php</em> file.','','11.2.5'),(8634,_binary 'Most modules and themes also provide settings forms for updating the configuration they provide. See the related topics listed below for specific tasks.','','11.2.5'),(8635,_binary 'Managing media','','11.2.5'),(8636,_binary 'What are media items?','','11.2.5'),(8637,_binary 'What is the media library?','','11.2.5'),(8638,_binary 'The media library is a visual user interface for managing and reusing media items. Add media items to content using Media reference fields and the Media library field widget.','','11.2.5'),(8639,_binary 'What is an image style?','','11.2.5'),(8640,_binary 'An image style is a set of processing steps, known as <em>effects</em>, that can be applied to images. Examples of effects include scaling and cropping images to different sizes. Responsive image styles can associate image styles with your theme\'s size breakpoints. This allows serving images sized for the browser width.','','11.2.5'),(8641,_binary 'Overview of managing media','','11.2.5'),(8642,_binary 'The following modules provide media-related functionality:','','11.2.5'),(8643,_binary 'Media items and media types are managed by the core Media module.','','11.2.5'),(8644,_binary 'The core Media module provides a Media reference field to add media to content entities. The core File and Image modules also provide reference fields. It is recommended to use the Media reference field because it is more versatile.','','11.2.5'),(8645,_binary 'The core Media Library module provides the media library and the Media library field widget. With this module installed, the Media library field widget becomes the default widget for editing Media reference fields.','','11.2.5'),(8646,_binary 'The core Image module provides a user interface for defining image styles. The core Responsive Image module provides responsive image styles. Using the core Breakpoint module, and a breakpoint-enabled theme, these responsive styles can serve images sized for the browser.','','11.2.5'),(8647,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/8/core/modules/media\">Media module</a>','','11.2.5'),(8648,_binary 'Adding an image style','','11.2.5'),(8649,_binary 'Click <em>Add image style</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8650,_binary 'Enter a descriptive <em>Image style name</em>, and click <em>Create new style</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8651,_binary 'Under <em>Effect</em>, choose an effect to apply and click <em>Add</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8652,_binary 'Configure the effect on the next page. Most effects require some additional configuration after they are added.  For example, for the <em>Crop</em> effect, enter the <em>Width</em> and <em>Height</em> to crop the image to, and choose the <em>Anchor</em> point. Click <em>Add effect</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8653,_binary 'Repeat the previous two steps until all of the effects have been added.','','11.2.5'),(8654,_binary 'Drag to change the order of the effects. Then click <em>Save</em> to save the new order.','','11.2.5'),(8655,_binary 'The image style can now be used to format a field containing an image in your layouts or traditional field displays. It can also be used as part of a responsive image style. See related topics below for more information.','','11.2.5'),(8656,_binary 'Adding a new media type','','none'),(8657,_binary 'If there is not already a media type for the type of media you want to use on your site, click <em>Add media type</em>.','','none'),(8658,_binary 'Enter a <em>Name</em> and <em>Description</em> for your media type, and select the <em>Media source</em>.','','none'),(8659,_binary 'For most media sources, there is additional information that will need to be stored with your media item, in a field on your media type. Under <em>Media source configuration</em>, select an existing field to re-use to store this information, or select <em> - Create -</em> to create a new field.','','none'),(8660,_binary 'Note the types of metadata in the <em>Field mapping</em> section that can be mapped to fields on your media type.','','none'),(8661,_binary 'Optionally, add additional fields for the metadata noted above or for other information that you want to store to your media type by clicking on <em>Manage fields</em> (see related topic below).','','none'),(8662,_binary 'If you have added metadata fields, click <em>Edit</em>. Under <em>Field mapping</em>, select the fields you added for each piece of metadata information.','','none'),(8663,_binary 'You can now use this media type by adding a Media reference field to any content entity sub-type. See related topic below.','','none'),(8664,_binary 'Migrating, updating, and upgrading','','none'),(8665,_binary 'What are updating, upgrading, and migrating?','','none'),(8666,_binary '<em>Updating</em> is the process of changing from one minor version of the software to a newer version, such as from version 8.3.4 to 8.3.5, or 8.3.5 to 8.4.0. Starting with version 8.x, you can also update to major versions 9, 10, and beyond if your add-on modules, themes, and install profiles are compatible. <em>Upgrading</em> is the process of changing from an older major version of the software to a newer version, such as from version 7 to 8. <em>Migrating</em> is the process of importing data into a site.','','none'),(8667,_binary 'To upgrade a site from Drupal 6 or 7 to Drupal 8 or later, keeping the content and configuration the same, you will install the new version of the software and add-on modules and themes in a new site, and then migrate the content and other data from your old site into the new site.','','none'),(8668,_binary 'Overview of Migrating','','none'),(8669,_binary 'Provides the underlying API for migrating data.','','none'),(8670,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/upgrading-drupal\">Upgrading Drupal</a>','','none'),(8671,_binary 'Migrating data for an upgrade using the user interface','','none'),(8672,_binary 'Read the introduction and follow the <em>Preparation steps</em> on the page. Then click <em>Continue</em>.','','none'),(8673,_binary 'Select the Drupal version of the source site. Also enter the database credentials and public and private files directories (private file directory is not available when migrating from Drupal 6). Click <em>Review upgrade</em>.','','none'),(8674,_binary 'If the next page you see contains a message about conflicting content, that means that the site where you are running the upgrade is not empty. If you continue, you will lose the data in the site. If that is acceptable, click the button to continue; if not, start these steps over in a new, clean Drupal site.','','none'),(8675,_binary 'On the <em>What will be upgraded?</em> page, review the list of modules whose data will not be upgraded. If that list is not empty and you want to migrate the data from those modules, you will need to download contributed modules and/or install core or contributed modules, and start these steps over.','','none'),(8676,_binary 'When the list of modules that will and will not be upgraded meets your expectations, click <em>Perform upgrade</em> and wait for the upgrade to complete. You will see a message about the number of upgrade tasks that were successful or failed, and you can review the upgrade message log by clicking the link on the results page.','','none'),(8677,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/upgrading-drupal/upgrading-from-drupal-6-or-7-to-drupal-8-and-newer\">Upgrading from Drupal 6 or 7 to Drupal 8 (and newer)</a>','','none'),(8678,_binary 'Configuring a responsive image style','','none'),(8679,_binary 'Click <em>Add responsive image style</em>.','','none'),(8680,_binary 'Enter a descriptive <em>Label</em> for your style.','','none'),(8681,_binary 'Select a <em>Breakpoint group</em> from the groups defined by your installed themes and modules.','','none'),(8682,_binary 'On the next page, locate the fieldsets for the breakpoints provided by the selected <em>Breakpoint group</em>.','','none'),(8683,_binary 'For each breakpoint that you want to use, expand the corresponding fieldset. Select the <em>Select a single image style.</em> radio button under <em>Type</em> for the breakpoint, and select the <em>Image style</em> to use for images when that breakpoint is in effect. Repeat this step for the rest of the breakpoints you want to use.','','none'),(8684,_binary 'Click <em>Save</em>','','none'),(8685,_binary 'You can now use this responsive image style to format a field containing an image, in your layouts or traditional field displays. See related topics below for more information.','','none'),(8686,_binary 'Entity create','','none'),(8687,_binary 'Human name of the parent node type.','','none'),(8688,_binary 'Machine name of the parent node type.','','none'),(8689,_binary '@title sub-navigation','','none'),(8690,_binary 'Moving content between workflow states','','none'),(8691,_binary 'Who can change workflow states?','','none'),(8692,_binary 'Click <em>Edit</em> to edit the entity.','','none'),(8693,_binary 'At the bottom of the page, select the new workflow state under <em>Change to:</em> and click <em>Save</em>.','','none'),(8694,_binary 'Who can configure a workflow?','','none'),(8695,_binary 'Make a plan for the new workflow:','','none'),(8696,_binary 'Decide which workflow states you need; for example, <em>Concept</em>, <em>Review</em>, and <em>Final</em>.','','none'),(8697,_binary 'Decide on the settings for each state:','','none'),(8698,_binary '<em>Label</em>: the state name','','none'),(8699,_binary '<em>Published</em>: if checked, when content reaches this state it will be made visible on the site (to users with permission).','','none'),(8700,_binary '<em>Default revision</em>: if checked, when content reaches this state it will become the default revision of the content; published content is automatically the default revision.','','none'),(8701,_binary 'Decide which state content should be created in.','','none'),(8702,_binary 'Decide on the list of allowed transitions between states. For example, you might want a transition between <em>Concept</em> and <em>Review</em>. Each transition has a label; for example, the Concept to Review transition might be labeled \"Review concept\".','','none'),(8703,_binary 'Click <em>Add workflow</em>.','','none'),(8704,_binary 'Enter a name in the <em>Label</em> field, select <em>Content moderation</em> from the <em>Workflow type</em> field, and click <em>Save</em>.','','none'),(8705,_binary 'Verify that the <em>States</em> list matches your planned states. You can add missing states by clicking <em>Add a new state</em>. You can edit or delete states by clicking <em>Edit</em> or <em>Delete</em> under <em>Operations</em> (if the <em>Delete</em> option is not available, you will first need to delete any <em>Transitions</em> to or from this state).','','none'),(8706,_binary 'Verify that the <em>Transitions</em> list matches your plan. You can add missing transitions by clicking <em>Add a new transition</em>. You can edit or delete transitions by clicking <em>Edit</em> or <em>Delete</em> under <em>Operations</em>.','','none'),(8707,_binary 'Check the entity subtypes that you want to apply the workflow to. For example, you might choose to apply your workflow to the <em>Page</em> content type, but not to <em>Article</em>.','','none'),(8708,_binary 'Under <em>Workflow settings</em>, select the <em>Default moderation state</em> for new content.','','none'),(8709,_binary 'Click <em>Save</em> to save your workflow.','','none'),(8710,_binary 'Optionally (recommended), create a view for your custom workflow, to provide a page for content editors to see what content needs to be moderated. You can do this if the Views UI module is installed, by following the steps in the related <em>Creating a new view</em> topic listed below under <em>Related topics</em>. When creating the view, under <em>View settings</em> &gt; <em>Show</em>, select the revision data type you configured the workflow for, and be sure to display the <em>Workflow State</em> field in your view.','','none'),(8711,_binary 'Managing content moderation workflows','','none'),(8712,_binary 'What is a content moderation workflow?','','none'),(8713,_binary 'On some sites, new content and content revisions need to be <em>moderated</em>. That is, they need to pass through several <em>states</em> before becoming visible to site visitors. The collection of states and the definition of the transitions between states is known as a <em>workflow</em>. For example, new content might start out in a <em>Draft</em> state, and then might need to pass through several <em>Review</em> states before it becomes <em>Published</em> on the live site.','','none'),(8714,_binary 'Overview of content moderation workflows','','none'),(8715,_binary 'The core Content Moderation module allows you to expand on core software\'s \"unpublished\" and \"published\" states for content. It allows you to have a published version that is live, but have a separate working copy that is undergoing review before it is published. This is achieved by using workflows to apply different states and transitions to entities as needed.','','none'),(8716,_binary 'The core Workflows module allows you to manage workflows with states and transitions.','','none'),(8717,_binary 'See the related topics listed below for specific tasks and background information.','','none'),(8718,_binary 'On-line documentation about Content Moderation','','none'),(8719,_binary 'If %identifier is a valid account, an email will be sent with instructions to reset your password.','','none'),(8720,_binary '@language translation was not added. To add a translation, you must modify the configuration.','','none'),(8721,_binary 'No page is specified','','none'),(8722,_binary 'Provide markup for the area using any available text format.','','none'),(8723,_binary 'Provide markup for the area with minimal filtering.','','none'),(8724,_binary 'You may enter data from this view as per the \"Available global token replacements\" above. You may include the following allowed HTML tags: <code>@tags</code>','','none'),(8725,_binary 'You may include the following allowed HTML tags with these \"Replacement patterns\": <code>@tags</code>','','none'),(8726,_binary 'There are no @entity_type_plural matching \"%value\".','','none'),(8727,_binary 'Many @entity_type_plural are called %value. Specify the one you want by appending the id in parentheses, like \"@value (@id)\".','','none'),(8728,_binary 'Multiple @entity_type_plural match this reference; \"%multiple\". Specify the one you want by appending the id in parentheses, like \"@value (@id)\".','','none'),(8729,_binary 'The module \'@module_name\' is providing the database driver \'@driver_name\'.','','none'),(8730,_binary 'Failed to connect to the server. The server reports the following message: <p class=\"error\">@message</p> For more help adding or updating code on your server, see the <a href=\":handbook_url\">handbook</a>.','','none'),(8731,_binary 'HTML tables can be created with table headers and caption/summary elements.','','none'),(8732,_binary 'Alt text is required by default on images added through CKEditor (note that this can be overridden).','','none'),(8733,_binary 'Semantic HTML5 figure/figcaption are available to add captions to images.','','none'),(8734,_binary 'This log is not persistent','','none'),(8735,_binary 'The Database Logging module logs may be cleared by administrators and automated cron tasks, so they should not be used for <a href=\":audit_trail_wiki\">forensic logging</a>. For forensic purposes, use the Syslog module.','','none'),(8736,_binary 'Your upload has been renamed to %filename.','','none'),(8737,_binary 'Separate extensions with a comma or space. Each extension can contain alphanumeric characters, \'.\', and \'_\', and should start and end with an alphanumeric character.','','none'),(8738,_binary 'The list of allowed extensions is not valid. Allowed characters are a-z, 0-9, \'.\', and \'_\'. The first and last characters cannot be \'.\' or \'_\', and these two characters cannot appear next to each other. Separate extensions with a comma or space.','','none'),(8739,_binary 'Add %txt_extension to the list of allowed extensions to securely upload files with a %extension extension. The %txt_extension extension will then be added automatically.','','none'),(8740,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; @layout_link.','','11.2.5'),(8741,_binary 'Configure the block and click <em>Save block</em>; see @configure_topic for configuration details.','','11.2.5'),(8742,_binary 'Translating configuration','','none'),(8743,_binary 'For configuration entities, find the specific entity that you want to translate on the next page, and click <em>Translate</em> under <em>Operations</em>.','','none'),(8744,_binary 'Enter translations for the translatable text fields for the configuration item, and save.','','none'),(8745,_binary 'Configuring content language settings and translation','','none'),(8746,_binary 'Under <em>Custom language settings</em>, find the content entity types that should have customized language settings on your site. Check the box next to each one. A section will appear below the list with settings for that entity type.','','none'),(8747,_binary 'For each entity type you checked, in the settings section below check the boxes for each entity sub-type that should be <em>Translatable</em> on your site. If the entity type does not have sub-types, there is just one check box for the entity type as a whole.','','none'),(8748,_binary 'For each entity type or subtype, select the <em>Default language</em>. Also, if you want to have languages other than the default available when you create content, check <em>Show language selector on create and edit pages</em>.','','none'),(8749,_binary 'For each <em>Translatable</em> type or sub-type, look through the list of fields for the type or sub-type, and verify that only the fields that should be translatable are checked. For example, you would probably want to translate a <em>Title</em> field, but you might not want to translate a <em>Start date</em> field.','','none'),(8750,_binary 'Click <em>Save configuration</em> when all of your changes are complete.','','none'),(8751,_binary 'Working with languages and translations','','11.2.5'),(8752,_binary 'What text can be translated in your site?','','11.2.5'),(8753,_binary 'There are three types of text that can be translated:','','11.2.5'),(8754,_binary 'User interface text that is provided by the core software, your install profile, themes, and modules is provided in English, but can be translated into other languages. You can also download translations that community-members have provided.','','11.2.5'),(8755,_binary 'Working with languages overview','','11.2.5'),(8756,_binary 'Adding a language','','11.2.5'),(8757,_binary 'Add a language to your site.','','11.2.5'),(8758,_binary 'Click <em>Add language</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8759,_binary 'If your language is in the <em>Language name</em> list, select it and click <em>Add language</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8760,_binary 'If your language is not in the list, select <em>Custom language...</em> and enter the <em>Language code</em>, <em>Language name</em>, and <em>Direction</em> for the language. Click <em>Add custom language</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8761,_binary 'Configuring language detection and selection','','11.2.5'),(8762,_binary 'Configure the methods used to decide which language will be used to display text on your site.','','11.2.5'),(8763,_binary 'What is a language detection method?','','11.2.5'),(8764,_binary 'A language detection method is a way for your site to decide what language should be used to display text. This decision is made by evaluating a series of detection methods for languages; the first detection method that gets a result will determine which language is used. If you have more than one language on your site, you can configure the detection methods that are used and the order they are evaluated, for both user interface text and content text. Configuration text always uses the interface text method, and most sites use the same detection methods for all types of text.','','11.2.5'),(8765,_binary 'What language detection methods are available?','','11.2.5'),(8766,_binary 'The available detection methods depend on what modules you have installed. Some of the most commonly-used language detection methods are:','','11.2.5'),(8767,_binary 'Use the language from the URL, which can either be in a path prefix like <em>example.com/fr/page_path</em> for French (fr) language, or in a domain like <em>fr.example.com/page_path</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8768,_binary 'For logged in users, use the language they have set in their profiles.','','11.2.5'),(8769,_binary 'Use the language preferences from the user\'s browser.','','11.2.5'),(8770,_binary 'Use the language most recently selected from a <em>Language switcher</em> block.','','11.2.5'),(8771,_binary 'Use the language from a session parameter or a request parameter; for example, adding <em>?language=fr</em> to the end of the URL.','','11.2.5'),(8772,_binary 'Check the boxes to enable the desired language detection methods, and uncheck boxes for the methods you do not want to use.','','11.2.5'),(8773,_binary 'Drag the methods to change their order, if desired.','','11.2.5'),(8774,_binary 'Click <em>Save settings</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8775,_binary 'Click <em>Configure</em> on each enabled detection method and verify that its configuration is correct (or update the configuration if not).','','11.2.5'),(8776,_binary 'Importing a translation file','','11.2.5'),(8777,_binary 'Import a file (.po extension) containing translations for user interface text.','','11.2.5'),(8778,_binary 'Browse to find the <em>Translation file</em> you want to import. Select the language and check the desired import options.','','11.2.5'),(8779,_binary 'Click <em>Import</em> and wait for your file to be imported.','','11.2.5'),(8780,_binary 'Translating user interface text','','11.2.5'),(8781,_binary 'Translate user interface text strings from English into a non-English language that is configured on your site.','','11.2.5'),(8782,_binary 'Using the filters, search for a string or set of strings that you want to translate; make sure to select the correct <em>Translation language</em> if you have more than one non-English language on your site.','','11.2.5'),(8783,_binary 'Enter new translations and click <em>Save translations</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8784,_binary 'Repeat these steps until all of the desired user interface text is translated for all languages on your site.','','11.2.5'),(8785,_binary 'Checking interface translation status','','11.2.5'),(8786,_binary 'Check the current status of interface translations, and see if there are any updates available.','','11.2.5'),(8787,_binary 'Look at the <em>Interface translation</em> column in the language table, to find the percentage of user interface text that has been translated for each language.','','11.2.5'),(8788,_binary 'Optionally, click <em>Check manually</em> to update the report.','','11.2.5'),(8789,_binary 'View the report to find out if any languages have translation updates that you can download.','','11.2.5'),(8790,_binary 'You can use the <em>Migration</em> group of modules to perform the migration step of upgrading from Drupal 6 or 7 to Drupal 8 or later, as well as other migrations. These modules also provide APIs that can be used by programmers to write custom software for migrations. Here are the functions of the core migration modules:','','none'),(8791,_binary '[user:account-name]: The user\'s account name.','','11.2.5'),(8792,_binary 'Help search is not fully indexed. Some results may be missing or incorrect.','','none'),(8793,_binary 'If an upgrade has been performed on this site, you will be informed.','','none'),(8794,_binary 'You need to enter the database credentials of the Drupal site that you want to upgrade. You can also include its files directory in the upgrade. For example local files, /var/www/docroot, or remote files http://www.example.com.','','none'),(8795,_binary 'If there is existing content on the site that may be overwritten by this upgrade, you will be informed.','','none'),(8796,_binary 'Finally, a message is displayed about the number of upgrade tasks that were successful or failed.','','none'),(8797,_binary 'To import private files from your current Drupal site, enter a local file directory containing your site (e.g. /var/www/docroot). Leave blank to use the same value as Public files directory.','','none'),(8798,_binary 'Add <a href=\":modules\">contributed modules</a> to extend your site\'s functionality.','','none'),(8799,_binary 'Database driver provided by module','','none'),(8800,_binary 'Error adding / updating','','none'),(8801,_binary 'Added / updated %project_name successfully','','none'),(8802,_binary 'View user email addresses','','11.2.5'),(8803,_binary 'Users without this permission will not have access to email addresses on user pages or other places where they might be shown, such as Views and JSON:API responses.','','11.2.5'),(8804,_binary 'The username or email address is invalid.','','none'),(8805,_binary 'Password reset form was submitted with an unknown or inactive account: %name.','','none'),(8806,_binary 'Always show the default display','','none'),(8807,_binary 'Publish workspace','','none'),(8808,_binary 'Publish %source_label workspace','','none'),(8809,_binary 'There are no changes that can be published from %source_label to %target_label.','','none'),(8810,_binary 'Would you like to publish the contents of the %label workspace?','','none'),(8811,_binary 'Publish workspace contents.','','none'),(8812,_binary 'Successful publication.','','none'),(8813,_binary 'Publication failed. All errors have been logged.','','none'),(8814,_binary 'There is @count item that can be published from %source_label to %target_labelThere are @count items that can be published from %source_label to %target_label','','none'),(8815,_binary 'Publish @count item to @targetPublish @count items to @target','','none'),(8816,_binary 'Failed to fetch security advisory data:','','none'),(8817,_binary 'See <a href=\":url\">Troubleshooting the advisory feed</a> for possible causes and resolutions.','','none'),(8818,_binary 'Check <a href=\":url\">your local system logs</a> for additional error messages.','','none'),(8819,_binary 'Critical security advisories','','none'),(8820,_binary 'The System module displays highly critical and time-sensitive security announcements to site administrators. Some security announcements will be displayed until a critical security update is installed. Announcements that are not associated with a specific release will appear for a fixed period of time. <a href=\":handbook\">More information on critical security advisories</a>.','','none'),(8821,_binary 'Only the most highly critical security announcements will be shown. <a href=\":advisories-list\">View all security announcements</a>.','','none'),(8822,_binary '(<a href=\":system-help\">What are critical security announcements?</a>)','','none'),(8823,_binary 'Critical security announcements','','none'),(8824,_binary 'Security advisory settings','','none'),(8825,_binary 'Display critical security advisories','','none'),(8826,_binary 'How often to check for security advisories, in hours','','none'),(8827,_binary 'The security advisory JSON feed from Drupal.org could not be decoded.','','none'),(8828,_binary '[user:display-name]\n\nA request to cancel your account has been made at [site:name].\n\nYou may now cancel your account on [site:url-brief] by clicking this link or copying and pasting it into your browser:\n\n[user:cancel-url]\n\nNOTE: The cancellation of your account is not reversible.\n\nThis link expires in one day and nothing will happen if it is not used.\n\n--  [site:name] team','','11.2.5'),(8829,_binary 'The label of the link.','','none'),(8830,_binary 'Pre-header','','none'),(8831,_binary 'Banner Top','','none'),(8832,_binary 'Hero (full width)','','11.2.5'),(8833,_binary 'Move content from %from state to %to state.Move content from %from states to %to state.','','none'),(8834,_binary 'Your server does not support updating modules and themes from this interface. Instead, update modules and themes by uploading the new versions directly to the server, as documented in <a href=\":doc_url\">Extending Drupal</a>.','','none'),(8835,_binary 'Your server does not support adding modules and themes from this interface. Instead, add modules and themes by uploading them directly to the server, as documented in <a href=\":doc_url\">Extending Drupal</a>.','','none'),(8836,_binary 'Updating modules and themes requires <strong>@backends access</strong> to your server. See <a href=\":doc_url\">Extending Drupal</a> for other update methods.Updating modules and themes requires access to your server via one of the following methods: <strong>@backends</strong>. See <a href=\":doc_url\">Extending Drupal</a> for other update methods.','','none'),(8837,_binary 'Adding modules and themes requires <strong>@backends access</strong> to your server. See <a href=\":doc_url\">Extending Drupal</a> for other methods.Adding modules and themes requires access to your server via one of the following methods: <strong>@backends</strong>. See <a href=\":doc_url\">Extending Drupal</a> for other methods.','','none'),(8838,_binary 'Configuring comments','','11.2.5'),(8839,_binary 'Configure a content entity type/subtype to allow commenting, using a comment type that you have configured. See @content_structure_topic for more about content entities and fields, and @comment_type_topic to configure a comment type.','','11.2.5'),(8840,_binary 'Who can configure comments?','','11.2.5'),(8841,_binary 'In order to follow these steps, the Field UI module must be installed. You\'ll need the Comment module\'s <em>@comment_permissions_link</em> permission, in order to change comment settings for a comment field. You\'ll also need to have the appropriate permission for adding fields to the entity type or subtype that the comments are attached to. For example, to add a comment field to content items provided by the Node module, you would need the Node module\'s <em>Administer content types</em> permission.','','11.2.5'),(8842,_binary 'Follow the steps in the related <em>Adding a field to an entity sub-type</em> topic to add a field of type <em>Comments</em> to the desired entity type or sub-type.','','11.2.5'),(8843,_binary 'On the first field settings page, choose the <em>Comment type</em> to use for this entity type or sub-type. You\'ll also notice that the <em>Allowed number of values</em> field cannot be changed for comment fields.','','11.2.5'),(8844,_binary 'On the next field settings page, enter the desired settings for the comment field:','','11.2.5'),(8845,_binary '<em>Threading</em>: whether or not the comments are collected by threads, with people able to reply to particular comments instead of to the content entity itself.','','11.2.5'),(8846,_binary '<em>Comments per page</em>: the maximum number of comments displayed on one page (a pager will be added if you exceed this limit).','','11.2.5'),(8847,_binary '<em>Anonymous commenting</em>: whether or not anonymous commenters are allowed or required to leave contact information with their comments (only applies if anonymous users have permission to post comments).','','11.2.5'),(8848,_binary '<em>Show reply form on the same page as comments</em>: whether the comment reply form is displayed on the same page as the comments. If this is not selected, clicking <em>Reply</em> will open a new page with the reply form.','','11.2.5'),(8849,_binary '<em>Preview comments</em>: whether previewing comments before submission is <em>Required</em>, <em>Optional</em>, or <em>Disabled</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8850,_binary '<em>Default value</em>: each individual entity has its own comment settings, but here you can set defaults for the comment settings for this entity type or subtype. The comment settings values are:','','11.2.5'),(8851,_binary '<em>Open</em>: comments are allowed.','','11.2.5'),(8852,_binary '<em>Closed</em>: past comments remain visible, but no new comments are allowed.','','11.2.5'),(8853,_binary '<em>Hidden</em>: past comments are hidden, and no new comments are allowed.','','11.2.5'),(8854,_binary 'Online documentation for content comment settings','','11.2.5'),(8855,_binary 'Creating a comment type','','11.2.5'),(8856,_binary 'Create a new comment type. See @comment_overview_topic for information about comments and comment types.','','11.2.5'),(8857,_binary 'Who can create a comment type?','','11.2.5'),(8858,_binary 'Users with the <em>@comment_permissions_link</em> permission (typically administrators) can create comment types.','','11.2.5'),(8859,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; <em>@comment_types_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8860,_binary 'Click <em>Add comment type</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8861,_binary 'In the <em>Label</em> field, enter a name for the comment type, which is how it will be listed in the administrative interface.','','11.2.5'),(8862,_binary 'In the <em>Target entity type</em> field, select the entity type to be commented on. See @content_structure_topic for more about content entities and fields.','','11.2.5'),(8863,_binary 'Click <em>Save</em>. The comment type will be created.','','11.2.5'),(8864,_binary 'Optionally, if you have the core Field UI module installed you can follow the steps in the related topics to add fields to the new comment type, set up the editing form, and configure the display.','','11.2.5'),(8865,_binary 'Disabling comments','','11.2.5'),(8866,_binary 'Turn off commenting for a particular entity (see @content_structure_topic for more about content entities and fields). Note that if you want to turn off commenting for all entities of an entity type or subtype, you will need to edit the field settings for the comment field; see @comment_config_topic for more about configuring the comment field.','','11.2.5'),(8867,_binary 'Who can disable comments?','','11.2.5'),(8868,_binary 'You will need the <em>@comment_permissions_link</em> permission in order to disable commenting. You will also need permission to edit the entity that the comments are on.','','11.2.5'),(8869,_binary 'Find the entity you want to disable comments for, and edit it. For example, to turn off comments on a content item, you could find it by navigating in the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu to <em>Content</em>, filtering to find the content item, and clicking <em>Edit</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8870,_binary 'Under <em>Comment settings</em>, select the desired comment setting:','','11.2.5'),(8871,_binary 'Save the entity.','','11.2.5'),(8872,_binary 'Moderating comments','','11.2.5'),(8873,_binary 'Decide which comments are shown on the website.','','11.2.5'),(8874,_binary 'Who can moderate comments?','','11.2.5'),(8875,_binary 'Users with the <em>@comment_permissions_link</em> permission (typically administrators) can moderate comments. You will also need the <em>Access the Content Overview page</em> permission from the Node module (if it is installed) to navigate to the comment management page.','','11.2.5'),(8876,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Content</em> &gt; <em>@comment_published_link</em>. A list of all comments is shown.','','11.2.5'),(8877,_binary 'To unpublish comments, select one or more comments by checking the boxes on the left side (right side in right-to-left languages). Then select <em>Unpublish comment</em> from the <em>Action</em> select list and click <em>Apply to selected items</em>. If you select the <em>Delete comment</em> action, you can instead delete the unwanted  comments.','','11.2.5'),(8878,_binary 'To change the content of a comment click <em>Edit</em> from the dropdown button for a particular comment.','','11.2.5'),(8879,_binary 'To publish comments that are not yet visible on the website, navigate to the <em>@comment_unpublished_link</em> tab. Select one or more comments by checking the boxes on the left side (right side in right-to-left languages). Then select <em>Publish comment</em> from the <em>Action</em> select list and click <em>Apply to selected items</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8880,_binary 'Online documentation for moderating comments','','11.2.5'),(8881,_binary 'Managing comments','','11.2.5'),(8882,_binary 'What is a comment?','','11.2.5'),(8883,_binary 'What is a comment type?','','11.2.5'),(8884,_binary 'Comments are divided into <em>comment types</em>, which are the entity sub-types for the comment entity type. Each comment type has its own fields and its own form and display settings; each type can be used to comment on a single entity type. You can set up different comment types for different commenting purposes on your web site; for example, you might set up a comment type for recipes that has fields \"How did it taste?\" and \"Did the instructions work?\", and another comment type for blog entries that has only a generic comment body field.','','11.2.5'),(8885,_binary 'What is moderation?','','11.2.5'),(8886,_binary '<em>Moderation</em> is a workflow where comments posted by some users on your site are verified before being published, to prevent spam and other bad behavior. The core software provides basic moderation functionality: you can configure permissions so that new comments posted by some user roles start as unpublished until a user with a different role reviews and publishes them. Contributed modules provide additional moderation and spam-reduction functionality, such as requiring untrusted users pass a CAPTCHA test before submitting comments and letting community members flag comments as possible spam. See @users_overview_topic for more about users, permissions, and roles.','','11.2.5'),(8887,_binary 'Overview of managing comments','','11.2.5'),(8888,_binary 'The core Comment module provides the following functionality:','','11.2.5'),(8889,_binary 'Posting comments','','11.2.5'),(8890,_binary 'Creating comment types; the core Field UI module allows you to attach fields to comment types and attach comment reference fields to other entities so that people can comment on them.','','11.2.5'),(8891,_binary 'Configuring commenting','','11.2.5'),(8892,_binary 'Moderating comments as discussed above','','11.2.5'),(8893,_binary 'What is quick editing?','','11.2.5'),(8894,_binary 'Click the contextual links <em>Edit</em> button on the toolbar (in most themes, it looks like a pencil). Contextual <em>Edit</em> links with the same icon will appear all over your page.','','11.2.5'),(8895,_binary 'Find the contextual link for the part of the page you want to edit. For example, if you want to edit the settings for a block, the link should be in the top-right corner of the block, or top-left for right-to-left languages.','','11.2.5'),(8896,_binary 'Make your edits and submit the form.','','11.2.5'),(8897,_binary 'The core administrative interface has built-in compliance with many accessibility standards so that most pages are accessible to most users in their default state. However, certain pages become more accessible to some users through the use of a non-default or improved interface. These interfaces include:','','11.2.5'),(8898,_binary 'Enabling inline form errors','','11.2.5'),(8899,_binary 'Errors that occur when you submit a form, such as not filling in a required field, are sometimes difficult for users to understand and locate. In order to make these errors easier to find, the best practice is to put a summary of the errors at the top of the form page. To make them easier to understand, the best practice is to display error messages with the form fields they are related to. Both of these practices are implemented by the core Inline Form Errors module.','','11.2.5'),(8900,_binary 'What administrative interface components are available?','','11.2.5'),(8901,_binary 'Accessibility features, to enable all users to perform administrative tasks. See @accessibility_topic for more information.','','11.2.5'),(8902,_binary 'What are the sections of the administrative menu?','','11.2.5'),(8903,_binary 'The administrative menu, which you can navigate by visiting <em>@admin_link</em> on your site or by using an administrative toolbar, has the following sections (some may not be available, depending on which modules are currently installed on your site, and your permissions):','','11.2.5'),(8904,_binary '<strong>Content:</strong> Find, manage, and create new pages; manage comments and files.','','11.2.5'),(8905,_binary '<strong>Structure:</strong> Place and edit blocks, set up content types and fields, configure menus, administer taxonomy, and configure some contributed modules.','','11.2.5'),(8906,_binary '<strong>Appearance:</strong> Switch between themes, install themes, and update existing themes.','','11.2.5'),(8907,_binary '<strong>Extend:</strong> Update, install, and uninstall modules.','','11.2.5'),(8908,_binary '<strong>Configuration:</strong> Configure the settings for various site functionality, including some contributed modules.','','11.2.5'),(8909,_binary '<strong>People:</strong> Manage user accounts and permissions.','','11.2.5'),(8910,_binary '<strong>Reports:</strong> Display information about site security, necessary updates, and site activity.','','11.2.5'),(8911,_binary '<strong>Help:</strong> Get help on using the administrative interface.','','11.2.5'),(8912,_binary 'Install the core modules mentioned above to use the corresponding aspect of the administrative interface. See the related topics listed below for more details on some aspects of the administrative interface.','','11.2.5'),(8913,_binary 'Creating a content item','','11.2.5'),(8914,_binary 'Create and publish a content item. See @content_overview_topic for more about content types and content items.','','11.2.5'),(8915,_binary 'Who can create content?','','11.2.5'),(8916,_binary 'Users with the <em>@content_permissions_link</em> permission can visit the <em>Content</em> page as described in this topic. Each content type has its own create permissions. For example, to create content of type Article, a user would need the Article: Create new content permission. In addition, users with the <em>Bypass content access control</em> or <em>Administer content</em> permission can create content items of all types. Some contributed modules change the permission structure for creating content.','','11.2.5'),(8917,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>@content_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8918,_binary 'Click <em>Add content</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8919,_binary 'If there is more than one content type defined on your site that you have permission to create, click the name of the type of content you want to create.','','11.2.5'),(8920,_binary 'On the content edit form, enter the <em>Title</em> of your content, which will show as the page title when the content item is displayed on a page, and also as the label for the content item in administration screens.','','11.2.5'),(8921,_binary 'Fill in the other fields shown on the edit form for this specific content type.','','11.2.5'),(8922,_binary 'Leave the <em>Published</em> field checked to publish the content immediately, or uncheck it to make it unpublished. Unpublished content is generally not shown to non-administrative site users.','','11.2.5'),(8923,_binary 'Optionally, click <em>Preview</em> to preview the content.','','11.2.5'),(8924,_binary 'Click <em>Save</em>. You will see the content displayed on a page.','','11.2.5'),(8925,_binary 'Creating a content type','','11.2.5'),(8926,_binary 'Create a new content type. See @content_overview_topic for more about content types.','','11.2.5'),(8927,_binary 'Who can create a content type?','','11.2.5'),(8928,_binary 'Users with the <em>@content_permissions_link</em> permission (typically administrators) can create new content types.','','11.2.5'),(8929,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; <em>@content_types_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8930,_binary 'Click <em>Add content type.</em>','','11.2.5'),(8931,_binary 'In the <em>Name</em> field, enter a name for the content type, which is how it will be listed in the administrative interface.','','11.2.5'),(8932,_binary 'Optionally, enter a <em>Description</em> for the content type. You may also want to adjust some of the settings in the vertical tabs section of the edit page.','','11.2.5'),(8933,_binary 'Click <em>Save and manage fields</em>. Your content type will be created, and assuming you have the core Field UI module installed, you will be taken to the <em>Manage fields</em> page for the content type. (If you do not have the core Field UI module installed, the button will say <em>Save</em> instead.)','','11.2.5'),(8934,_binary 'If you have the core Field UI module installed, follow the steps in the related topics to add fields to the new content type, set up the editing form, and configure the display.','','11.2.5'),(8935,_binary 'Editing a content item','','11.2.5'),(8936,_binary 'Find a content item and edit it, or update a group of content items in bulk. See @node_overview_topic for more about content types and content items.','','11.2.5'),(8937,_binary 'Who can find and edit content?','','11.2.5'),(8938,_binary 'Users with the <em>@content_permissions_link</em> permission can use the <em>Content</em> page to find content. Each content type has its own edit permissions. For example, to edit content of type Article, a user would need the <em>Article: Edit own content</em> permission to edit an article they created, or the <em>Article: Edit any content</em> permission to edit an article someone else created. In addition, users with the <em>Bypass content access control</em> or <em>Administer content</em> permission can edit content items of all types. Some contributed modules change the permission structure for editing content.','','11.2.5'),(8939,_binary 'Optionally, use filters to reduce the list of content items shown:','','11.2.5'),(8940,_binary '<em>Title</em>: key word(s) from the title','','11.2.5'),(8941,_binary '<em>Content type</em>','','11.2.5'),(8942,_binary '<em>Published status</em>','','11.2.5'),(8943,_binary '<em>Language</em>','','11.2.5'),(8944,_binary 'If you enter or select filter values, click <em>Filter</em> to apply the filters.','','11.2.5'),(8945,_binary 'Optionally, sort the list by clicking a column header. Click again to reverse the order.','','11.2.5'),(8946,_binary 'To edit the title or other field values for one content item, click <em>Edit</em> in the row of the content item. Update the values and click <em>Save</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8947,_binary 'A few types of edits can be done in bulk to multiple content items. For example, to publish several unpublished content items, check the boxes in the left column (right column in right-to-left languages) to select the desired content items. For <em>Action</em>, select the <em>Publish content</em> action. Click <em>Apply to selected items</em> to make the change. The other actions under <em>Action</em> work in a similar manner.','','11.2.5'),(8948,_binary 'What is a content item?','','11.2.5'),(8949,_binary 'A <em>content item</em> is a type of content entity for page-level content, which can have fields that store text, HTML markup, images, attached files, and other data. See @content_structure_topic for more about content entities and fields.','','11.2.5'),(8950,_binary 'What is a content type?','','11.2.5'),(8951,_binary 'Content items are divided into <em>content types</em>, which are the entity sub-types for the content item entity type; each content type has its own fields and display settings. For example, you might set up content types for pages, articles, recipes, events, and blog entries on your web site.','','11.2.5'),(8952,_binary 'Overview of managing content','','11.2.5'),(8953,_binary 'The core Node module allows you to define content types, and add and edit content items. The core Field UI module allows you to attach fields to each content type and manage the edit form and display for each content type. See the related topics listed below for specific tasks. Many other core and contributed modules and installation profiles provide pre-defined content types, modify the permission structure for content items, and provide other functionality.','','11.2.5'),(8954,_binary 'Creating a URL alias for a content item','','11.2.5'),(8955,_binary 'Give a content item page a human- or SEO-friendly URL alias; you can follow similar steps to create an alias for a taxonomy term page. See @overview_topic for more about aliases.','','11.2.5'),(8956,_binary 'Who can create URL aliases?','','11.2.5'),(8957,_binary 'Users with the <em>@path_permissions_link</em> permission can create aliases. To follow the steps in this topic, you will also need permission to edit the content item.','','11.2.5'),(8958,_binary 'Locate and open the content edit form for the content item, or create a new content item (see related topics on creating and editing content).','','11.2.5'),(8959,_binary 'Under <em>URL alias</em> on the edit form, enter the desired alias (for example, \"/about-us\"). Make sure the alias starts with a \"/\" character.','','11.2.5'),(8960,_binary 'Verify that the page can be visited with the new alias, for example <em>https://example.com/about-us</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8961,_binary 'Editing a URL alias','','11.2.5'),(8962,_binary 'Change an existing URL alias, to correct the path or the alias value. See @path_overview_topic for more about aliases.','','11.2.5'),(8963,_binary 'Who can manage URL aliases?','','11.2.5'),(8964,_binary 'Users with the <em>@path_permissions_link</em> permission can edit aliases.','','11.2.5'),(8965,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administration menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Search and metadata</em> &gt; <em>@path_aliases_link</em>. A list of all the site\'s aliases will appear.','','11.2.5'),(8966,_binary 'Click <em>Edit</em> in the dropdown button for the alias that you would like to change.','','11.2.5'),(8967,_binary 'Make the required changes and click <em>Save</em>. You will be returned to the URL alias list page.','','11.2.5'),(8968,_binary 'Note that you can also add new aliases from this page, for any path on your site.','','11.2.5'),(8969,_binary 'Configuring aliases for URLs','','11.2.5'),(8970,_binary 'What is a URL?','','11.2.5'),(8971,_binary 'URL is the abbreviation for \"Uniform Resource Locator\", which is the page\'s address on the web. It is the \"name\" by which a browser identifies a page to display. In the example \"Visit us at <em>example.com</em>.\", <em>https://example.com</em> would be the URL for the home page of your website. Users use URLs to locate content on the web.','','11.2.5'),(8972,_binary 'What is a path?','','11.2.5'),(8973,_binary 'A path is the unique, last part of the URL for a specific function or piece of content. For example, for a page whose full URL is <em>https://example.com/node/7</em>, the path is <em>node/7</em>. Here are some examples of paths you might find in your site:','','11.2.5'),(8974,_binary 'node/7: Path to a particular content item.','','11.2.5'),(8975,_binary 'taxonomy/term/6: Path to a taxonomy term page.','','11.2.5'),(8976,_binary 'user/3: Path to a user profile page.','','11.2.5'),(8977,_binary 'What is an alias?','','11.2.5'),(8978,_binary 'The core software allows you to provide more understandable URLs for pages on your site, which are called <em>aliases</em>. For example, if you have an \"About Us\" page with the path <em>node/7</em>, you can set up an alias of <em>about</em> so that your visitors will see it as <em>https://www.example.com/about</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8979,_binary 'Overview of configuring paths, aliases, and URLs','','11.2.5'),(8980,_binary 'The core Path module provides the URL aliasing functionality. The contributed <a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/project/pathauto\">Pathauto</a> module allows you to configure automatically-generated URL aliases for content items and other pages. See the related topics listed below for specific tasks.','','11.2.5'),(8981,_binary 'Configuring taxonomy','','11.2.5'),(8982,_binary 'Create a taxonomy vocabulary and add a reference field for that vocabulary to a content entity. See @taxonomy_overview_topic for information about taxonomy and @content_structure_topic for more on content entities.','','11.2.5'),(8983,_binary 'Who can configure a taxonomy vocabulary?','','11.2.5'),(8984,_binary 'Users with the <em>@taxonomy_permissions_link</em> permission can configure a vocabulary. To add a field in the administrative interface, the core Field UI module must be installed, and you will also need the <em>Administer fields</em> permission for the entity you are adding the field to.','','11.2.5'),(8985,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; <em>@taxonomy_admin_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8986,_binary 'Click <em>Add vocabulary</em>.','','11.2.5'),(8987,_binary 'In the <em>Name</em> field, enter a name for the vocabulary (for example \"Ingredients\"), which is how it will be shown in the administrative interface. Optionally, add a description.','','11.2.5'),(8988,_binary 'Click <em>Save</em>. Your vocabulary will be created and you will see the page that lists all the terms in this vocabulary.','','11.2.5'),(8989,_binary 'Optionally, click <em>Add term</em> to add a term to the new vocabulary. In the <em>Name</em> field, enter the term name (for example \"Butter\"). Click <em>Save</em>. You will receive a confirmation about the term you created. You may optionally continue to add more terms.','','11.2.5'),(8990,_binary 'If you have the Field UI module installed, follow the instructions on the related <em>Adding a reference field to an entity sub-type</em> topic to add a taxonomy reference field to the entity type of your choice. The settings page will allow you to choose the <em>Vocabulary</em> that you created as the vocabulary to reference.','','11.2.5'),(8991,_binary 'You may also want to configure the display and form display of the new field (see related topics).','','11.2.5'),(8992,_binary 'Managing taxonomy','','11.2.5'),(8993,_binary 'What is taxonomy?','','11.2.5'),(8994,_binary '<em>Taxonomy</em> is used to classify website content. One common example of taxonomy is the tags used to classify or categorize posts in a blog website; a cooking website could use an ingredients taxonomy to classify recipes. Individual taxonomy items are known as <em>terms</em> (the blog tags or recipe ingredients in these examples); and a set of terms is known as a <em>vocabulary</em> (the set of all blog post tags, or the set of all recipe ingredients in these examples). Technically, taxonomy terms are an entity type and the entity subtypes are the vocabularies; see @content_structure_topic for more on content entities. Like other entities, taxonomy terms can have fields attached; for instance, you could set up an image field to contain an icon for each term.','','11.2.5'),(8995,_binary 'An individual vocabulary can organize its terms in a hierarchy, or it could be flat. For example, blog tags normally have a flat structure, while a recipe ingredients vocabulary could be hierarchical (for example, tomatoes could be a sub-term of vegetables, and under tomatoes, you could have green and red tomatoes).','','11.2.5'),(8996,_binary 'Taxonomy terms are normally attached as reference fields to other content entities, which is how you can use them to classify content. When you set up a taxonomy reference field, you can let users enter terms in two ways:','','11.2.5'),(8997,_binary 'New terms can be created right on the content editing form.','','11.2.5'),(8998,_binary 'Fixed list of terms','','11.2.5'),(8999,_binary 'The list of terms is curated and managed outside the content editing form, and users can only select from the existing list when editing content.','','11.2.5'),(9000,_binary 'Overview of managing taxonomy','','11.2.5'),(9001,_binary 'The core Taxonomy module allows you to create and edit taxonomy vocabularies and taxonomy terms. The core Field UI module provides a user interface for adding fields to entities, including the taxonomy reference field, and configuring field editing and display. See the related topics listed below for specific tasks.','','11.2.5'),(9002,_binary '<em>Page settings</em>, <em>Block settings</em>, etc.: settings specific to the display type, such as the URL for a page display. Most display types support an <em>Access</em> setting, where you can choose a Permission or Role that a user must have in order to see the view.','','11.2.5'),(9003,_binary 'What are bulk operations?','','11.2.5'),(9004,_binary 'Adding a bulk operations form to a view','','11.2.5'),(9005,_binary 'Who can edit views?','','11.2.5'),(9006,_binary 'The core Views UI module will need to be installed and you will need <em>@views_permissions</em> permission in order to edit a view.','','11.2.5'),(9007,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; <em>@views</em>. A list of all views is shown.','','11.2.5'),(9008,_binary 'If there is not already an <em>Operations bulk form</em> in the <em>Fields</em> list for the view, click <em>Add</em> in the <em>Fields</em> section to add it. (The exact name of the bulk form field will vary, and may contain keywords like \"bulk update\", \"form element\" or \"operations\" -- not to be confused with <em>operations links</em>, which are applied to each item in a row.) If the bulk operations field already exists, click the field name to edit its settings.','','11.2.5'),(9009,_binary 'Check the action(s) you want to make available in the <em>Selected actions</em> list and click <em>Apply (all displays)</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9010,_binary 'Verify that the <em>Access</em> settings for the view are at least as restrictive as the permissions necessary to perform the bulk operations. People with permission to see the view, but who don\'t have permission to do the bulk operations, will experience problems.','','11.2.5'),(9011,_binary 'Click <em>Save</em>. The action(s) will be available as bulk operations in the view.','','11.2.5'),(9012,_binary 'Create and download an archive containing all your site\'s configuration, exported as YAML files. See @config_overview_topic for more information about configuration.','','11.2.5'),(9013,_binary 'Export a single configuration item to a file. See @config_overview_topic for more information about configuration.','','11.2.5'),(9014,_binary 'Import the complete configuration of your site from an archive file, such as one that was previously exported (see @export_full_topic). See @config_overview_topic for more information about configuration.','','11.2.5'),(9015,_binary 'Import a single configuration item in YAML format, such as one that was previously exported (see @export_single_topic). See @config_overview_topic for more information about configuration.','','11.2.5'),(9016,_binary 'Find either the configuration entity type or the simple configuration item that you want to translate in the <em>Label</em> column of the list. Click <em>List</em> under <em>Operations</em> for a configuration entity, or <em>Translate</em> for simple configuration. (See @config_overview_topic to learn more about types of configuration and configuration entities.)','','none'),(9017,_binary 'The contact form will always have <em>Subject</em> and <em>Message</em> fields. If you want to add more fields, follow the steps in @adding_fields_topic.','','11.2.5'),(9018,_binary 'Change the workflow state of a particular entity. See @workflows_overview_topic for an overview of workflows, and @content_structure_topic for an overview of content entities.','','none'),(9019,_binary 'Create or edit a workflow with various workflow states (for example <em>Concept</em>, <em>Archived</em>, etc.) for moderating content. See @workflows_overview_topic for more information on workflows.','','none'),(9020,_binary 'Decide which roles should have permissions to make each transition; see @user_overview_topic for an overview of roles and permissions.','','none'),(9021,_binary 'Decide which <em>entity types</em> and subtypes the workflow should apply to. Only entity types that support revisions are possible to define workflows for. See @content_structure_topic for more information on content entities and fields.','','none'),(9022,_binary 'Configure language and translation settings for one or more content entity types (see @content_structure_topic for an overview of content entities). To do this, you must have at least two languages configured. Afterwards, you will have a <em>Translate</em> operation available for your content entities, either as a tab or link when you are viewing or editing content, or on content administration pages.','','none'),(9023,_binary 'A <em>layout</em> is a template that defines where blocks and other pieces of content should be displayed. The core Layout Discovery module allows modules and themes to register layouts, and the core Layout Builder module provides a visual interface for placing fields and blocks in layouts for entity sub-types and individual entity items (see @content_structure_topic for more on entities and fields).','','11.2.5'),(9024,_binary 'Core media items include audio, images, documents, and videos. You can add other media types, such as social media posts, through the use of contributed modules. Media items may be files located in your site\'s file system, or remote items referenced by a URL. Media items are content entities, and they are divided into media types (which are entity sub-types); media types can have fields. See @content_structure_topic for more information on content entities and fields.','','11.2.5'),(9025,_binary 'Content (blocks, content items, etc.) can be written in English or another language, and can be translated into additional languages. See @content_structure_topic to learn more about content.','','11.2.5'),(9026,_binary 'Many configuration items also include text that can be translated. Default configuration provided by your site\'s software is provided in English; you can also download community-provided translations. See @config_overview_topic to learn more about configuration.','','11.2.5'),(9027,_binary 'Exposes <em>entities</em> to other applications using a fully compliant implementation of the <a href=\"https://jsonapi.org\">JSON:API Specification</a>. See @content_structure_topic for more information on content entities and fields.','','11.2.5'),(9028,_binary 'Configure a text format so that when a user is editing text and selects this text format, a text editor installed on your site is shown. Configure the text editor, such as choosing which buttons and functions are available. See @filter_overview_topic for more about text formats.','','11.2.5'),(9029,_binary 'Follow the steps on @filter_overview_topic to add a new text format or configure an existing text format; when you reach the step about text editors, return to this topic.','','11.2.5'),(9030,_binary 'Return to @filter_overview_topic to complete the text format configuration, and be sure to save the text format.','','11.2.5'),(9031,_binary 'Add a field to an entity sub-type; see @content_structure_topic for an overview of entity types and sub-types, as well as an overview of field types.','','11.2.5'),(9032,_binary 'In <em>Add a new field</em>, select the type of field you want to add; see @content_structure_topic for an overview of field types.','','11.2.5'),(9033,_binary 'Configure the <em>formatters</em> used to display the fields of an entity sub-type, their order in the display, and the formatter settings. See @content_structure_topic for background information.','','11.2.5'),(9034,_binary 'Configure the <em>widgets</em> used to edit the fields of an entity sub-type, their order on the form, and the widget settings. See @content_structure_topic for background information.','','11.2.5'),(9035,_binary 'Add an entity reference field to an entity sub-type; see @content_structure_topic for more information on entities and reference fields.','','11.2.5'),(9036,_binary 'Check the indexing status of the Help search page. If it is not fully indexed, see @cron_topic about how to run Cron until indexing is complete.','','11.2.5'),(9037,_binary 'In the future, you can click <em>Rebuild search index</em> on this page, or @cache_topic, in order to force help topic text to be reindexed for searching. This should be done whenever a module, theme, language, or string translation is updated.','','11.2.5'),(9038,_binary 'Add a new image style, which can be used to process and display images. See @media_topic for an overview of image styles.','','11.2.5'),(9039,_binary 'Configure an entity sub-type to have its fields displayed using a layout (see @content_structure_topic for more on entities and fields).','','none'),(9040,_binary 'A layout consists of one or more <em>sections</em>. Each section can have from one to four <em>columns</em>. You can place blocks, including special blocks for the fields on the entity sub-type, in each column of each section (see @block_overview_topic for more on blocks).','','none'),(9041,_binary 'Add a new media type that can be referenced in Media reference fields; media types are a content entity type. See @media_topic for an overview of media items and media types, and @content_structure_topic for more information on content entities and fields.','','none'),(9042,_binary 'Migrate data into a new, empty site, as part of an upgrade from an older version of Drupal. See @migrate_overview_topic for an overview of migrating and upgrading.','','none'),(9043,_binary 'Configure a responsive image style, which can be used to display images at different sizes on different devices. See @media_topic for an overview of responsive image styles, and @breakpoint_overview_topic for an overview of breakpoints.','','none'),(9044,_binary 'Select a <em>Fallback image style</em> to use when none of the other styles apply. See @image_style_topic if you need to add a new style.','','none'),(9045,_binary 'Follow the steps in @search_index_topic to make sure that the search index is updated.','','11.2.5'),(9046,_binary 'The <em>Content</em> and <em>Help</em> search types provided by the core software pre-index their content and store the results in several database tables that are collectively called the <em>search index</em>. The process of indexing renders the content and breaks it up into words, which can then be matched more efficiently with keyword queries when users perform searches. Search indexing happens during cron runs; see @cron_topic for more information about cron.','','11.2.5'),(9047,_binary 'Follow the steps in @cron_topic to make sure a cron task has been configured.','','11.2.5'),(9048,_binary 'In order to configure site search using the core Search module, you will need to configure one or more search pages. You will also need to verify or alter permissions so that the desired user roles can search the site. (See @user_overview_topic for more information about roles and permissions.) For content search, you will also need to make sure that the search index is configured and that the site is fully indexed. Finally, you may wish to place the <em>Search form</em> block on pages of your site, or add the search page to a navigation menu, to give users easy access to search. See the related topics listed below for specific tasks.','','11.2.5'),(9049,_binary 'Clear the site cache. See @cache_topic for instructions.','','11.2.5'),(9050,_binary 'Uninstall a module. Your site should be in <em>maintenance mode</em> when you uninstall modules. See @maintenance_topic for details.','','11.2.5'),(9051,_binary 'Follow the steps in @view_edit_topic to edit the other settings for the display.','','11.2.5'),(9052,_binary 'Find the section whose settings you want to change, such as <em>Format</em> or <em>Filter criteria</em>. (See @views_overview_topic for more information.)','','11.2.5'),(9053,_binary 'The core software allows you to configure workflows in which each transition has an associated permission that can be granted to a particular role. See @configuring_workflows_topic for more information.','','none'),(9054,_binary 'Users with sufficient permissions can change the workflow state of a particular entity. See @changing_states_topic for more information.','','none'),(9055,_binary 'Remote oEmbed providers could not be retrieved due to error: @error. Using previously stored data. This may contain out of date information.','','none'),(9056,_binary 'Remote oEmbed providers database returned invalid or empty list. Using previously stored data. This may contain out of date information.','','none'),(9057,_binary 'Block type settings','','none'),(9058,_binary 'Navigation logo','','none'),(9059,_binary '@bundle_type is not @bundles or @last','','none'),(9060,_binary '@bundle_type is not @bundle','','none'),(9061,_binary 'Are you sure you want to remove the @entity-type %label from the %region region?','','none'),(9062,_binary 'This will remove the block placement. You will need to <a href=\":url\">place it again</a> in order to undo this action.','','none'),(9063,_binary 'The @entity-type %label has been removed from the %region region.','','none'),(9064,_binary 'Destination file \"%file\" exists','','none'),(9065,_binary 'The file could not be uploaded because the destination \"%destination\" is invalid.','','none'),(9066,_binary 'For more information see the <a href=\":html-specifications\">HTML Living Standard</a> or use your favorite search engine to find other sites that explain HTML.','','none'),(9067,_binary 'Converts an image to a format (such as JPEG).','','none'),(9068,_binary 'Determines the content language from the request parameter named \'language_content_entity\'.','','none'),(9069,_binary 'The source field definition for the %type media type is missing.','','none'),(9070,_binary 'Author/owner name','','none'),(9071,_binary 'Author/owner URL','','none'),(9072,_binary 'Media item default name','','none'),(9073,_binary 'Thumbnail local URI','','none'),(9074,_binary 'Resource source URL','','none'),(9075,_binary 'Resource width','','none'),(9076,_binary 'Resource height','','none'),(9077,_binary 'Resource HTML representation','','none'),(9078,_binary 'For more detailed information, see the <a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/updating-drupal\">Updating Drupal guide</a>. If you are unsure what these terms mean you should probably contact your hosting provider.','','none'),(9079,_binary 'Defined on the <a href=\"@appearance\">Appearance Settings</a> page.','','none'),(9080,_binary 'Save and go to list','','none'),(9081,_binary 'Automatic updating of Drupal core is not supported. See the <a href=\":update-guide\">Updating Drupal guide</a> for information on how to update Drupal core manually.','','none'),(9082,_binary 'Other permissions pages','','none'),(9083,_binary 'The main Permissions page can be overwhelming, so each module that defines permissions has its own page for setting them. There are links to these pages on the <a href=\":modules\">Extend page</a>. When editing a content type, vocabulary, etc., there is also a Manage permissions tab for permissions related to that configuration.','','none'),(9084,_binary 'Account %name has been disabled.','','none'),(9085,_binary 'Delete the account and make its content belong to the %anonymous-name user. This action cannot be undone.','','none'),(9086,_binary 'Delete the account and its content. This action cannot be undone.','','none'),(9087,_binary 'To log in to this site, your browser must accept cookies from the domain %domain.','','none'),(9088,_binary 'Cancellation method','','none'),(9089,_binary 'This view will be displayed by visiting this path on your site. You may use \"%\" or named route parameters like \"%node\" in your URL to represent values that will be used for contextual filters: For example, \"node/%node/feed\" or \"view_path/%\". Named route parameters are required when this path matches an existing path. For example, paths such as \"taxonomy/term/%taxonomy_term\" or \"user/%user/custom-view\".','','none'),(9090,_binary 'Sort field identifier','','none'),(9091,_binary 'This will appear in the URL after the ?, as value of \'sort_by\' parameter, to identify this sort field. Cannot be blank. Only letters, digits and the dot (\'.\'), hyphen (\'-\'), underscore (\'_\'), and tilde (\'~\') characters are allowed.','','none'),(9092,_binary 'This identifier is already used by %label sort handler.','','none'),(9093,_binary 'Switch to this workspace','','none'),(9094,_binary 'Workspace changes','','none'),(9095,_binary 'This workspace has no changes.','','none'),(9096,_binary '@entity_type_label: @entity_bundle_label','','none'),(9097,_binary 'admin/reports/dblog/event/{{ wid }}','','11.2.5'),(9098,_binary 'admin/content/files/usage/{{ fid }}','','11.2.5'),(9099,_binary '@interval','','11.2.5'),(9100,_binary 'Code Block','','none'),(9101,_binary 'The CKEditor 5 module provides a highly-accessible, highly-usable visual text editor and adds a toolbar to text fields. Users can use buttons to format content and to create semantically correct and valid HTML. The CKEditor module uses the framework provided by the <a href=\":text_editor\">Text Editor module</a>. It requires JavaScript to be enabled in the browser. For more information, see the <a href=\":doc_url\">online documentation for the CKEditor 5 module</a> and the <a href=\":cke5_url\">CKEditor 5 website</a>.','','none'),(9102,_binary 'Enabling CKEditor 5 for individual text formats','','none'),(9103,_binary 'When CKEditor 5 is chosen from the <em>Text editor</em> drop-down menu, its toolbar configuration is displayed. You can add and remove buttons from the <em>Active toolbar</em> by dragging and dropping them. Separators and rows can be added to organize the buttons.','','none'),(9104,_binary 'Filtering HTML content','','none'),(9105,_binary 'Unlike other text editors, plugin configuration determines the tags and attributes allowed in text formats using CKEditor 5. If using the <em>Limit allowed HTML tags and correct faulty HTML</em> filter, this filter\'s values will be automatically set based on enabled plugins and toolbar items.','','none'),(9106,_binary 'Developing CKEditor 5 plugins in Drupal','','none'),(9107,_binary 'See the <a href=\":dev_docs_url\">online documentation</a> for detailed information on developing CKEditor 5 plugins for use in Drupal.','','none'),(9108,_binary 'The built in WYSIWYG editor (CKEditor 5) comes with a number of accessibility features. CKEditor 5 comes with built in <a href=\":shortcuts\">keyboard shortcuts</a>, which can be beneficial for both power users and keyboard only users.','','none'),(9109,_binary 'To support multilingual page content, CKEditor 5 can be configured to include a language button in the toolbar.','','none'),(9110,_binary 'With CKEditor 5 this is a\n          read-only field. The allowed HTML tags and attributes are determined\n          by the CKEditor 5 configuration. Manually removing tags would break\n          enabled functionality, and any manually added tags would be removed by\n          CKEditor 5 on render.','','none'),(9111,_binary 'CKEditor 5','','none'),(9112,_binary 'Text Format plus Text Editor pair using CKEditor 5','','none'),(9113,_binary 'CKEditor 5 settings','','none'),(9114,_binary 'Enabled Headings','','none'),(9115,_binary 'Source Editing','','none'),(9116,_binary 'Allowed Tag','','none'),(9117,_binary 'Button @name has been copied to the active toolbar.','','none'),(9118,_binary 'Button @name has been removed from the active toolbar.','','none'),(9119,_binary 'The <em>Source Editing</em> plugin was enabled to support tags and/or attributes that are not explicitly supported by any available CKEditor 5 plugins.','','none'),(9120,_binary 'These are the headings that will appear in the headings dropdown. If a heading is not chosen here, it does not necessarily mean the corresponding tag is disallowed in the text format.','','none'),(9121,_binary 'Manually editable HTML tags','','none'),(9122,_binary 'A list of HTML tags that can be used while editing source. It is only necessary to add tags that are not already supported by other enabled plugins. For example, if \"Bold\" is enabled, it is not necessary to add the <code>&lt;strong&gt;</code> tag, but it may be necessary to add <code>&lt;dl&gt;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;dd&gt;</code> in a format that does not have a definition list plugin, but requires definition list markup.','','none'),(9123,_binary 'CKEditor 5 toolbar configuration','','none'),(9124,_binary 'Press the down arrow key to add to the toolbar.','','none'),(9125,_binary 'Move this button in the toolbar by pressing the left or right arrow keys. Press the up arrow key to remove from the toolbar.','','none'),(9126,_binary 'Invalid toolbar value.','','none'),(9127,_binary 'CKEditor 5 element','Validation','none'),(9128,_binary 'The following tag is not valid HTML: %provided_element.','','none'),(9129,_binary 'CKEditor 5 enabled configurable plugins','Validation','none'),(9130,_binary 'Configuration for the enabled plugin \"%plugin_label\" (%plugin_id) is missing.','','none'),(9131,_binary 'CKEditor 5 fundamental text format compatibility','Validation','none'),(9132,_binary 'CKEditor 5 only works with HTML-based text formats. The \"%filter_label\" (%filter_plugin_id) filter implies this text format is not HTML anymore.','','none'),(9133,_binary 'CKEditor 5 needs at least the &lt;p&gt; and &lt;br&gt; tags to be allowed to be able to function. They are not allowed by the \"%filter_label\" (%filter_plugin_id) filter.','','none'),(9134,_binary 'The current CKEditor 5 build requires the following elements and attributes: <br><code>@list</code><br>The following elements are not supported: <br><code>@diff</code>','','none'),(9135,_binary 'The current CKEditor 5 build requires the following elements and attributes: <br><code>@list</code><br>The following elements are missing: <br><code>@diff</code>','','none'),(9136,_binary 'CKEditor 5 toolbar item conditions must be met','Validation','none'),(9137,_binary 'The %toolbar_item toolbar item requires image uploads to be enabled.','','none'),(9138,_binary 'The %toolbar_item toolbar item requires the %filter filter to be enabled.','','none'),(9139,_binary 'The %toolbar_item toolbar item requires the %plugin plugin to be enabled.','','none'),(9140,_binary 'The %toolbar_item toolbar item requires the %plugins plugins to be enabled.','','none'),(9141,_binary 'CKEditor 5 toolbar item','Validation','none'),(9142,_binary 'The provided toolbar item %toolbar_item is not valid.','','none'),(9143,_binary 'CKEditor 5 toolbar item dependency','Validation','none'),(9144,_binary 'Depends on %toolbar_item, which is not enabled.','','none'),(9145,_binary 'Move a button into the <em>Active toolbar</em> to enable it, or into the list of <em>Available buttons</em> to disable it. Buttons may be moved with the mouse or keyboard arrow keys.','','none'),(9146,_binary 'PostgreSQL pg_trgm extension','','none'),(9147,_binary 'Not created','','none'),(9148,_binary 'Package Manager','','none'),(9149,_binary 'Package Manager settings','','none'),(9150,_binary 'The Drupal directory \"@dir\" is not writable.','','none'),(9151,_binary 'The vendor directory \"@dir\" is not writable.','','none'),(9152,_binary 'The file system is not writable.','','none'),(9153,_binary 'Preview failed','','none'),(9154,_binary 'Drupal Media toolbar','','none'),(9155,_binary 'Link media','','none'),(9156,_binary 'Add %label effect to style %style','','none'),(9157,_binary 'Edit %label effect on style %style','','none'),(9158,_binary 'Maintenance mode Retry-After header settings','','none'),(9159,_binary 'Minimum value for Retry-After header in seconds','','none'),(9160,_binary 'Maximum value for Retry-After header in seconds','','none'),(9161,_binary 'The MySQL module provides the connection between Drupal and a MySQL, MariaDB or equivalent database. For more information, see the <a href=\":mysql\">online documentation for the MySQL module</a>.','','none'),(9162,_binary 'The PostgreSQL module provides the connection between Drupal and a PostgreSQL database. For more information, see the <a href=\":pgsql\">online documentation for the PostgreSQL module</a>.','','none'),(9163,_binary 'The SQLite module provides the connection between Drupal and a SQLite database. For more information, see the <a href=\":sqlite\">online documentation for the SQLite module</a>.','','none'),(9164,_binary 'Deprecated modules found: %module_list.','','none'),(9165,_binary 'Deprecated themes found: %theme_list.','','none'),(9166,_binary 'Database support for JSON','','11.2.5'),(9167,_binary 'Non-stable modules','','none'),(9168,_binary '@lifecycle','','none'),(9169,_binary 'View information on the @lifecycle status of the module @module','','none'),(9170,_binary 'Help <span class=\"visually-hidden\">for @module</span>','','none'),(9171,_binary 'Permissions <span class=\"visually-hidden\">for @module</span>','','none'),(9172,_binary 'Configure <span class=\"visually-hidden\">@module</span>','','none'),(9173,_binary '<a href=\":url\">Deprecated modules</a> are modules that may be removed from the next major release of Drupal core and the relevant contributed module. Use at your own risk.','','none'),(9174,_binary '<a href=\":url\">Deprecated modules</a> are modules that may be removed from the next major release of this project. Use at your own risk.','','none'),(9175,_binary '<a href=\":url\">Deprecated modules</a> are modules that may be removed from the next major release of Drupal core. Use at your own risk.','','none'),(9176,_binary 'The @name module is deprecated. (more information)','','none'),(9177,_binary 'about the status of the @name module','','none'),(9178,_binary 'The following module is experimental: @modules.The following modules are experimental: @modules.','','none'),(9179,_binary 'Get the actual @label from a @label revision','','none'),(9180,_binary 'Database connection supports the JSON type.','','none'),(9181,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/system-requirements\">Database connection does not support JSON.</a>','','none'),(9182,_binary 'Media widget','','none'),(9183,_binary 'Not all functionality may be available because some information could not be retrieved.','','none'),(9184,_binary 'Allow the user to resize images','','none'),(9185,_binary 'PostgreSQL has the pg_trgm extension enabled.','','none'),(9186,_binary 'The <a href=\":pg_trgm\">pg_trgm</a> PostgreSQL extension is not present. The extension is required by Drupal 10 to improve performance when using PostgreSQL. See <a href=\":requirements\">Drupal database server requirements</a> for more information.','','none'),(9187,_binary 'Drupal could not check for the pg_trgm extension: @error.','','none'),(9188,_binary 'Alternative text override','','none'),(9189,_binary 'Override media image alternative text','','none'),(9190,_binary 'Enter media caption','','none'),(9191,_binary 'Caption media','','none'),(9192,_binary 'Toggle caption off','','none'),(9193,_binary 'Toggle caption on','','none'),(9194,_binary 'Package Manager is a framework for updating Drupal core and installing contributed modules and themes via Composer. It has no user interface, but it provides an API for creating a temporary copy of the current site, making changes to the copy, and then syncing those changes back into the live site.','','none'),(9195,_binary 'Package Manager dispatches events before and after various operations, and external code can integrate with it by subscribing to those events. For more information, see <code>package_manager.api.php</code>.','','none'),(9196,_binary 'Modules cannot be uninstalled while Package Manager is applying staged changes to the active code base.','','none'),(9197,_binary 'Post updating @extension','','none'),(9198,_binary 'Press the down arrow key to activate','','none'),(9199,_binary 'Decorative image','','11.2.5'),(9200,_binary 'Add missing alternative text','','11.2.5'),(9201,_binary 'Change image alternative text','','11.2.5'),(9202,_binary 'Source editing should only use otherwise unavailable tags and attributes','Validation','none'),(9203,_binary 'The following @element_type(s) are already supported by enabled plugins and should not be added to the Source Editing \"Manually editable HTML tags\" field: %overlapping_tags.','','none'),(9204,_binary 'The following @element_type(s) are already supported by available plugins and should not be added to the Source Editing \"Manually editable HTML tags\" field. Instead, enable the following plugins to support these @element_types: %overlapping_tags.','','none'),(9205,_binary 'There is no staged configuration.','','none'),(9206,_binary 'The staged configuration is identical to the active configuration.','','none'),(9207,_binary 'The main way to change the overall appearance of your site is to switch the default theme. The core Layout Builder and Layout Discovery modules allow you to define layouts for your site\'s content, and the core Breakpoint module helps themes change appearance for different-sized devices. See the related topics listed below for specific tasks.','','11.2.5'),(9208,_binary 'Using in-line (quick) settings editing','','11.2.5'),(9209,_binary 'Edit settings in place.','','11.2.5'),(9210,_binary 'The core Settings Tray module provides the ability to quickly edit settings inline. It requires the core Contextual Links module in order to expose the links that let you edit in place.','','11.2.5'),(9211,_binary 'Who can edit settings in place?','','11.2.5'),(9212,_binary 'In order to follow these steps to edit settings in place, the core Settings Tray module must be installed. Also, either the core Toolbar module or a contributed replacement must be installed. You will need to have <em>Use contextual links</em> permission, as well as permission to edit the particular content or settings.','','11.2.5'),(9213,_binary 'Find and visit a page on your site that has the settings that you would like to edit.','','11.2.5'),(9214,_binary 'Click the link to open the contextual links menu, and click <em>Quick edit</em>. An editing form for the settings should appear on the page.','','11.2.5'),(9215,_binary 'In-place or <em>quick</em> editing. In-place editing of configuration is provided by the core Settings Tray module. See @settings_tray_topic for more information.','','11.2.5'),(9216,_binary 'Image loading settings','','none'),(9217,_binary 'Loading attribute','','none'),(9218,_binary 'Image loading','','none'),(9219,_binary 'Lazy render images with native image loading attribute (<em>loading=\"lazy\"</em>). This improves performance by allowing browsers to lazily load images.','','none'),(9220,_binary 'Lazy (<em>loading=\"lazy\"</em>)','','none'),(9221,_binary 'Eager (<em>loading=\"eager\"</em>)','','none'),(9222,_binary 'Image loading attribute','','none'),(9223,_binary 'Select the loading attribute for images. <a href=\":link\">Learn more about the loading attribute for images.</a>','','none'),(9224,_binary 'Delays loading the image until that section of the page is visible in the browser. When in doubt, lazy loading is recommended.','','none'),(9225,_binary 'Force browsers to download an image as soon as possible. This is the browser default for legacy reasons. Only use this option when the image is always expected to render.','','none'),(9226,_binary 'Image loading: @attribute','','none'),(9227,_binary 'Your PHP installation is too old. Drupal requires at least PHP %version. It is recommended to upgrade to PHP version %recommended or higher for the best ongoing support. See <a href=\"http://php.net/supported-versions.php\">PHP\'s version support documentation</a> and the <a href=\":php_requirements\">Drupal PHP requirements</a> page for more information.','','none'),(9228,_binary 'It is recommended to upgrade to PHP version %recommended or higher for the best ongoing support.  See <a href=\"http://php.net/supported-versions.php\">PHP\'s version support documentation</a> and the <a href=\":php_requirements\">Drupal PHP requirements</a> page for more information.','','none'),(9229,_binary 'View information on the @lifecycle status of the theme @theme','','none'),(9230,_binary 'Drupal multisite is not supported by Package Manager.','','none'),(9231,_binary 'Xdebug is enabled, which may have a negative performance impact on Package Manager and any modules that use it.','','none'),(9232,_binary 'Allow reverse list','','none'),(9233,_binary 'Allow start index','','none'),(9234,_binary 'Allow the user to reverse an ordered list','','none'),(9235,_binary 'Allow the user to specify the start index of an ordered list','','none'),(9236,_binary 'Check <a href=\":handbook\">this handbook page</a> for details about compatibility issues of contrib modules.','','none'),(9237,_binary 'Source Editing should never allow self-XSS.','Validation','none'),(9238,_binary 'The following tag in the Source Editing \"Manually editable HTML tags\" field is a security risk: %dangerous_tag.','','none'),(9239,_binary 'Enabled Alignments','','none'),(9240,_binary 'Alignment type','','none'),(9241,_binary 'Allow view mode override','','none'),(9242,_binary 'These are the alignment types that will appear in the alignment dropdown.','','none'),(9243,_binary 'Allow the user to override the default view mode','','none'),(9244,_binary 'CKEditor 5 Media plugin in sync with filter settings','Validation','none'),(9245,_binary 'The CKEditor 5 \"%cke5_media_plugin_label\" plugin\'s \"%cke5_allow_view_mode_override_label\" setting should be in sync with the \"%filter_media_plugin_label\" filter\'s \"%filter_media_allowed_view_modes_label\" setting: when checked, two or more view modes must be allowed by the filter.','','none'),(9246,_binary 'You can choose to send email only if a security update is available, or to be notified about all newer versions. If there are updates available of Drupal core or any of your installed modules and themes, your site will always print a message on the <a href=\":status_report\">status report</a> page. If there is a security update, an error message will be printed on administration pages for users with <a href=\":update_permissions\">permission to view update notifications</a>.','','none'),(9247,_binary 'Congratulations and welcome to the Drupal community.','','11.2.5'),(9248,_binary 'The %plugin plugin needs another plugin to create <code>@non_creatable_tag</code>, for it to be able to create the following attributes: <code>@attributes_on_tag</code>. Enable a plugin that supports creating this tag. If none exists, you can configure the Source Editing plugin to support it.','','none'),(9249,_binary 'Olivero Color Scheme Settings','','none'),(9250,_binary 'These settings adjust the look and feel of the Olivero theme. Changing the color below will change the base hue, saturation, and lightness values the Olivero theme uses to determine its internal colors.','','none'),(9251,_binary 'Olivero Color Scheme','','none'),(9252,_binary 'Derivatives will be formed from this color.','','none'),(9253,_binary 'Base Primary Color','','none'),(9254,_binary '@fieldName has changed to @fieldValue','','none'),(9255,_binary 'Unable to uninstall the %module module because: @reason.','','none'),(9256,_binary 'Unable to install the %theme theme since it requires the %required_module module.','','none'),(9257,_binary 'If the <em>Source</em> button is available in the toolbar, users can click this button to disable the visual editor and edit the HTML source directly. After toggling back, the visual editor uses the HTML tags allowed via plugin configuration (and not explicity disallowed by filters) to format the text. Tags not enabled via plugin configuration will be stripped out of the HTML source when the user toggles back to the text editor.','','none'),(9258,_binary '@theme theme','','none'),(9259,_binary 'The <code>update_fetch_with_http_fallback</code> setting must be disabled.','','none'),(9260,_binary 'Resolve all issues below to continue the installation. For help configuring your database server, see the <a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/installing-drupal\">installation handbook</a>, or contact your hosting provider.','','none'),(9261,_binary 'Updating to Drupal @current_major is only supported from Drupal version @required_min_version or higher. If you are trying to update from an older version, first update to the latest version of Drupal @previous_major. (<a href=\":url\">Drupal upgrade guide</a>)','','none'),(9262,_binary 'Migrating an Existing Text Format to CKEditor 5','','none'),(9263,_binary 'When switching an existing text format to use CKEditor 5, an automatic process is initiated that helps text formats switching to CKEditor 5 from CKEditor 4 (or no text editor) to do so with minimal effort and zero data loss.','','none'),(9264,_binary 'This process is designed for there to be no data loss risk in switching to CKEditor 5. However some of your editor\'s functionality may not be 100% equivalent to what was available previously. In most cases, these changes are minimal. After the process completes, status and/or warning messages will summarize any changes that occurred, and more detailed information will be available in the site\'s logs.','','none'),(9265,_binary 'CKEditor 5 will attempt to enable plugins that provide equivalent toolbar items to those used prior to switching to CKEditor 5. All core CKEditor 4 plugins and many popular contrib plugins already have CKEditor 5 equivalents. In some cases, functionality that required contrib modules is now built into CKEditor 5. In instances where a plugin does not have an equivalent, no data loss will occur but elements previously provided via the plugin may need to be added manually as HTML via source editing.','','none'),(9266,_binary 'Additional migration considerations for text formats with restricted HTML','','none'),(9267,_binary 'The “Allowed HTML tags\" field in the “Limit allowed HTML tags and correct Faulty HTML\" filter is now read-only','','none'),(9268,_binary 'This field accurately represents the tags/attributes allowed by a text format, but the allowed tags are based on which plugins are enabled and how they are configured. For example, enabling the Underline plugin adds the &lt;u&gt; tag to “Allowed HTML tags\".','','none'),(9269,_binary 'The &lt;p&gt; and &lt;br &gt; tags will be automatically added to your text format.','','none'),(9270,_binary 'CKEditor 5 requires the &lt;p&gt; and &lt;br &gt; tags to achieve basic functionality. They will be automatically added to “Allowed HTML tags\" on formats that previously did not allow them.','','none'),(9271,_binary 'Tags/attributes that are not explicitly supported by any plugin are supported by Source Editing','','none'),(9272,_binary 'When a necessary tag/attribute is not directly supported by an available plugin, the \"Source Editing\" plugin is enabled. This plugin is typically used for by passing the CKEditor 5 UI and editing contents as HTML source. In the settings for Source Editing, tags/attributes that aren\'t available via other plugins are added to Source Editing\'s \"Manually editable HTML tags\" setting so they are supported by the text format.','','none'),(9273,_binary 'To maintain the capabilities of this text format, <a target=\"_blank\" href=\":ck_migration_url\">the CKEditor 5 migration</a> did the following:','','none'),(9274,_binary 'To maintain the capabilities of this text format, the CKEditor 5 migration did the following:','','none'),(9275,_binary 'Enabled these plugins: (%plugins).','','none'),(9276,_binary 'Added these tags/attributes to the Source Editing Plugin\'s <a target=\"_blank\" href=\":source_edit_url\">Manually editable HTML tags</a> setting: @tag_list','','none'),(9277,_binary 'Added these tags/attributes to the Source Editing Plugin\'s Manually editable HTML tags setting: @tag_list','','none'),(9278,_binary 'Additional details are available <a target=\"_blank\" href=\":dblog_url\">in your logs</a>.','','none'),(9279,_binary 'Additional details are available in your logs.','','none'),(9280,_binary 'Updating to CKEditor 5 added support for some previously unsupported tags/attributes.','','none'),(9281,_binary 'A plugin introduced support for the following:','','none'),(9282,_binary 'for','Ckeditor 5 tag list','none'),(9283,_binary 'The @tag tag was added because it is <a target=\"_blank\" href=\":fundamental_tag_link\">required by CKEditor 5</a>.The @tag tags were added because they are <a target=\"_blank\" href=\":fundamental_tag_link\">required by CKEditor 5</a>.','','none'),(9284,_binary 'The @tag tag was added because it is required by CKEditor 5.The @tag tags were added because they are required by CKEditor 5.','','none'),(9285,_binary 'The tag %tags;The tags %tags;','','none'),(9286,_binary 'This attribute: %attributes;These attributes: %attributes;','','none'),(9287,_binary 'The migration of %text_format to CKEditor 5 has been saved.','','none'),(9288,_binary 'Date range (Datetime range module): Stores time/date periods with a start and an end','','11.2.5'),(9289,_binary 'Find the view that you would like to edit, and click <em>Edit</em> from the dropdown button. Note that bulk operations work best in a view with a Page display, and a Table format.','','11.2.5'),(9290,_binary 'Note that anonymous users with this permission are able to edit any content created by any anonymous user.','','11.2.5'),(9291,_binary 'Note that anonymous users with this permission are able to delete any content created by any anonymous user.','','11.2.5'),(9292,_binary 'The fallback image style is typically the smallest size image you expect to appear in this space. The fallback image should only appear on a site if an error occurs.','','none'),(9293,_binary 'The %relationship_name relationship used in %handler_type %handler is not present in the %display_name display.','','none'),(9294,_binary 'Configure @type @current of @total: @item','','none'),(9295,_binary 'Heading Level','','none'),(9296,_binary 'Updates failed for the entity type %entity_type, for %entity_ids. Check the logs.','','none'),(9297,_binary 'Unable to update %entity_type %view due to error @message %function (line %line of %file). <pre>@backtrace_string</pre>','','none'),(9298,_binary 'Block content entity changed','Validation','none'),(9299,_binary 'Style label','','none'),(9300,_binary 'Style tag + classes','','none'),(9301,_binary 'A list of classes that will be provided in the \"Style\" dropdown. Enter one or more classes on each line in the format: element.classA.classB|Label. Example: h1.title|Title. Advanced example: h1.fancy.title|Fancy title.<br />These styles should be available in your theme\'s CSS file.','','none'),(9302,_binary 'Line @line-number does not contain a valid value. Enter a valid CSS selector containing one or more classes, followed by a pipe symbol and a label.Lines @line-numbers do not contain a valid value. Enter a valid CSS selector containing one or more classes, followed by a pipe symbol and a label.','','none'),(9303,_binary 'The following tag is missing the required attribute <code>@required_attribute_name</code>: <code>@provided_element</code>.','','none'),(9304,_binary 'The following tag does not have the minimum of @min_attribute_value_count allowed values for the required attribute <code>@required_attribute_name</code>: <code>@provided_element</code>.','','none'),(9305,_binary 'Styles can only be specified for already supported tags.','Validation','none'),(9306,_binary 'A style can only be specified for an HTML 5 tag. <code>@tag</code> is not an HTML5 tag.','','none'),(9307,_binary 'A style must only specify classes not supported by other plugins. The <code>@classes</code> classes on <code>@tag</code> are already supported by the enabled %plugin plugin.','','none'),(9308,_binary 'A style must only specify classes not supported by other plugins. The <code>@classes</code> classes on <code>@tag</code> are supported by the %plugin plugin. Remove this style and enable that plugin instead.','','none'),(9309,_binary 'Unique label in list','Validation','none'),(9310,_binary 'The label %label is not unique.','','none'),(9311,_binary 'The Text Editor module provides a framework that other modules (such as <a href=\":ckeditor5\">CKEditor5 module</a>) can use to provide toolbars and other functionality that allow users to format text more easily than typing HTML tags directly. For more information, see the <a href=\":documentation\">online documentation for the Text Editor module</a>.','','none'),(9312,_binary 'To search help, you will need to install the core Search module, configure a search page, and add a search block to the Help page or another administrative page. (A search page is provided automatically, and if you use the core Claro administrative theme, a help search block is shown on the main Help page.) Then users with search permissions, and permission to view help, will be able to search help. See the <a href=\":search_help\">Search module help page</a> for more information.','','none'),(9313,_binary 'A base theme is a theme that is not meant to be used directly on a site, but instead acts as a scaffolding for building other themes. The core Stable 9 theme is one example; other base themes can be downloaded from the <a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/project/project_theme\">Download &amp; Extend page on drupal.org</a>.','','11.2.5'),(9314,_binary 'The core Filter, Responsive Image, and Path modules provide settings and display options for entities and fields.','','11.2.5'),(9315,_binary 'A text editor is software (typically, a JavaScript library) that provides buttons and other command mechanisms to make editing HTML text easier. Some editors are called <em>visual</em> or <em>WYSIWYG (What You See Is What You Get)</em> editors; these editors hide the details of HTML from the user, and instead show formatted output on the screen. The core Text Editor module provides a framework for deploying text editors on your site. The core CKEditor 5 module provides CKEditor 5, which is a widely-used JavaScript text editor that creates clean and valid HTML; the module also enforces the HTML tag restrictions in the associated text format. Various contributed modules provide other editors; to install a new editor, besides installing the module, you may need to download the editor library from a third-party site.','','11.2.5'),(9316,_binary 'Select <em>CKEditor 5</em> as the <em>Text editor</em>, or another text editor that you have installed. The rest of these steps assume you selected <em>CKEditor 5</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9317,_binary 'Under <em>Toolbar configuration</em>, drag buttons between <em>Available buttons</em> and <em>Active toolbar</em>; only buttons in <em>Active toolbar</em> will be shown to the user. Focusing or hovering over a button will display a tooltip explaining what the button does.','','11.2.5'),(9318,_binary 'Drag buttons within <em>Active toolbar</em> to the desired order, and group buttons by dragging them between group identifiers; drag <em>a new group identifier</em> to the toolbar to add additional groups.','','11.2.5'),(9319,_binary 'If you add buttons that require configuration, the <em>CKEditor 5 plugin settings</em> section will be visible, and provide their respective configuration forms.','','11.2.5'),(9320,_binary 'Click the link for your administrative theme (such as the core Claro theme), near the top of the page, and verify that there is already a search block for help located in the Help region. If not, follow the steps in the related topic to place the <em>Search form</em> block in the Help region. When configuring the block, choose <em>Help</em> as the search page, and in the <em>Pages</em> tab under <em>Visibility</em>, enter <em>/admin/help</em> to make the search form only visible on the main <em>Help</em> page.','','11.2.5'),(9321,_binary 'Click the shortcut link to add the page to your shortcut list -- in the core Claro administrative theme, the link looks like a star, and is displayed next to the page title. However, if the page is already in your shortcut set, clicking the shortcut link will remove it from your shortcut set.','','11.2.5'),(9322,_binary 'The Shortcut module creates an add/remove link for each page on your site; the link lets you add or remove the current page from the currently-enabled set of shortcuts (if your theme displays it and you have permission to edit your shortcut set). The core Claro administration theme displays this link next to the page title, as a gray or yellow star. If you click on the gray star, you will add that page to your preferred set of shortcuts. If the page is already part of your shortcut set, the link will be a yellow star, and will allow you to remove the current page from your shortcut set.','','none'),(9323,_binary 'Grid - Responsive','','none'),(9324,_binary 'Maximum number of columns','','none'),(9325,_binary 'Minimum cell width','','none'),(9326,_binary 'The maximum number of columns that will be displayed within the grid.','','none'),(9327,_binary 'Minimum grid cell width','','none'),(9328,_binary 'The minimum width of the grid cells. If the grid container becomes narrow, the grid cells will reflow onto the next row as needed.','','none'),(9329,_binary 'Grid gutter spacing','','none'),(9330,_binary 'The spacing between the grid cells.','','none'),(9331,_binary 'The Drupal application\'s codebase must be writable in order to use Automatic Updates. This includes Drupal core, modules, themes and the Composer dependencies in the <code>vendor</code> directory. This makes Automatic Updates incompatible with some hosting platforms.','','none'),(9332,_binary 'Because Package Manager modifies the current site\'s code base, it is intentionally limited in certain ways to prevent unexpected changes to the live site:','','none'),(9333,_binary 'It does not support Drupal multi-site installations.','','none'),(9334,_binary 'It does not automatically perform version control operations, e.g., with Git. Site administrators are responsible for committing updates.','','none'),(9335,_binary 'It can only maintain one copy of the site at any given time. If a copy of the site already exists, another one cannot be created until the existing copy is destroyed.','','none'),(9336,_binary 'It associates the temporary copy of the site with the user or session that originally created it, and only that user or session can make changes to it.','','none'),(9337,_binary 'It does not allow modules to be uninstalled while syncing changes into live site.','','none'),(9338,_binary 'The new package @package will be installed in the directory @path, which already exists but is not managed by Composer.','','none'),(9339,_binary '@message See <a href=\":package-manager-help\">the help page</a> for information on how to resolve the problem.','','none'),(9340,_binary 'Staged changes failed to apply, and the site is in an indeterminate state. It is strongly recommended to restore the code and database from a backup.','','none'),(9341,_binary 'Post-apply tasks are running in the same request during which staged changes were applied to the active code base. This can result in unpredictable behavior.','','none'),(9342,_binary 'Failed to download remote thumbnail file due to \"%error\".','','none'),(9343,_binary 'Package Manager is not supported by your environment.','','none'),(9344,_binary 'CKEditor 5 plugin settings','','none'),(9345,_binary 'Enter a value like \"512\" (bytes), \"80 KB\" (kilobytes) or \"50 MB\" (megabytes) in order to restrict the allowed file size. If left empty the file sizes could be limited only by PHP\'s maximum post and file upload sizes (current limit <strong>%limit</strong>).','','none'),(9346,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>People</em> &gt; <em>@ban_link</em>','','none'),(9347,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; <em>@layout_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9348,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Development</em> &gt; <em>Configuration synchronization</em> &gt; <em>@export_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9349,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Development</em> &gt; <em>Configuration synchronization</em> &gt; <em>Export</em> &gt; <em>@single_export_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9350,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Development</em> &gt; <em>Configuration synchronization</em> &gt; <em>@import_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9351,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Development</em> &gt; <em>Configuration synchronization</em> &gt; <em>Import</em> &gt; <em>@single_import_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9352,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; <em>@contact_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9353,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>People</em> &gt; <em>@config_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9354,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>People</em> &gt; <em>@permission_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9355,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administration menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>System</em> &gt; <em>@cron_link</em>. Note the <em>Last run</em> time on the page.','','11.2.5'),(9356,_binary 'What are security advisories?','','11.2.5'),(9357,_binary 'A security advisory is a public announcement about a reported security problem in the core software. Contributed projects with a shield icon and \"Stable releases for this project are covered by the security advisory policy\" on their project page are also covered by Drupal\'s security advisory policy. Security advisories are managed by the <a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/drupal-security-team\">Drupal Security Team</a>.','','11.2.5'),(9358,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/drupal-security-team/security-advisory-process-and-permissions-policy\">Security advisory process and permissions policy</a>','','11.2.5'),(9359,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Content Authoring</em> &gt; <em>@overview_link</em>. The <em>Text editor</em> column in the table shows the text editor that is currently connected to each text format, if any.','','11.2.5'),(9360,_binary 'Navigate to the page for managing the entity sub-type you want to add the field to. For example, to add a field to a content type, in the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; <em>@content_types_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9361,_binary 'Navigate to the page for managing the entity type you want to add the field to. For example, to add a field to a content type, in the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; <em>@content_types_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9362,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Content Authoring</em> &gt; <em>@overview_link</em>. If you do not have the core Text Editor module installed, the menu link and page title will instead be <em>Text formats</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9363,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>@help_link</em>. Verify that the search block is visible, and try a search.','','11.2.5'),(9364,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Media</em> &gt; @styles_link.','','11.2.5'),(9365,_binary 'Navigate to the page for managing the entity type you want to add the field to. For example, to add a field to a content type, in the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; @content_types_link.','','none'),(9366,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Reports</em> &gt; <em>@translation_updates_link</em>. This report is only available if the core Update Status module is installed.','','11.2.5'),(9367,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; @media_link.','','none'),(9368,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; @content_types_link.','','11.2.5'),(9369,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administration menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; @structure_menu_link.','','11.2.5'),(9370,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administration menu, navigate <em>Structure</em> &gt; @structure_menu_link.','','11.2.5'),(9371,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Development</em> &gt; <em>@migrate_drupal_upgrade_link</em>.','','none'),(9372,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Media</em> &gt; <em>@styles_link</em>.','','none'),(9373,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Search and Metadata</em> &gt; <em>@search_settings_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9374,_binary 'Source connection','','none'),(9375,_binary '- User defined -','','none'),(9376,_binary 'Choose one of the keys from the $databases array or else select \"User defined\" and enter database credentials.','','none'),(9377,_binary 'The email address is not made public. It will only be used if you need to be contacted about your account or for opted-in notifications.','','none'),(9378,_binary 'Add HTML class','','none'),(9379,_binary 'Migration @id did not meet the requirements. @message','','none'),(9380,_binary 'Check the <a href=\"https://www.php.net/manual/en/image.installation.php\">PHP GD installation documentation</a> if you want to add support.','','none'),(9381,_binary '@unsupported<br>@ref','','none'),(9382,_binary 'The GD Library for PHP is enabled, but was compiled without support for functions used by the rotate and desaturate effects. It was probably compiled using the official GD libraries from the <a href=\"https://libgd.github.io/\">gdLibrary site</a> instead of the GD library bundled with PHP. You should recompile PHP --with-gd using the bundled GD library. See <a href=\"https://www.php.net/manual/book.image.php\">the PHP manual</a>.','','none'),(9383,_binary 'Supported image file format: %formats.Supported image file formats: %formats.','','none'),(9384,_binary 'Unsupported image file format: %formats.Unsupported image file formats: %formats.','','none'),(9385,_binary 'No blocks settings to update.','','none'),(9386,_binary '<a href=\":url\">@module</a>','','none'),(9387,_binary '<a href=\":url\">@theme</a>','','none'),(9388,_binary 'For more information read the <a href=\":url\">documentation on deprecated modules.</a>','','none'),(9389,_binary 'For more information read the <a href=\":url\">documentation on deprecated themes.</a>','','none'),(9390,_binary 'You must add the following contributed module and reload this page.You must add the following contributed modules and reload this page.','','none'),(9391,_binary 'Removed core moduleRemoved core modules','','none'),(9392,_binary 'This module is installed on your site but is no longer provided by Core.These modules are installed on your site but are no longer provided by Core.','','none'),(9393,_binary 'You must add the following contributed theme and reload this page.You must add the following contributed themes and reload this page.','','none'),(9394,_binary 'Removed core themeRemoved core themes','','none'),(9395,_binary 'This theme is installed on your site but is no longer provided by Core.These themes are installed on your site but are no longer provided by Core.','','none'),(9396,_binary 'API module providing functionality to stage package installs and updates with Composer.','','none'),(9397,_binary 'There is not enough disk space to create a stage directory.','','none'),(9398,_binary 'The stage directory has @stage_count instances of @stage_info_file as compared to @active_count in the active directory. This likely indicates that a duplicate extension was installed.','','none'),(9399,_binary 'The stage directory has @stage_count instances of @stage_info_file. This likely indicates that a duplicate extension was installed.','','none'),(9400,_binary 'The stage root directory will not able to be created at \"@dir\".','','none'),(9401,_binary 'The stage root directory \"@dir\" is not writable.','','none'),(9402,_binary 'You do not have permission to view @item_label.','','none'),(9403,_binary 'Removing media.','','none'),(9404,_binary 'These settings apply to the %field field everywhere it is used. Some also impact the way that data is stored and cannot be changed once data has been created.','','11.2.5'),(9405,_binary 'There is @count entity with @delta or more values in this field, so the allowed number of values cannot be set to @allowed.There are @count entities with @delta or more values in this field, so the allowed number of values cannot be set to @allowed.','','none'),(9406,_binary 'It only allows supported Composer plugins. If you have any, see <a href=\"#package-manager-faq-unsupported-composer-plugin\">What if it says I have unsupported Composer plugins in my codebase?</a>.','','none'),(9407,_binary 'What if it says I have unsupported Composer plugins in my codebase?','','none'),(9408,_binary 'It is possible to <em>trust</em> additional Composer plugins, but this requires significant expertise: understanding the code of that Composer plugin, what the effects on the file system are and how it affects the Package Manager module. Some Composer plugins could result in a broken site!','','none'),(9409,_binary 'What if it says <code>cweagans/composer-patches</code> cannot be installed/removed?','','none'),(9410,_binary 'To install it:','','none'),(9411,_binary 'To remove it:','','none'),(9412,_binary 'What if it says <code>cweagans/composer-patches</code> must be a root dependency?','','none'),(9413,_binary 'If <code>cweagans/composer-patches</code> is installed, it must be defined as a dependency of the main project (i.e., it must be listed in the <code>require</code> or <code>require-dev</code> section of <code>composer.json</code>). You can run the following command in your site root to add it as a dependency of the main project:','','none'),(9414,_binary 'Additional trusted composer plugins','','none'),(9415,_binary 'Cannot claim the stage because no stage has been created.','','none'),(9416,_binary 'Cannot claim the stage because it is not owned by the current user or session.','','none'),(9417,_binary 'Cannot claim the stage because the current lock does not match the stored lock.','','none'),(9418,_binary 'This operation has already been applied.','','none'),(9419,_binary 'This operation was canceled by another user.','','none'),(9420,_binary 'This operation was already canceled.','','none'),(9421,_binary '<code>@package_name</code>\'s requested version @package_version is less stable (@package_stability) than the minimum stability (@minimum_stability) required in @file.','','none'),(9422,_binary 'It cannot be installed by Package Manager.','','none'),(9423,_binary 'It cannot be removed by Package Manager.','','none'),(9424,_binary 'It must be a root dependency.','','none'),(9425,_binary 'The <code>composer-exit-on-patch-failure</code> key is not set to <code>true</code> in the <code>extra</code> section of <code>composer.json</code>.','','none'),(9426,_binary 'Problems detected related to the Composer plugin <code>@plugin</code>.','','none'),(9427,_binary '@message See <a href=\":url\">the help page</a> for information on how to resolve the problem.','','none'),(9428,_binary 'Unable to determine Composer <code>allow-plugins</code> setting.','','none'),(9429,_binary 'All composer plugins are allowed because <code>config.allow-plugins</code> is configured to <code>true</code>. This is an unacceptable security risk.','','none'),(9430,_binary 'j M Y - H:i','PHP date format','11.2.5'),(9431,_binary 'The CKEditor 5 migration enabled the following plugins to support tags that are allowed by the %text_format text format: %enabling_message_content. The text format must be saved to make these changes active.','','none'),(9432,_binary 'The following tags were permitted by the %text_format text format\'s filter configuration, but no plugin was available that supports them. To ensure the tags remain supported by this text format, the following were added to the Source Editing plugin\'s <em>Manually editable HTML tags</em>: @unsupported_string. The text format must be saved to make these changes active.','','none'),(9433,_binary 'The CKEditor 5 migration process enabled the following plugins to support specific attributes that are allowed by the %text_format text format: %enabled_for_attributes_message_content.','','none'),(9434,_binary 'As part of migrating to CKEditor 5, it was found that the %text_format text format\'s HTML filters includes plugins that support the following tags, but not some of their attributes. To ensure these attributes remain supported, the following were added to the Source Editing plugin\'s <em>Manually editable HTML tags</em>: @missing_attributes. The text format must be saved to make these changes active.','','none'),(9435,_binary 'As part of migrating the %text_format text format to CKEditor 5, the following tag(s) were added to <em>Limit allowed HTML tags and correct faulty HTML</em>, because they are needed to provide fundamental CKEditor 5 functionality : @missing_tags. The text format must be saved to make these changes active.','','none'),(9436,_binary 'C#','','11.2.5'),(9437,_binary 'C++','','11.2.5'),(9438,_binary 'TypeScript','','11.2.5'),(9439,_binary 'Tooltip date format','','none'),(9440,_binary 'Tooltip custom date format','','none'),(9441,_binary 'Time difference','','none'),(9442,_binary 'Show as time difference','','none'),(9443,_binary 'Time units','','none'),(9444,_binary 'A worker for @queue queue suspended further processing of the queue.','','none'),(9445,_binary 'Updates failed for the entity type %entity_type, for %entity_ids. <a href=\":url\">Check the logs</a>.','','none'),(9446,_binary 'Config exists','Validation','none'),(9447,_binary 'The \'@name\' config does not exist.','','none'),(9448,_binary 'Required config dependency types','Validation','none'),(9449,_binary 'This @entity_type requires a @dependency_type.','','none'),(9450,_binary 'Revision of %title','','none'),(9451,_binary '<em>Current revision</em>','','none'),(9452,_binary 'Revision of @type %title has been deleted.','','none'),(9453,_binary '@type %title has been reverted.','','none'),(9454,_binary 'Extension exists','Validation','none'),(9455,_binary 'Module \'@name\' is not installed.','','none'),(9456,_binary 'Theme \'@name\' is not installed.','','none'),(9457,_binary 'Valid extension name','Validation','none'),(9458,_binary 'Render the referenced entity.','','none'),(9459,_binary 'Display as a time difference (e.g. \'6 months ago\')','','none'),(9460,_binary 'Use the <code>@interval</code> placeholder to represent the formatted time difference interval. E.g. <code>@interval hence</code> will be displayed as <em>2 hours 5 minutes hence</em>.','','none'),(9461,_binary 'Use the <code>@interval</code> placeholder to represent the formatted time difference interval. E.g. <code>@interval ago</code> will be displayed as <em>2 hours 5 minutes ago</em>.','','none'),(9462,_binary 'How many time units will be used in formatting the time difference. For example, if \'1\' is selected then the displayed time difference will only contain a single time unit such as \'2 years\' or \'5 minutes\' never \'2 years 3 months\' or \'5 minutes 8 seconds\'.','','none'),(9463,_binary 'How often to refresh the displayed time difference. The time difference is refreshed on client-side, by JavaScript, without reloading the page.','','none'),(9464,_binary 'Fallback configuration','','none'),(9465,_binary 'The configuration below is used as a fallback when JavaScript is not available on the page.','','none'),(9466,_binary 'Select the date format to be used for the title and displayed on mouse hover.','','none'),(9467,_binary '- No tooltip -','','none'),(9468,_binary 'Displayed as a time difference','','none'),(9469,_binary 'Refresh every @interval','','none'),(9470,_binary 'Disabled JavaScript format: @date_format','','none'),(9471,_binary 'Tooltip date format: @date_format','','none'),(9472,_binary 'Reference type: @entity_type','','none'),(9473,_binary 'The submitted value %choice in the %name element is not allowed.','','none'),(9474,_binary 'The image toolkit \'@toolkit\' failed processing \'@operation\' for image \'@image\'. Reported error: @class - @message','','none'),(9475,_binary 'Plugin exists','Validation','none'),(9476,_binary 'The \'@plugin_id\' plugin does not exist.','','none'),(9477,_binary 'The \'@plugin_id\' plugin must implement or extend @interface.','','none'),(9478,_binary 'Optimized assets files','','none'),(9479,_binary 'Public local optimized assets files served by the webserver.','','none'),(9480,_binary 'Valid mapping keys','Validation','none'),(9481,_binary '\'@key\' is not a supported key.','','none'),(9482,_binary 'Numerically indexed arrays are not allowed.','','none'),(9483,_binary 'Edit machine name','','11.2.5'),(9484,_binary 'The Announcements module displays announcements from the Drupal community. For more information, see the <a href=\":documentation\">online documentation for the Announcements module</a>.','','none'),(9485,_binary 'Accessing announcements','','none'),(9486,_binary 'Displays announcements from the Drupal community.','','11.2.5'),(9487,_binary 'View official announcements related to Drupal','','11.2.5'),(9488,_binary 'Community announcements','','none'),(9489,_binary 'Announcements Settings','','none'),(9490,_binary 'Cache announcements for max-age seconds.','','none'),(9491,_binary 'Cron interval for fetching announcements in seconds.','','none'),(9492,_binary 'Number of announcements that will be displayed.','','none'),(9493,_binary 'The feed format is not valid.','','none'),(9494,_binary 'An error occurred while parsing the announcements feed, check the logs for more information.','','none'),(9495,_binary 'No announcements available','','none'),(9496,_binary 'Allows banning visits from specific IP addresses.','','none'),(9497,_binary 'Provides an HTTP Basic authentication provider.','','none'),(9498,_binary 'Adding content blocks','','none'),(9499,_binary 'You can add content blocks, if the <em>Block Content</em> module is installed. For more information, see the <a href=\":blockcontent-help\">Block Content help page</a>.','','none'),(9500,_binary 'Allows users to configure blocks (containing content, forms, etc.) and to place them in the regions of a theme.','','none'),(9501,_binary 'The Block Content module allows you to create and manage custom <em>block types</em> and <em>content-containing blocks</em>. For more information, see the <a href=\":online-help\">online documentation for the Block Content module</a>.','','none'),(9502,_binary 'Creating and managing block types','','none'),(9503,_binary 'Users with the <em>Administer blocks</em> permission can create and edit block types with fields and display settings, from the <a href=\":types\">Block types</a> page under the Structure menu. For more information about managing fields and display settings, see the <a href=\":field-ui\">Field UI module help</a> and <a href=\":field\">Field module help</a>.','','none'),(9504,_binary 'Creating content blocks','','none'),(9505,_binary 'Users with the <em>Administer blocks</em> permission can create, edit, and delete content blocks of each defined block type, from the <a href=\":block-library\">Content blocks page</a>. After creating a block, place it in a region from the <a href=\":blocks\">Block layout page</a>, just like blocks provided by other modules.','','none'),(9506,_binary 'Allows the creation of content blocks and block types.','','none'),(9507,_binary 'Add content block','','11.2.5'),(9508,_binary 'Create and manage fields, forms, and display settings for your content blocks.','','11.2.5'),(9509,_binary 'Access the Content blocks overview page','','11.2.5'),(9510,_binary 'Get an overview of all content blocks.','','11.2.5'),(9511,_binary 'Maintain the block types of block content available and the fields that are associated with those types.','','11.2.5'),(9512,_binary 'View, edit and delete all block content regardless of permission restrictions.','','11.2.5'),(9513,_binary 'Edit content block %label','','11.2.5'),(9514,_binary '%type_name: Create new content block','','11.2.5'),(9515,_binary '%type_name: Edit content block','','11.2.5'),(9516,_binary '%type_name: Delete content block','','11.2.5'),(9517,_binary '%type_name: View content block history pages','','11.2.5'),(9518,_binary '%type_name: Revert content block revisions','','11.2.5'),(9519,_binary '%type_name: Delete content block revisions','','11.2.5'),(9520,_binary 'Edit %label block type','','none'),(9521,_binary 'Block type %label has been updated.','','none'),(9522,_binary 'Block type %label has been added.','','11.2.5'),(9523,_binary 'Add %type content block','','11.2.5'),(9524,_binary 'Content block ID','','11.2.5'),(9525,_binary 'The content block ID.','','none'),(9526,_binary 'The content block UUID.','','none'),(9527,_binary 'The content block language code.','','11.2.5'),(9528,_binary 'The time that the content block was last edited.','','none'),(9529,_binary 'content blocks','','none'),(9530,_binary 'block type','','none'),(9531,_binary 'block types','','none'),(9532,_binary '%label is used by 1 content block on your site. You can not remove this block type until you have removed all of the %label blocks.%label is used by @count content blocks on your site. You may not remove %label until you have removed all of the %label content blocks.','','none'),(9533,_binary 'Block with uuid %uuid does not exist. <a href=\":url\">Add content block</a>.','','none'),(9534,_binary 'Input format of the content block/box content.','','none'),(9535,_binary 'Add a <a href=\":url\">content block</a>.','','none'),(9536,_binary 'Provides the CKEditor 5 rich text editor.','','none'),(9537,_binary 'Language label','','none'),(9538,_binary 'Images can only be uploaded.','','none'),(9539,_binary 'Images can only be added by URL.','','none'),(9540,_binary 'A list of programming languages that will be provided in the \"Code Block\" dropdown. Enter one value per line, in the format key|label. Example: php|PHP.','','none'),(9541,_binary 'Line @line-number does not contain a valid value. Enter a valid language key followed by a pipe symbol and a label.Lines @line-numbers do not contain a valid value. Enter a valid language key followed by a pipe symbol and a label.','','none'),(9542,_binary 'Allows importing and exporting configuration changes.','','none'),(9543,_binary 'Content Moderation allows you to apply <a href=\":workflows\">Workflows</a> to content, content blocks, and other <a href=\":field_help\" title=\"Field module help, with background on content entities\">content entities</a>, to provide more fine-grained publishing options. For example, a Basic page might have states such as Draft and Published, with allowed transitions such as Draft to Published (making the current revision \"live\"), and Published to Draft (making a new draft revision of published content).','','none'),(9544,_binary 'Provides additional publication states that can be used by other modules to moderate content.','','none'),(9545,_binary 'The Content Translation module allows you to translate content, comments, content blocks, taxonomy terms, users and other <a href=\":field_help\" title=\"Field module help, with background on content entities\">content entities</a>. Together with the modules <a href=\":language\">Language</a>, <a href=\":config-trans\">Configuration Translation</a>, and <a href=\":locale\">Interface Translation</a>, it allows you to build multilingual websites. For more information, see the <a href=\":translation-entity\">online documentation for the Content Translation module</a>.','','none'),(9546,_binary 'Defines field types for storing dates and times.','','none'),(9547,_binary 'When enabled, images can only be uploaded. When disabled, images can only be added by URL.','','none'),(9548,_binary 'The Text Editor module provides a framework for managing editors. To use it, you also need to install a text editor. This can either be the core <a href=\":ckeditor5\">CKEditor5 module</a>, which can be installed on the <a href=\":extend\">Extend page</a>, or a contributed module for any other text editor. When installing a contributed text editor module, be sure to check the installation instructions, because you will most likely need to download an external library as well as the Drupal module.','','none'),(9549,_binary 'Provides a framework to associate text editors (like WYSIWYGs) and toolbars with text formats.','','none'),(9550,_binary 'Text editors','','none'),(9551,_binary 'Ensures that the latest versions of images uploaded via a Text Editor are displayed, along with their dimensions.','','none'),(9552,_binary 'The website\'s content and configuration is managed using <em>entities</em>, which are grouped into <em>entity types</em>. <em>Content entity types</em> are the entity types for site content (such as the main site content, comments, content blocks, taxonomy terms, and user accounts). <em>Configuration entity types</em> are used to store configuration information for your site, such as individual views in the Views module, and settings for your main site content types.','','none'),(9553,_binary 'Provides the capabilities to add fields to entities.','','none'),(9554,_binary 'Once you have created a field, you can use it again in other sub-types of the same entity type. For instance, if you create a field for the article content type, you can also use it for the page content type, but you cannot use it for content blocks or taxonomy terms. If there are fields available for re-use, after clicking <em>Add field</em> from the <em>Manage fields</em> page, you will see a list of available fields for re-use. After selecting a field for re-use, you can configure the sub-type-level settings.','','none'),(9555,_binary 'Provide a pre-filled value for the editing form.','','11.2.5'),(9556,_binary 'You need to select a field type.','','none'),(9557,_binary 'You can re-use a field from other sub-types of the same entity type. Re-using a field creates another usage of the same field storage.','','none'),(9558,_binary 'Filter by field or field type','','none'),(9559,_binary 'Used in: @list','','none'),(9560,_binary 'Re-use','','none'),(9561,_binary 'Reuse @field_name','','none'),(9562,_binary 'There was a problem reusing field %label: @message','','none'),(9563,_binary 'Single valueMultiple values: @cardinality','','none'),(9564,_binary 'Create a new field','','11.2.5'),(9565,_binary 'Provides a field type for files and defines a \"managed_file\" Form API element.','','none'),(9566,_binary 'Filters text content in preparation for display.','','none'),(9567,_binary 'Lazy load images','','none'),(9568,_binary 'Instruct browsers to lazy load images if dimensions are specified. Use in conjunction with and place after the \'Track images uploaded via a Text Editor\' filter that adds image dimensions required for lazy loading. Results can be overridden by <code>&lt;img loading=&quot;eager&quot;&gt;</code>.','','none'),(9569,_binary 'Generates help pages and provides a Help block with page-level help.','','none'),(9570,_binary 'What are content blocks?','','11.2.5'),(9571,_binary 'Content blocks are blocks whose content you can edit. You can define one or more <em>block types</em>, and attach fields to each block type. Content blocks can be placed just like blocks provided by other modules.','','11.2.5'),(9572,_binary 'Overview for managing blocks','','11.2.5'),(9573,_binary 'The <em>Block</em> module allows you to place blocks in regions of your installed themes, and configure block settings. The <em>Block Content</em> module allows you to manage block types and content blocks. See the related topics listed below for specific tasks.','','11.2.5'),(9574,_binary 'Creating a content block','','11.2.5'),(9575,_binary 'Create a content block, which can later be placed on the site.','','11.2.5'),(9576,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Content</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9577,_binary 'Open the @library_link tab.','','11.2.5'),(9578,_binary 'Click <em>Add content block</em>. If you have more than one block type defined on your site, click the name of the type you want to create.','','11.2.5'),(9579,_binary 'Defining a block type','','11.2.5'),(9580,_binary 'Define a block type and its fields.','','11.2.5'),(9581,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; <em>@types_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9582,_binary 'Click  <em>Add block type</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9583,_binary 'A comment is a piece of content, typically posted by a website visitor, which provides discussion or commentary on other content like blog posts and news articles. Comments are a type of content entity, and can have fields that store text, HTML markup, and other data. Comments are attached to other content entities via Comment fields. See @content_structure_topic for more about content entities and fields.','','11.2.5'),(9584,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Region and language</em> &gt; <em>@config_translation_link</em>.','','none'),(9585,_binary 'Both personal and site-wide contact forms will always have <em>Subject</em> and <em>Message</em> fields. You can add additional fields for users to fill out if desired. Note that if you want to display other content on a form page, such as text or images, you can use a content block.','','11.2.5'),(9586,_binary 'Users with <em>content moderation permissions</em> can change workflow states. There are separate permissions for each transition. See Permissions &gt; <em>@content_moderation_permissions_link</em> to configure content moderation permissions.','','none'),(9587,_binary 'Find the entity that you want to moderate in either the content moderation view page, if you created one, or the appropriate administrative page for managing that type of entity (such as the administration page for content items; see @content_link).','','none'),(9588,_binary 'Users with <em>workflows permissions</em> (typically administrators) can configure workflows. See Permissions &gt; <em>@workflows_permissions_link</em> to configure workflows permissions.','','none'),(9589,_binary 'To implement your plan, in the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Workflow</em> &gt; <em>@workflows_link</em>. A list of workflows is shown, including the default workflow <em>Editorial</em> that you can adapt.','','none'),(9590,_binary 'Under <em>This workflow applies to:</em>, find the entity type that you want this workflow to apply to, such as Content revisions, Content block revisions, or Taxonomy term revisions. Click <em>Select</em>.','','none'),(9591,_binary 'Follow the steps in @user_permissions_topic to assign permissions for each transition to roles. The permissions are listed under the <em>@content_moderation_permissions_link</em> section; there is one permission for each transition in each workflow.','','none'),(9592,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Region and language</em> &gt; <em>@translation_settings_link</em>.','','none'),(9593,_binary 'A <em>content entity</em> (or more commonly, <em>entity</em>) is an item of content data, which can consist of text, HTML markup, images, attached files, and other data. Content entities are grouped into <em>entity types</em>, which have different purposes and are displayed in very different ways on the site. Most entity types are also divided into <em>entity sub-types</em>, which are divisions within an entity type to allow for smaller variations in how the entities are used and displayed. For example, the <em>Content item</em> entity type that stores page-level content is divided into <em>content type</em> sub-types; the <em>Content block</em> entity type has <em>block types</em>; but the <em>User</em> entity type (for user profile information) does not have sub-types.','','11.2.5'),(9594,_binary 'The core Node, Comment, Content Block, Custom Menu Links, User, File, Image, Media, Taxonomy, and Contact modules all provide content entity types.','','11.2.5'),(9595,_binary 'Depending on the core and contributed modules that you currently have installed on your site, the related topics below and other topics listed on the main help page (see @help_link) will help you with tasks related to content structure.','','11.2.5'),(9596,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Region and language</em> &gt; @languages_link.','','11.2.5'),(9597,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Region and language</em> &gt; <em>Languages</em> &gt; @detection_link.','','11.2.5'),(9598,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Region and language</em> &gt; <em>User interface translation</em> &gt; @import_link.','','11.2.5'),(9599,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Region and language</em> &gt; @translate_link.','','11.2.5'),(9600,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Region and language</em> &gt; @language_link.','','11.2.5'),(9601,_binary 'When users visit the main search page (see @search_link), they will see the configured search pages that they have access to. Each search page has a search form on it, and the page will display search results after the user enters keywords into the form and clicks the search button.','','11.2.5'),(9602,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Development</em> &gt; <em>@performance_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9603,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>System</em> &gt; <em>@information_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9604,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Region and language</em> &gt; <em>@regional_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9605,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Region and language</em> &gt; <em>@datetime_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9606,_binary 'In the <em>Error pages</em> section, enter the URL for your 403/404 pages, starting after the site home page URL. For example, if your site URL is <em>https://example.com</em> and your 404 page is <em>https://example.com/not-found</em>, you would enter <em>/not-found</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9607,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Development</em> &gt; <em>@log_settings_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9608,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Development</em> &gt; <em>@maintenance_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9609,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>@extend_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9610,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Extend</em> &gt; <em>@uninstall_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9611,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Reports</em> &gt; <em>@status_link</em> to see a report that summarizes the health and status of your site. If there are any warnings or errors, you will need to fix them. Take note of any upcoming highly critical security releases that may impact your site.','','11.2.5'),(9612,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>@themes_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9613,_binary 'Taxonomy reference fields can be added to any entity, such as user accounts, content blocks, or regular content items. If you use them to classify regular content items, your site will automatically be set up with taxonomy listing pages for each term; each of these pages lists all of the content items that are classified with that term.','','11.2.5'),(9614,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>@people_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9615,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>People</em> &gt; <em>@roles_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9616,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>People</em> &gt; <em>@permissions_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9617,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>People</em> &gt; <em>@account_settings_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9618,_binary 'Views using a table display format can include a bulk operations form, which allows users with sufficient permission to select one or more items from the view and apply an administrative action to them. The bulk actions available are specific to the base data type of the view; for example, a view of content items could support bulk publishing and unpublishing actions. If you have the core Actions UI module installed, see the related topic \"Configuring actions\" for more about actions.','','11.2.5'),(9619,_binary 'If you are not already editing your view, in the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; <em>@views_link</em>. Find the view you want to edit, and click its <em>Edit</em> link.','','11.2.5'),(9620,_binary 'Add one or more existing actions as bulk operations to an existing table-style view. If you have the core Actions UI module installed, see the related topic \"Configuring actions\" for more information about actions.','','11.2.5'),(9621,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Structure</em> &gt; <em>@views_link</em>.','','11.2.5'),(9622,_binary 'Records which content users have viewed and marks it as new or updated.','','none'),(9623,_binary 'Layout Builder allows you to use layouts to customize how content, content blocks, and other <a href=\":field_help\" title=\"Field module help, with background on content entities\">content entities</a> are displayed.','','none'),(9624,_binary 'Create and edit content blocks','','none'),(9625,_binary 'Add a new content block','','none'),(9626,_binary 'Provides a field type for internal and external URLs.','','none'),(9627,_binary 'Updated default configuration to %langcode','','11.2.5'),(9628,_binary 'Allows users to translate interface text and to switch between interface languages.','','none'),(9629,_binary 'oEmbed loading settings','','none'),(9630,_binary 'oEmbed loading','','none'),(9631,_binary 'Lazy render oEmbed with native loading attribute (<em>loading=\"lazy\"</em>). This improves performance by allowing browsers to lazily load assets.','','none'),(9632,_binary 'oEmbed loading attribute','','none'),(9633,_binary 'Select the loading attribute for oEmbed. <a href=\":link\">Learn more about the loading attribute for oEmbed.</a>','','none'),(9634,_binary 'Delays loading the resource until that section of the page is visible in the browser. When in doubt, lazy loading is recommended.','','none'),(9635,_binary 'Force browsers to download a resource as soon as possible. This is the browser default for legacy reasons. Only use this option when the resource is always expected to render.','','none'),(9636,_binary 'Loading attribute: @attribute','','none'),(9637,_binary 'Content of this type can be placed in the selected menus.','','none'),(9638,_binary 'Provides a user interface for managing menus.','','none'),(9639,_binary 'Provides a framework for migrating data to Drupal.','','none'),(9640,_binary 'Provides a framework to migrate data from previous versions of Drupal into the site.','','none'),(9641,_binary 'This is not supported by Drupal.','','none'),(9642,_binary 'The recommended level for Drupal is \"READ COMMITTED\".','','none'),(9643,_binary 'For this to work correctly, all tables must have a primary key. The following table(s) do not have a primary key: @tables.','','none'),(9644,_binary 'See the <a href=\":performance_doc\">setting MySQL transaction isolation level</a> page for more information.','','11.2.5'),(9645,_binary 'Transaction isolation level','','11.2.5'),(9646,_binary 'Provides the MySQL database driver.','','none'),(9647,_binary 'READ COMMITTED','','none'),(9648,_binary 'REPEATABLE READ','','none'),(9649,_binary 'Use database default','','none'),(9650,_binary 'The recommended database transaction level for Drupal is \"READ COMMITTED\". For more information, see the <a href=\":performance_doc\">setting MySQL transaction isolation level</a> page.','','none'),(9651,_binary 'Manages the creation, configuration, and display of the main site content.','','none'),(9652,_binary 'Defines field types with select lists, checkboxes, and radio buttons to select values from fixed lists of options.','','none'),(9653,_binary 'Allows users to create custom URLs for existing paths on the site.','','none'),(9654,_binary 'Provides the PostgreSQL database driver.','','none'),(9655,_binary 'Password Compatibility','','none'),(9656,_binary 'The breakpoint group typically only needs a single breakpoint with an empty media query in order to do <em>viewport sizing.</em> Multiple breakpoints are used for changing the crop or aspect ratio of images at different viewport sizes, which is often referred to as <em>art direction.</em> A new breakpoint group should be created for each aspect ratio to avoid content shift. Once you select a breakpoint group, you can choose which breakpoints to use for the responsive image style. By default, the option <em>do not use this breakpoint</em> is selected for each breakpoint. See the <a href=\":breakpoint_help\">help page of the Breakpoint module</a> for more information.','','none'),(9657,_binary 'While you have the option to provide only one image style per breakpoint, the sizes attribute allows you to provide more options to browsers as to which image file it can display. If using sizes field and art direction, all selected image styles should use the same aspect ratio to avoid content shifting. Breakpoints are defined in the configuration files of the theme.','','none'),(9658,_binary 'The sizes attribute paired with the srcset attribute provides information on how much space these images take up within the viewport at different browser breakpoints, but the aspect ratios should remain the same across those breakpoints. Once the sizes option is selected, you can let the browser know the size of this image in relation to the site layout, using the <em>Sizes</em> field. For a hero image that always fills the entire screen, you could simply enter 100vw, which means 100% of the viewport width. For an image that fills 90% of the screen for small viewports, but only fills 40% of the screen when the viewport is larger than 40em (typically 640px), you could enter \"(min-width: 40em) 40vw, 90vw\" in the Sizes field. The last item in the comma-separated list is the smallest viewport size: other items in the comma-separated list should have a media condition paired with an image width. <em>Media conditions</em> are similar to a media query, often a min-width paired with a viewport width using em or px units: e.g. (min-width: 640px) or (min-width: 40em). This is paired with the <em>image width</em> at that viewport size using px, em or vw units. The vw unit is viewport width and is used instead of a percentage because the percentage always refers to the width of the entire viewport.','','none'),(9659,_binary 'Provides functionality to output responsive images using the HTML5 picture tag.','','none'),(9660,_binary 'Select the image style you wish to use as the style when a browser does not support responsive images.','','none'),(9661,_binary 'Lazy render images with native image loading attribute (<em>loading=\"lazy\"</em>). This improves performance by allowing browsers to lazily load images. See <a href=\"@url\">Lazy loading</a>.','','none'),(9662,_binary 'Lazy','','none'),(9663,_binary 'Eager','','none'),(9664,_binary 'Lazy loading attribute','','none'),(9665,_binary 'Select the lazy loading attribute for images. <a href=\":link\">Learn more.</a>','','none'),(9666,_binary 'In order to use REST on a website, you need to install modules that provide serialization and authentication services. You can use the Core module <a href=\":serialization\">serialization</a> for serialization and <a href=\":basic_auth\">HTTP Basic Authentication</a> for authentication, or install a contributed or custom module.','','none'),(9667,_binary 'Provides a framework for exposing REST resources.','','none'),(9668,_binary 'Allows discovery and rendering of self-contained UI components.','','none'),(9669,_binary 'Provides a service for converting data to and from formats such as JSON and XML.','','none'),(9670,_binary 'Allows users to create sets of shortcuts within the site.','','none'),(9671,_binary 'Provides the SQLite database driver.','','none'),(9672,_binary 'Logs events to the web server\'s system log.','','none'),(9673,_binary 'The base URL of the site, currently: @base_url','','none'),(9674,_binary 'The base path of the site, currently: @base_path','','none'),(9675,_binary 'The URL of the site\'s front page with the language prefix, if it exists.','','none'),(9676,_binary 'Obsolete extensions found: %extensions. Obsolete extensions are provided only so that they can be uninstalled cleanly. You should immediately <a href=\":uninstall_url\">uninstall these extensions</a> since they may be removed in a future release.','','none'),(9677,_binary 'PHP APCu available caching','','11.2.5'),(9678,_binary 'APCu is using over 90% of its allotted memory (@apcu_actual_size). To improve APCu performance, consider increasing this limit.','','none'),(9679,_binary 'APCu is using over 75% of its allotted memory (@apcu_actual_size). To improve APCu performance, consider increasing this limit.','','none'),(9680,_binary 'SameSite cookie attribute','','11.2.5'),(9681,_binary 'This attribute should be explicitly set to Lax, Strict or None. If set to None then the request must be made via HTTPS. See <a href=\":url\" target=\"_blank\">PHP documentation</a>','','none'),(9682,_binary 'Provides user interfaces for core systems.','','none'),(9683,_binary 'Region and language','','11.2.5'),(9684,_binary 'Menu Linkset Settings','','11.2.5'),(9685,_binary 'Enable or disable the menu linkset endpoint','','11.2.5'),(9686,_binary 'System Feature Flags','','none'),(9687,_binary 'Enable the menu linkset endpoint','','none'),(9688,_binary 'Use this utility to update your database whenever a module, theme, or the core software is updated.','','none'),(9689,_binary 'Update your files (as described in the handbook page linked above).','','none'),(9690,_binary 'The phpinfo() function is disabled. For more information, visit the <a href=\":phpinfo\">Enabling and disabling phpinfo()</a> handbook page.','','none'),(9691,_binary 'Optimized assets file system path','','none'),(9692,_binary 'A local file system path where optimized assets files will be stored. This directory must exist and be writable by Drupal. This directory must be relative to the Drupal installation directory and be accessible over the web. This must be changed in settings.php','','none'),(9693,_binary 'See the <a href=\"@docs-link\">decoupled menus documentation</a> for more information.','','none'),(9694,_binary '<strong class=\"error\">Set up the <a href=\":file-system\">optimized assets file system path</a> to make these optimizations available.</strong>','','none'),(9695,_binary 'Specify a relative URL to display as the front page.','','none'),(9696,_binary 'The path %path requires a leading forward slash when used with the Pages setting.','','none'),(9697,_binary 'The image toolkit \'@toolkit\' can not process image \'@image\'.','','none'),(9698,_binary 'The image toolkit \'@toolkit\' failed loading image \'@image\'. Reported error: @class - @message','','none'),(9699,_binary 'The image toolkit \'@toolkit\' failed saving image \'@image\'. Reported error: @class - @message','','none'),(9700,_binary 'The raw vocabulary ID.','','none'),(9701,_binary 'Defines field types for short and long text with optional summaries.','','none'),(9702,_binary 'Allowed text formats','','11.2.5'),(9703,_binary 'The selected text format is not allowed.','','none'),(9704,_binary 'Select the allowed text formats. If no formats are selected, all available text formats will be displayed to the user.','','11.2.5'),(9705,_binary 'Text editors may override this setting.','','none'),(9706,_binary 'Provides an administration toolbar to display links provided by modules.','','none'),(9707,_binary 'Regularly review <a href=\":updates\">available updates</a> and update as required to maintain a secure and current site. Always run the <a href=\":update-php\">update script</a> each time you update software.','','none'),(9708,_binary 'Permissions let you control what users can do and see on your site. You can define a specific set of permissions for each role. (See the <a href=\":role\">Roles</a> page to create a role.) Any permissions granted to the Authenticated user role will be given to any user who is logged in to your site. On the <a href=\":settings\">Role settings</a> page, you can make any role into an Administrator role for the site, meaning that role will be granted all permissions. You should be careful to ensure that only trusted users are given this access and level of control of your site.','','none'),(9709,_binary 'Allows users to register and log in, and manages user roles and permissions.','','none'),(9710,_binary 'This role will be automatically granted all permissions.','','none'),(9711,_binary 'Provides a framework to fetch information from the database and to display it in different formats.','','none'),(9712,_binary 'Use the administration theme when rendering the view page','','none'),(9713,_binary 'Yes (admin path)','','none'),(9714,_binary 'Use the administration theme when rendering this display.','','none'),(9715,_binary 'Use the administration theme','','none'),(9716,_binary 'Paths starting with \"@admin\" always use the administration theme.','','none'),(9717,_binary 'No %title option selected.','','none'),(9718,_binary 'The view %id failed to load an entity of type %entity_type at row %index for field %field','','none'),(9719,_binary 'Perform actions on the selected items in the %view_title view','','11.2.5'),(9720,_binary 'Find and manage content blocks.','','11.2.5'),(9721,_binary 'There are no content blocks available.','','11.2.5'),(9722,_binary 'Create and edit content blocks.','','11.2.5'),(9723,_binary 'Field %field_name exists but is missing a corresponding field definition and may be misconfigured.','','none'),(9724,_binary 'Enter 0 to show all comments.','','none'),(9725,_binary 'Viewing Drupal announcements','','11.2.5'),(9726,_binary 'What are Drupal announcements?','','11.2.5'),(9727,_binary 'A feed of announcements about the Drupal project and Drupal Association programs.','','11.2.5'),(9728,_binary 'The purpose of this feed is to provide a channel for outreach directly to Drupal site owners. This content must be highly relevant to site owners interests, serve the strategic goals of the project, and/or promote the sustainability of the project and the Drupal Association.','','11.2.5'),(9729,_binary 'The module sources its content from a JSON feed generated from <a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/about/announcements\">here</a>. The governance policy for the content is documented <a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/node/3274085\">here</a>.','','11.2.5'),(9730,_binary 'How can I see the Announcements in my site?','','11.2.5'),(9731,_binary 'If you have the toolbar module enabled, you will see a direct link to them in the toolbar. If the toolbar module is not enabled, the content can always be accessed in the <em>@actions_link</em> page.','','11.2.5'),(9732,_binary 'Who can see the Announcements?','','11.2.5'),(9733,_binary 'Users with the <em>@permissions_link</em> permission can view Drupal announcements.','','11.2.5'),(9734,_binary 'Announcement module overview','','11.2.5'),(9735,_binary 'Twig development mode','','none'),(9736,_binary 'Twig development mode settings are turned on. Go to @link to disable them.','','none'),(9737,_binary 'Markup caching disabled','','none'),(9738,_binary 'Render cache, dynamic page cache, and page cache are bypassed. Go to @link to enable them.','','none'),(9739,_binary 'Configure theme development settings','','11.2.5'),(9740,_binary 'These settings should only be enabled on development environments and never on production.','','none'),(9741,_binary 'Exposes Twig development settings.','','none'),(9742,_binary 'Provides Twig\'s <code>dump()</code> function for debugging, outputs template suggestions to HTML comments, and automatically recompile Twig templates after changes.','','none'),(9743,_binary 'Disable Twig cache','','none'),(9744,_binary 'Twig templates are not cached and are always compiled when rendered.','','none'),(9745,_binary 'Do not cache markup','','none'),(9746,_binary 'Disables render cache, dynamic page cache, and page cache.','','none'),(9747,_binary 'Your Drupal site\'s <code>composer.json</code> file must be valid according to <code>composer validate</code>. See <a href=\":url\">Composer\'s documentation</a> for more information.','','none'),(9748,_binary 'Composer must be configured for secure downloads. This means that <a href=\":disable-tls\">the <code>disable-tls</code> option</a> must be <code>false</code>, and <a href=\":secure-http\">the <code>secure-http</code> option</a> must be <code>true</code> in the <code>config</code> section of your <code>composer.json</code> file. If these options are not set in your <code>composer.json</code>, Composer will behave securely by default. To set these values at the command line, run the following commands:','','none'),(9749,_binary 'For more information, see the <a href=\":url\">online documentation for the Package Manager module</a>.','','none'),(9750,_binary 'FAQs related to Composer','','none'),(9751,_binary 'What if it says the <code>proc_open()</code> function is disabled on your PHP installation?','','none'),(9752,_binary 'Ask your system administrator to remove <code>proc_open()</code> from the <a href=\":url\">disable_functions</a> setting in <code>php.ini</code>.','','none'),(9753,_binary 'What if it says the <code>composer</code> executable cannot be found?','','none'),(9754,_binary 'What if it says the detected version of Composer is not supported?','','none'),(9755,_binary 'What if it says the <code>composer validate</code> command failed?','','none'),(9756,_binary 'Composer detected problems with your <code>composer.json</code> and/or <code>composer.lock</code> files, and the project is not in a completely valid state. See <a href=\":url\">the Composer documentation</a> for more information.','','none'),(9757,_binary 'Using rsync','','none'),(9758,_binary 'Enabling PHP-TUF protection','','none'),(9759,_binary 'Package Manager requires <a href=\":php-tuf\">PHP-TUF</a>, which implements <a href=\":tuf\">The Update Framework</a> as a way to help secure Composer package downloads via the <a href=\":php-tuf-plugin\">PHP-TUF Composer integration plugin</a>. This plugin must be installed and configured properly in order to use Package Manager.','','none'),(9760,_binary 'To install and configure the plugin as needed, you can run the following commands:','','none'),(9761,_binary 'Installation or removal of <code>cweagans/composer-patches</code> via Package Manager is not supported. You can install or remove it manually by running Composer commands in your site root.','','none'),(9762,_binary 'composer.lock not found in @dir.','','none'),(9763,_binary 'The detected Composer version, @version, does not satisfy <code>@constraint</code>.','','none'),(9764,_binary 'Any packages other than the implicitly allowed packages are not allowed to scaffold files. See <a href=\":url\">the scaffold documentation</a> for more information.','','none'),(9765,_binary '<code>@name</code>','','none'),(9766,_binary '<code>@name</code> is supported, but only version <code>@supported_version</code>, found <code>@installed_version</code>.','','none'),(9767,_binary 'Composer cannot be used because the <code>proc_open()</code> function is disabled.','','none'),(9768,_binary 'Unable to determine Composer <code>@key</code> setting.','','none'),(9769,_binary 'TLS must be enabled for HTTPS Composer downloads.','','none'),(9770,_binary '@message See <a href=\":url\">the help page</a> for more information on how to configure Composer to download packages securely.','','none'),(9771,_binary '@message See <a href=\":url\">the Composer documentation</a> for more information.','','none'),(9772,_binary 'You should also check the value of <code>secure-http</code> and make sure that it is set to <code>true</code> or not set at all.','','none'),(9773,_binary 'HTTPS must be enabled for Composer downloads.','','none'),(9774,_binary 'Composer settings don\'t satisfy Package Manager\'s requirements.','','none'),(9775,_binary '\'@name\' @type (provided by <code>@package</code>)','','none'),(9776,_binary 'The update cannot proceed because the following enabled Drupal extension was removed during the update.The update cannot proceed because the following enabled Drupal extensions were removed during the update.','','none'),(9777,_binary '<a href=\":url\">@message</a>','','none'),(9778,_binary 'Problem detected in lock file during stage operations.Problems detected in lock file during stage operations.','','none'),(9779,_binary 'The OpenSSL extension is not enabled, which is a security risk. See <a href=\":url\">the PHP documentation</a> for information on how to enable this extension.','','none'),(9780,_binary 'The active directory is not protected by PHP-TUF, which is required to use Package Manager securely.','','none'),(9781,_binary 'The stage directory is not protected by PHP-TUF, which is required to use Package Manager securely.','','none'),(9782,_binary 'The <code>@plugin</code> plugin is not installed.','','none'),(9783,_binary '@message See <a href=\":url\">the help page</a> for more information on how to install the plugin.','','none'),(9784,_binary 'The <code>@plugin</code> plugin is not listed as an allowed plugin.','','none'),(9785,_binary '@message See <a href=\":url\">the help page</a> for more information on how to configure the plugin.','','none'),(9786,_binary '@message See <a href=\":url\">the help page</a> for more information on how to set up this repository.','','none'),(9787,_binary '@message See the <a href=\":url\">Package Manager help</a> for more information on how to resolve this.','','none'),(9788,_binary '<code>rsync</code> is not available.','','none'),(9789,_binary '@project_name (@package_name) @version','','none'),(9790,_binary 'The Password Compatibility module provides the password checking algorithm for user accounts created with Drupal prior to version 10.1.0. For more information, see the <a href=\":phpass\">online documentation for the Password Compatibility module</a>.','','none'),(9791,_binary 'Drupal 10.1.0 and later use a different algorithm to compute the hashed password. This provides better security against brute-force attacks. The hashed passwords are different from the ones computed with Drupal versions before 10.1.0.','','none'),(9792,_binary 'When the Password Compatibility module is installed, a user can log in with a username and password created before Drupal 10.1.0. The first time these credentials are used, a new hash is computed and saved. From then on, the user will be able to log in with the same username and password whether or not this module is installed.','','none'),(9793,_binary 'Passwords created before Drupal 10.1.0 <strong>will not work</strong> unless they are used at least once while this module is installed. Make sure that you can log in before uninstalling this module.','','none'),(9794,_binary 'Make sure that you can log in before uninstalling the Password Compatibility module. For more information, see the <a href=\":phpass\">online documentation for the Password Compatibility module</a>.','','none'),(9795,_binary 'Provides the password checking algorithm for user accounts created with Drupal prior to version 10.1.0.','','none'),(9796,_binary '* (any version)','','none'),(9797,_binary '- Install @name @constraint','','none'),(9798,_binary '- Update @name from @installed_version to @constraint','','none'),(9799,_binary '- Updated @name from @installed_version to @updated_version','','none'),(9800,_binary '- Installed @name @version','','none'),(9801,_binary '- Uninstalled @name','','none'),(9802,_binary 'Applied changes:\n@change_list','','none'),(9803,_binary 'Users with the \"View drupal.org announcements\" permission may click on the \"Announcements\" item in the administration toolbar, or access @link, to see all announcements relevant to the Drupal version of your site.','','none'),(9804,_binary 'Database updates have been detected in the following extensions.','','none'),(9805,_binary 'The project root directory \"@dir\" is not writable.','','none'),(9806,_binary 'Unable to send password reset email for blocked or not yet activated user %identifier.','','none'),(9807,_binary 'Unable to send password reset email for unrecognized username or email address %identifier.','','none'),(9808,_binary 'A fresh Drupal installation only uses supported Composer plugins, but some modules or themes may depend on additional Composer plugins. <a href=\":new-issue\">Create a new issue</a> when you encounter this.','','none'),(9809,_binary 'Composer version','','none'),(9810,_binary '@version (<code>@path</code>)','','none'),(9811,_binary 'Composer was not found. The error message was: @message','','none'),(9812,_binary 'Unexpected changes were detected in the active lock file (@file), which indicates that other Composer operations were performed since this Package Manager operation started. This can put the code base into an unreliable state and therefore is not allowed.','','none'),(9813,_binary 'There appear to be no pending Composer operations because the active lock file (@active_file) and the staged lock file (@staged_file) are identical.','','none'),(9814,_binary 'Related recipes','','none'),(9815,_binary 'Related recipes listing','','none'),(9816,_binary 'Collapse sidebar','','none'),(9817,_binary 'Expand sidebar','','none'),(9818,_binary 'The %field date is invalid. Enter a date in the correct format.','','none'),(9819,_binary 'Properties are unchanged','Validation','none'),(9820,_binary 'The \'@name\' property cannot be changed.','','none'),(9821,_binary 'The website encountered an unexpected error. Try again later.','','11.2.5'),(9822,_binary 'Field to store a true or false value.','','none'),(9823,_binary 'Field to store an email address.','','none'),(9824,_binary 'The minimum value must be less than or equal to %max.','','none'),(9825,_binary 'Security warning: Couldn\'t write .htaccess file. Create a .htaccess file in your %directory directory which contains the following lines: <pre><code>@htaccess</code></pre>','','none'),(9826,_binary 'Entry @human_index: @validation_error_message','','none'),(9827,_binary 'Symfony mailer (Experimental)','','none'),(9828,_binary 'The email address %mail is not valid. Use the format user@example.com.','','none'),(9829,_binary 'You cannot use an external URL. Enter a relative path.','','none'),(9830,_binary 'Announcements Feed','','11.2.5'),(9831,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/user_guide/en/blocks-chapter.html\">Blocks (Drupal User Guide)</a>','','11.2.5'),(9832,_binary 'The human-readable name for this block type, displayed on the <em>Block types</em> page.','','11.2.5'),(9833,_binary 'Unique machine-readable name: lowercase letters, numbers, and underscores only.','','11.2.5'),(9834,_binary 'Displays on the <em>Block types</em> page.','','11.2.5'),(9835,_binary 'Working with breakpoints in Drupal','','11.2.5'),(9836,_binary 'Allowed list attributes','','none'),(9837,_binary 'Allow blocks to be created in list items','','none'),(9838,_binary 'An error occurred while trying to preview the media. Save your work and reload this page.','','none'),(9839,_binary 'The list of languages in the CKEditor \"Language\" dropdown can present the <a href=\":united-nations-official\">@count_united_nations official languages of the UN</a>, all @count_predefined languages predefined in Drupal, or the <a href=\":admin-configure-languages\">@count_configured languages configured for this site</a>.','','none'),(9840,_binary 'The list of languages in the CKEditor \"Language\" dropdown can present the <a href=\":united-nations-official\">@count_united_nations official languages of the UN</a>, all @count_predefined languages predefined in Drupal, or the languages configured for this site.','','none'),(9841,_binary 'United Nations\' official languages (@count)','','none'),(9842,_binary 'Drupal predefined languages (@count)','','none'),(9843,_binary 'Site-configured languages (@count)','','none'),(9844,_binary 'Allow the user to create paragraphs in list items (or other block elements)','','none'),(9845,_binary 'Edit %label comment type','','none'),(9846,_binary 'The human-readable name for this comment type, displayed on the <em>Comment types</em> page.','','none'),(9847,_binary 'Displays on the <em>Comment types</em> page.','','none'),(9848,_binary 'Comments and the comment form are hidden from view.','','none'),(9849,_binary 'the form displayed on the default contact page','','11.2.5'),(9850,_binary 'Set a site-wide contact form to be the default contact form (@contact_page_link; for example, <em>/contact</em>).','','11.2.5'),(9851,_binary 'Error sending auto-reply, missing sender email address in %contact_form','','none'),(9852,_binary 'Add %label for @entity-type','','none'),(9853,_binary 'This text will be displayed on the @mode_label list page.','','none'),(9854,_binary 'Enable this @display-mode for the following @bundle-label types:','','none'),(9855,_binary 'This @display-mode will still be available for the rest of the @bundle-label types if not checked here, but it will not be enabled by default.','','none'),(9856,_binary '<a href=\":url\">Configure the %display_mode_label %mode mode for %bundle_label</a>.','','none'),(9857,_binary 'The field %field has been deleted from the %type %source_label.','','none'),(9858,_binary 'There was a problem removing the %field from the %type %source_label.','','none'),(9859,_binary 'Field Storage','','11.2.5'),(9860,_binary 'An error occurred while saving the field: @error','','none'),(9861,_binary 'Choose a type of field','','none'),(9862,_binary 'Sanitize filenames','','none'),(9863,_binary 'These settings only apply to new files as they are uploaded. Changes here do not affect existing file names.','','none'),(9864,_binary 'Dash (-)','','none'),(9865,_binary 'Used when replacing whitespace, replacing non-alphanumeric characters or transliterating unknown characters.','','none'),(9866,_binary 'Transliteration replaces any characters that are not alphanumeric, underscores, periods or hyphens with the replacement character. It ensures filenames only contain ASCII characters. It is recommended to keep transliteration enabled.','','none'),(9867,_binary 'Replace whitespace with the replacement character','','none'),(9868,_binary 'Replace non-alphanumeric characters with the replacement character','','none'),(9869,_binary 'Alphanumeric characters, dots <span aria-hidden=\"true\">(.)</span>, underscores <span aria-hidden=\"true\">(_)</span> and dashes <span aria-hidden=\"true\">(-)</span> are preserved.','','none'),(9870,_binary 'Replace sequences of dots, underscores and/or dashes with the replacement character','','none'),(9871,_binary 'Uploaded filename sanitization options','','none'),(9872,_binary 'Replace whitespace','','none'),(9873,_binary 'Replace non-alphanumeric characters except dot, underscore and dash','','none'),(9874,_binary 'Character to use in replacements','','none'),(9875,_binary 'File Extension','Validation','none'),(9876,_binary 'File Extension Secure','Validation','none'),(9877,_binary 'File Image Dimensions','Validation','none'),(9878,_binary 'File Is Image','Validation','none'),(9879,_binary 'File Name Length','Validation','none'),(9880,_binary 'File Size Limit','Validation','none'),(9881,_binary 'The Help module generates <a href=\":help-page\">Help topics and reference pages</a> to guide you through the use and configuration of modules, and provides a Help block with page-level help. The reference pages are a starting point for <a href=\":handbook\">Drupal.org online documentation</a> pages that contain more extensive and up-to-date information, are annotated with user-contributed comments, and serve as the definitive reference point for all Drupal documentation. For more information, see the <a href=\":help\">online documentation for the Help module</a>.','','none'),(9882,_binary 'Modules and themes can provide help topics as Twig-file-based plugins in a project sub-directory called <em>help_topics</em>; plugin meta-data is provided in YAML front matter within each Twig file. Plugin-based help topics provided by modules and themes will automatically be updated when a module or theme is updated. Use the plugins in <em>core/modules/help/help_topics</em> as a guide when writing and formatting a help topic plugin for your theme or module.','','none'),(9883,_binary 'Use help pages','','11.2.5'),(9884,_binary 'Extending and Customizing Your Site (Drupal User Guide)','','11.2.5'),(9885,_binary 'Theming Drupal','','11.2.5'),(9886,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/configuration-management/workflow-using-drush\">Configuration Management: Workflow using Drush</a>','','11.2.5'),(9887,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/user_guide/en/understanding-data.html\">Concept: Types of Data (Drupal User Guide)</a>','','11.2.5'),(9888,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/user_guide/en/install-dev-sites.html\">Concept: Development Sites (Drupal User Guide)</a>','','11.2.5'),(9889,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/user_guide/en/install-dev-making.html\">Making a Development Site (Drupal User Guide)</a>','','11.2.5'),(9890,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/user_guide/en/planning-chapter.html\">Planning your Site (Drupal User Guide)</a>','','11.2.5'),(9891,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/user_guide/en/structure-reference-fields.html\">Concept: Reference Fields (Drupal User Guide)</a>','','11.2.5'),(9892,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/user_guide/en/security-cron-concept.html\">Concept: Cron (Drupal User Guide)</a>','','11.2.5'),(9893,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/user_guide/en/security-cron.html\">Configuring Cron Maintenance Tasks (Drupal User Guide)</a>','','11.2.5'),(9894,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/user_guide/en/understanding-modules.html\">Concept: Modules (Drupal User Guide)</a>','','11.2.5'),(9895,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/user_guide/en/extend-chapter.html\">Extending and Customizing Your Site (Drupal User Guide)</a>','','11.2.5'),(9896,_binary 'When performing maintenance, such as installing, uninstalling, or updating a module, put your site in maintenance mode.','','11.2.5'),(9897,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/user_guide/en/prevent-chapter.html\">Preventing and Fixing Problems (Drupal User Guide)</a>','','11.2.5'),(9898,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/user_guide/en/security-chapter.html\">Security and Maintenance (Drupal User Guide)</a>','','11.2.5'),(9899,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/user_guide/en/menu-concept.html\">Concept: Menu (Drupal User Guide)</a>','','11.2.5'),(9900,_binary 'The following core software modules and mechanisms can improve your site\'s performance:','','11.2.5'),(9901,_binary 'The following administrative interface components are provided by the core software and its modules (some contributed modules offer additional functionality):','','11.2.5'),(9902,_binary 'The following core software modules provide web services:','','11.2.5'),(9903,_binary 'Provides a way for web services to be authenticated using HTTP Basic authentication against site user accounts.','','11.2.5'),(9904,_binary 'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>@extend_link</em>. Verify that the Search, Help, and Block modules are installed (or install them if they are not already installed).','','11.2.5'),(9905,_binary 'Working with help topics','','11.2.5'),(9906,_binary 'What is a help topic?','','11.2.5'),(9907,_binary 'A help topic describes a concept, or steps to accomplish a task, related to a feature provided by one or more modules or themes. If the core Search module is enabled, these topics are also searchable.','','11.2.5'),(9908,_binary 'Where are help topics listed?','','11.2.5'),(9909,_binary 'The top-level help topics are listed at @help_link. Links to other topics, including non-top-level help topics, can be found under the \"Related\" heading when viewing a topic page.','','11.2.5'),(9910,_binary 'How are help topics provided?','','11.2.5'),(9911,_binary 'Modules and themes can provide help topics as Twig-file-based plugins in a project sub-directory called <em>help_topics</em>; plugin metadata is provided in YAML front matter within each Twig file. Plugin-based help topics provided by modules and themes will automatically be updated when a module or theme is updated. Use the plugins in <em>core/modules/help/help_topics</em> as a guide when writing and formatting a help topic plugin for your theme or module.','','11.2.5'),(9912,_binary 'How are help topics translated?','','11.2.5'),(9913,_binary 'The title and body text of help topics provided by contributed modules and themes are translatable using @translate_link (provided by Interface Translation module). Topics provided by custom modules and themes are also translatable if they have been viewed at least once in a non-English language, which triggers putting their translatable text into the translation database.','','11.2.5'),(9914,_binary 'How can users search for help topics?','','11.2.5'),(9915,_binary 'To enable users to search help, including help topics, you will need to install the core Search module, configure a search page, and add a search block to the Help page or another administrative page. (A search page is provided automatically, and if you use the core Claro administrative theme, a help search block is shown on the main Help page.) Then users with search permissions, and permission to view help, will be able to search help. See the related topic, @help_search_topic, for step-by-step instructions.','','11.2.5'),(9916,_binary 'Help Topics Standards','','11.2.5'),(9917,_binary 'Field to reference media. Allows uploading and selecting from uploaded media.','','none'),(9918,_binary 'The human-readable name for this media type, displayed on the <em>Media types</em> page.','','none'),(9919,_binary 'Displays on the <em>Media types</em> page.','','none'),(9920,_binary 'There are currently @total items selected. The maximum number of items for the field is @max. Remove @count item from the selection.There are currently @total items selected. The maximum number of items for the field is @max. Remove @count items from the selection.','','none'),(9921,_binary 'There are no allowed media types configured for this field. Contact the site administrator.','','none'),(9922,_binary 'Provides data migration from older versions of the core software into a new site.','','none'),(9923,_binary 'Provides a user interface for performing data migration from older versions of the core software into a new site.','','none'),(9924,_binary 'If the source of the data you want to migrate is a different content management system, or if the data source is a site that was built using contributed modules that the core migration modules do not support, then you will also need one or more contributed or custom modules in order to migrate your data.','','none'),(9925,_binary 'Migration @migration_id: Source ID @source_id: @message','','none'),(9926,_binary 'The publication status of the node (\"Published\" or \"Unpublished\").','','none'),(9927,_binary 'Basic Page Management (Drupal User Guide)','','11.2.5'),(9928,_binary 'Creating a Content Item (Drupal User Guide)','','11.2.5'),(9929,_binary 'Adding a Content Type (Drupal User Guide)','','11.2.5'),(9930,_binary 'Setting Up Content Structure (Drupal User Guide)','','11.2.5'),(9931,_binary 'Editing a Content Item (Drupal User Guide)','','11.2.5'),(9932,_binary 'The human-readable name for this content type, displayed on the <em>Content types</em> page.','','none'),(9933,_binary 'Displays on the <em>Content types</em> page.','','none'),(9934,_binary '@language_name revisions for %title','','none'),(9935,_binary 'The date and time that the content was created.','','none'),(9936,_binary 'The name will be used in displayed options and edit forms. The value is the stored value, and must be numeric.','','none'),(9937,_binary 'Cannot be removed: option in use.','','none'),(9938,_binary 'Adding a new item...','','none'),(9939,_binary 'The name will be used in displayed options and edit forms.','','none'),(9940,_binary 'The value is automatically generated machine name of the name provided and will be the stored value.','','none'),(9941,_binary 'Concept: Paths, Aliases, and URLs (Drupal User Guide)','','11.2.5'),(9942,_binary 'Number of items to index per run','','none'),(9943,_binary 'The maximum number of items processed per indexing run. If necessary, reduce the number of items to prevent timeouts and memory errors while indexing. Some search page types may have their own setting for this.','','none'),(9944,_binary 'Changing these settings will cause the default search index to be rebuilt to reflect the new settings. Searching will continue to work, based on the existing index, but new content will not be indexed until all existing content has been re-indexed.','','none'),(9945,_binary 'Enter some keywords.','','none'),(9946,_binary 'Make sure that the core Shortcut module is installed, and that you have a role with <em>Edit current shortcut set</em> or <em>Administer shortcuts</em> permission. Also, make sure that a toolbar module is installed (either the core Toolbar module or a contributed module replacement).','','11.2.5'),(9947,_binary 'Output Buffering','','none'),(9948,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.ob-start.php\">Output buffering</a> is not enabled. This may degrade Drupal\'s performance. You can enable output buffering by default <a href=\"https://www.php.net/manual/en/outcontrol.configuration.php#ini.output-buffering\">in your PHP settings</a>.','','none'),(9949,_binary 'Multibyte string input conversion in PHP is active and must be disabled. Check the php.ini <em>mbstring.encoding_translation</em> setting. Refer to the <a href=\"http://php.net/mbstring\">PHP mbstring documentation</a> for more information.','','none'),(9950,_binary 'Symfony mailer transport DSN','','none'),(9951,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/user_guide/en/prevent-cache.html\">Concept: Cache (Drupal User Guide)</a>','','11.2.5'),(9952,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/user_guide/en/security-chapter.html\">Security and Maintenance (Drupal User Guide)</a>, which includes information on how to update your site\'s core software, modules, and themes.','','11.2.5'),(9953,_binary 'Log in to access this page.','','none'),(9954,_binary 'Note that the administration theme is still set to the %admin_theme theme; consequently, the theme on this page remains unchanged. All non-administrative sections of the site, however, will show the selected %selected_theme theme by default.','','none'),(9955,_binary 'The selected modules could not be uninstalled, either due to a website problem or due to the uninstall confirmation form timing out.','','none'),(9956,_binary 'Success (@status_code)','','11.2.5'),(9957,_binary 'Access denied (@status_code)','','11.2.5'),(9958,_binary 'Page not found (@status_code)','','11.2.5'),(9959,_binary 'Shows the block on pages with any matching response status. If nothing is checked, the block is shown on all pages. Other response statuses are not used.','','11.2.5'),(9960,_binary 'Request response code is not: @codesRequest response code is not one of the following: @codes','','none'),(9961,_binary 'Request response code is: @codesRequest response code is one of the following: @codes','','none'),(9962,_binary 'Creates a new transparent object and sets it for the image.','','none'),(9963,_binary 'Setting Up a Taxonomy (Drupal User Guide)','','11.2.5'),(9964,_binary 'Concept: Taxonomy (Drupal User Guide)','','11.2.5'),(9965,_binary 'An invalid vocabulary is selected. Change it in the options.','','none'),(9966,_binary 'This field stores a telephone number.','','none'),(9967,_binary 'Another user (%other_user) is already logged into the site on this computer, but you tried to use a one-time link for user %resetting_user. <a href=\":logout\">Log out</a> and try using the link again.','','none'),(9968,_binary 'You have tried to use a one-time login link that has expired. Request a new one using the form below.','','none'),(9969,_binary 'You have tried to use a one-time login link that has either been used or is no longer valid. Request a new one using the form below.','','none'),(9970,_binary 'You have tried to use an account cancellation link that has expired. Request a new one using the form below.','','none'),(9971,_binary 'Filter by permission name','','11.2.5'),(9972,_binary '<a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/docs/user_guide/en/views-chapter.html\">Creating Listings with Views (Drupal User Guide)</a>','','11.2.5'),(9973,_binary '%current_display: The link in the %area area points to the %linked_display display which uses different settings than the %current_display display for: %unequal_options. To make sure users see the exact same result when clicking the link, check that the settings are the same.','','none'),(9974,_binary 'Numeric placeholders may not be used. Use plain placeholders (%).','','none'),(9975,_binary 'If checked, multiple values for this field will be shown in the same row. If not checked, each value in this field will create a new row. If using group by, make sure to group by \"Entity ID\" for this setting to have any effect.','','none'),(9976,_binary 'This will appear in the URL after the ? to identify this filter. Cannot be blank. Only letters, digits and the dot (\".\"), hyphen (\"-\"), underscore (\"_\"), and tilde (\"~\") characters are allowed. @reserved_identifiers are reserved words and cannot be used.','','none'),(9977,_binary 'Negated regular expression','','none'),(9978,_binary 'Hero tiny','','none'),(9979,_binary 'Hero medium','','none'),(9980,_binary 'Hero large','','none'),(9981,_binary 'Hero wide','','none'),(9982,_binary 'Scale crop 7:3 medium','','none'),(9983,_binary 'Scale crop 7:3 small','','none'),(9984,_binary 'Scale crop 7:3 tiny','','none'),(9985,_binary 'Scale crop 7:3 wide','','none'),(9986,_binary 'Sark','','none'),(9987,_binary 'Türkiye','','none'),(9988,_binary 'CKEditor 5 has to be installed and configured separately for individual text formats from the <a href=\":formats\">Text formats and editors page</a> because the filter settings for each text format can be different. For more information, see the <a href=\":text_editor\">Text Editor help page</a> and <a href=\":filter\">Filter help page</a>.','','none'),(9989,_binary 'The <code>@tag</code> tag is not yet supported by the Style plugin.','','none'),(9990,_binary 'Comment functionality can be enabled for any entity sub-type (for example, a <a href=\":content-type\">content type</a>) by adding a <em>Comments</em> field on its <em>Manage fields page</em>. Adding or removing commenting for an entity through the user interface requires the <a href=\":field_ui\">Field UI</a> module to be installed, even though the commenting functionality works without it. For more information on fields and entities, see the <a href=\":field\">Field module help page</a>.','','none'),(9991,_binary 'Commenting settings can be configured by editing the <em>Comments</em> field on the <em>Manage fields page</em> of an entity type if the <em>Field UI module</em> is installed. Configuration includes the label of the comments field, the number of comments to be displayed, and whether they are shown in threaded list. Commenting can be configured as: <em>Open</em> to allow new comments, <em>Closed</em> to view existing comments, but prevent new comments, or <em>Hidden</em> to hide existing comments and prevent new comments. Changing this configuration for an entity type will not change existing entity items.','','none'),(9992,_binary 'If you have the <a href=\":toolbar\">Toolbar module</a> installed, clicking the contextual links button in the toolbar (which looks like a pencil) will make all contextual links buttons on the page visible. Clicking this button again will toggle them to invisible.','','none'),(9993,_binary 'The Field module provides the infrastructure for fields; the field types, formatters, and widgets are provided by Drupal core or additional modules. Some of the modules are required; the optional modules can be installed from the <a href=\":modules\">Extend administration page</a>. Additional fields, formatters, and widgets may be provided by contributed modules, which you can find in the <a href=\":contrib\">contributed module section of Drupal.org</a>.','','none'),(9994,_binary 'Here is a list of the currently installed field, formatter, and widget modules:','','none'),(9995,_binary 'The Field UI module provides an administrative user interface (UI) for managing and displaying fields. Fields can be attached to most content entity sub-types. Different field types, widgets, and formatters are provided by the modules installed on your site, and managed by the Field module. For background information and terminology related to fields and entities, see the <a href=\":field\">Field module help page</a>. For more information about the Field UI, see the <a href=\":field_ui_docs\">online documentation for the Field UI module</a>.','','none'),(9996,_binary 'There are two reports available that list the fields defined on your site. The <a href=\":entity-list\" title=\"Entities field list report\">Entities</a> report lists all your fields, showing the field machine names, types, and the entity types or sub-types they are used on (each sub-type links to the Manage fields page). If the <a href=\":views\">Views</a> and <a href=\":views-ui\">Views UI</a> modules are installed, the <a href=\":views-list\" title=\"Used in views field list report\">Used in views</a> report lists each field that is used in a view, with a link to edit that view.','','none'),(9997,_binary 'You can create and edit text formats on the <a href=\":formats\">Text formats page</a> (if the Text Editor module is installed, this page is named Text formats and editors). One text format is included by default: Plain text (which removes all HTML tags). Additional text formats may be created during installation. You can create a text format by clicking \"<a href=\":add_format\">Add text format</a>\".','','none'),(9998,_binary '<strong>Enable additional functionality</strong> Next, visit the <a href=\":modules\">Extend page</a> and install modules that suit your specific needs. You can find additional modules at the <a href=\":download_modules\">Drupal.org modules page</a>.','','none'),(9999,_binary 'Help topics provided by modules and themes are also part of the Help module. If the core Search module is installed, these topics are searchable. For more information, see the <a href=\":online\">online documentation, Help Topic Standards</a>.','','none'),(10000,_binary 'A few of the settings for image fields are defined once when you create the field and cannot be changed later; these include the choice of public or private file storage and the number of images that can be stored in the field. The rest of the settings can be edited later; these settings include the field label, help text, allowed file extensions, image dimensions restrictions, and the subdirectory in the public or private file storage where the images will be stored. The editable settings can also have different values for different entity sub-types; for instance, if your image field is used on both Page and Article content types, you can store the files in a different subdirectory for the two content types.','','none'),(10001,_binary 'You can also configure a minimum and/or maximum dimensions for uploaded images. Images that are too small will be rejected. Images that are to large will be resized. During the resizing the <a href=\"http://wikipedia.org/wiki/Exchangeable_image_file_format\">EXIF data</a> in the image will be lost.','','none'),(10002,_binary 'Minimum image dimensions','','none'),(10003,_binary 'The Language module allows you to configure the languages used on your site, and provides information for the <a href=\":content\">Content Translation</a>, <a href=\":interface\">Interface Translation</a>, and <a href=\":configuration\">Configuration Translation</a> modules, if they are installed. For more information, see the <a href=\":doc_url\">online documentation for the Language module</a>.','','none'),(10004,_binary 'You can add languages on the <a href=\":language_list\">Languages</a> page by selecting <em>Add language</em> and choosing a language from the drop-down menu. This language is then displayed in the languages list, where it can be configured further. If the <a href=\":interface\">Interface translation module</a> is installed, and the <em>translation server</em> is set as a translation source, then the interface translation for this language is automatically downloaded as well.','','none'),(10005,_binary 'If the Block module is installed, then you can add a language switcher block on the <a href=\":blocks\">Block layout</a> page to allow users to switch between languages.','','none'),(10006,_binary 'If the Block module is installed, then the Language module allows you to set the visibility of a block based on selected languages on the <a href=\":blocks\">Block layout</a> page.','','none'),(10007,_binary 'Translation files with translated interface text are imported automatically when languages are added on the <a href=\":languages\">Languages</a> page, or when modules or themes are installed. On the <a href=\":locale-settings\">Interface translation settings</a> page, the <em>Translation source</em> can be restricted to local files only, or to include the <a href=\":server\">Drupal translation server</a>. Although modules and themes may not be fully translated in all languages, new translations become available frequently. You can specify whether and how often to check for translation file updates and whether to overwrite existing translations on the <a href=\":locale-settings\">Interface translation settings</a> page. You can also manually import a translation file on the <a href=\":import\">Interface translation import</a> page.','','none'),(10008,_binary 'Interface translations are automatically imported when a language is added, or when new modules or themes are installed. The report <a href=\":update\">Available translation updates</a> shows the status. Interface text can be customized in the <a href=\":translate\">user interface translation</a> page.','','11.2.5'),(10009,_binary 'Translation files are automatically downloaded and imported when <a title=\"Languages\" href=\":language\">languages</a> are added, or when modules or themes are installed.','','none'),(10010,_binary 'Use <em>Media</em> reference fields for most files, images, audio, videos, and remote media. Use <em>File</em> or <em>Image</em> reference fields when creating your own media types, or for legacy files and images created before installing the Media module.','','none'),(10011,_binary 'Revert %type_name: Revert media revisions','','none'),(10012,_binary 'Delete %type_name: Delete media revisions','','none'),(10013,_binary 'For more information, see the <a href=\":drupal-org-help\">online documentation for the Custom Menu Links module</a>. If you install the Menu UI module, it provides an interface for managing menus and menu links.','','none'),(10014,_binary 'If you have the Block module installed, then each menu that you create is rendered in a block that you enable and position on the <a href=\":blocks\">Block layout page</a>. In some <a href=\":themes\">themes</a>, the main menu and possibly the secondary menu will be output automatically; you may be able to disable this behavior on the <a href=\":themes\">theme\'s settings page</a>.','','none'),(10015,_binary 'You need to install all modules on this site that are installed on the previous site. For example, if you have used the Book module on the previous site then you must install the Book module on this site for that data to be available on this site.','','none'),(10016,_binary 'The RESTful Web Services module provides a framework for exposing REST resources on your site. It provides support for content entity types such as the main site content, comments, content blocks, taxonomy terms, and user accounts, etc. (see the <a href=\":field\">Field module help page</a> for more information about entities). REST support for content items of the Node module is installed by default, and support for other types of content entities can be enabled. Other modules may add support for other types of REST resources. For more information, see the <a href=\":rest\">online documentation for the RESTful Web Services module</a>.','','none'),(10017,_binary 'Modules providing search page plugins generally ensure that content-related actions on your site (creating, editing, or deleting content and comments) automatically cause affected content items to be marked for indexing or reindexing at the next cron run. When content is marked for reindexing, the previous content remains in the index until cron runs, at which time it is replaced by the new content. However, there are some actions related to the structure of your site that do not cause affected content to be marked for reindexing. Examples of structure-related actions that affect content include deleting or editing taxonomy terms, installing or uninstalling modules that add text to content (such as Taxonomy, Comment, and field-providing modules), and modifying the fields or display parameters of your content types. If you take one of these actions and you want to ensure that the search index is updated to reflect your changed site structure, you can mark all content for reindexing by clicking the \"Re-index site\" button on the <a href=\":search-settings\">Search pages page</a>. If you have a lot of content on your site, it may take several cron runs for the content to be reindexed.','','none'),(10018,_binary 'The Search module includes a block, which can be enabled and configured on the <a href=\":blocks\">Block layout page</a>, if you have the Block module installed; the default block title is Search, and it is the Search form block in the Forms category, if you wish to add another instance. The block is available to users with the <a href=\":search_permission\">Use search</a> permission, and it performs a search using the configured default search page.','','none'),(10019,_binary 'The current date in \'short\' format. (%date)','','none'),(10020,_binary 'The current date in \'medium\' format. (%date)','','none'),(10021,_binary 'The current date in \'long\' format. (%date)','','none'),(10022,_binary 'The current date in a custom format. See <a href=\"https://www.php.net/manual/datetime.format.php#refsect1-datetime.format-parameters\">the PHP documentation</a> for details.','','none'),(10023,_binary 'The current date in \'time-since\' format. (%date)','','none'),(10024,_binary 'The current date in UNIX timestamp format (%date)','','none'),(10025,_binary 'The installed version of at least one of your modules or themes has been revoked and is no longer available for download. Upgrading or uninstalling is strongly recommended!','','none'),(10026,_binary 'The installed version of at least one of your modules or themes is no longer supported. Upgrading or uninstalling is strongly recommended. See the project homepage for more details.','','none'),(10027,_binary '<em>Roles</em> are used to group and classify users; each user can be assigned one or more roles. Typically there are two pre-defined roles: <em>Anonymous user</em> (users that are not logged in), and <em>Authenticated user</em> (users that are registered and logged in). Depending on how your site was set up, an <em>Administrator</em> role may also be available: users with this role will automatically be assigned any new permissions whenever a module is installed. You can create additional roles on the <a href=\":roles\">Roles administration page</a>.','','none'),(10028,_binary 'The <a href=\":accounts\">Account settings page</a> allows you to manage settings for the displayed name of the Anonymous user role, personal contact forms, user registration settings, and account cancellation settings. On this page you can also manage settings for account personalization, and adapt the text for the email messages that users receive when they register or request a password recovery. You may also set which role is automatically assigned new permissions whenever a module is installed (the Administrator role).','','none'),(10029,_binary 'In order to create and modify your own views using the administration and configuration user interface, you will need to install either the Views UI module in core or a contributed module that provides a user interface for Views. See the <a href=\":views-ui\">Views UI module help page</a> for more information.','','none'),(10030,_binary 'Stage directory cleaner','','none'),(10031,_binary 'The following @element_type(s) can optionally be supported by enabled plugins and should not be added to the Source Editing \"Manually editable HTML tags\" field: %overlapping_tags.','','none'),(10032,_binary 'Include unrecognized files and directories in the project root in staging operations','','none'),(10033,_binary 'The following paths in @project_root aren\'t recognized as part of your Drupal site, so to be safe, Package Manager is excluding them from all stage operations. If these files are not needed for Composer to work properly in your site, no action is needed. Otherwise, you can disable this behavior by setting the <code>package_manager.settings:include_unknown_files_in_project_root</code> config setting to <code>TRUE</code>.\n\n@list','','none'),(10034,_binary 'Text field that does not support markup.','','none'),(10035,_binary 'Field to store number. I.e. id, price, or quantity.','','none'),(10036,_binary 'Field to reference other content.','','none'),(10037,_binary 'Field to store date and time values.','','none'),(10038,_binary 'Field to upload any type of files.','','none'),(10039,_binary 'Selection list','','none'),(10040,_binary 'Field to select from predefined options.','','none'),(10041,_binary 'Text field with markup support and optional editor.','','none'),(10042,_binary 'Checked version of %project.','','none'),(10043,_binary 'The UUID of the comment.','','none'),(10044,_binary 'New administration navigation','','none'),(10045,_binary 'Navigation blocks','','none'),(10046,_binary 'Manage navigation blocks.','','none'),(10047,_binary 'Access navigation bar','','none'),(10048,_binary 'Select Navigation logo handling','','none'),(10049,_binary 'Maximum file sizes (bytes)','','none'),(10050,_binary 'Choose logo handling','','none'),(10051,_binary 'Administrative toolbar content','','none'),(10052,_binary 'Administrative toolbar footer','','none'),(10053,_binary 'More actions','','none'),(10054,_binary 'Cannot update because the following new or updated Drupal package does not have project information: @unknown_packagesCannot update because the following new or updated Drupal packages do not have project information: @unknown_packages','','none'),(10055,_binary 'If the Interface Translation module is installed, this page will provide an overview of how much of the site\'s interface has been translated for each configured language.','','none'),(10056,_binary 'Depending on your site features, additional modules that you might want to install are:','','none'),(10057,_binary 'If you don\'t want to receive such messages, you can change your settings at @recipient-edit-url.','','none'),(10058,_binary 'This block is broken or missing. You may be missing content or you might need to install the original module.','','none'),(10059,_binary 'Translatable config has langcode','Validation','none'),(10060,_binary 'The @name config object must specify a language code, because it contains translatable values.','','none'),(10061,_binary 'The @name config object does not contain any translatable values, so it should not specify a language code.','','none'),(10062,_binary 'Edit @entity_label','','11.2.5'),(10063,_binary 'Edit @entity_bundle @entity_id','','none'),(10064,_binary 'Delete @entity_label','','11.2.5'),(10065,_binary 'Delete @entity_bundle @entity_id','','none'),(10066,_binary 'The install profile %profile is not in the list of installed modules.','','none'),(10067,_binary 'The install profile \'@profile_name\' is providing the following module(s): @profile_modules','','none'),(10068,_binary 'The install profile \'@profile_name\' is providing the following theme(s): @profile_themes','','none'),(10069,_binary 'The \'@profile_name\' install profile requires \'@module_name\'','','none'),(10070,_binary 'Ideal for exact counts and measures (prices, temperatures, distances, volumes, etc.)','','none'),(10071,_binary 'Stores a number in the database in a fixed decimal format','','none'),(10072,_binary 'For example, 12.34 km or € when used for further detailed calculations (such as summing many of these)','','none'),(10073,_binary 'In most instances, it is best to use Number (decimal) instead, as decimal numbers stored as floats may contain errors in precision','','none'),(10074,_binary 'This type of field offers faster processing and more compact storage, but the differences are typically negligible on modern sites','','none'),(10075,_binary 'For example, 123.4 km when used in imprecise contexts such as a walking trail distance','','none'),(10076,_binary 'Number without decimals','','none'),(10077,_binary 'For example, 123','','none'),(10078,_binary 'Ideal for titles and names','','none'),(10079,_binary 'Efficient storage for short text','','none'),(10080,_binary 'Requires specifying a maximum length','','none'),(10081,_binary 'Good for fields with known or predictable length','','none'),(10082,_binary 'Ideal for longer texts, like body or description','','none'),(10083,_binary 'Supports long text without specifying a maximum length','','none'),(10084,_binary 'May use more storage and be slower for searching and sorting','','none'),(10085,_binary 'Ideal for using date and time calculations or comparisons','','none'),(10086,_binary 'Date and time stored in the form of seconds since January 1, 1970 (UTC)','','none'),(10087,_binary 'Compact and efficient for storage, sorting and calculations','','none'),(10088,_binary 'The user %username does not have administrator access. For more information, see the documentation on <a href=\"@secure-user-1-docs\">securing the admin super user</a>.','','none'),(10089,_binary 'Default PHP Mailer','','none'),(10090,_binary 'CountryCode','Validation','none'),(10091,_binary 'Entity bundle exists','Validation','none'),(10092,_binary 'The \'@bundle\' bundle does not exist on the \'@entity_type_id\' entity type.','','none'),(10093,_binary 'Whether this config schema type is fully validatable','Validation','none'),(10094,_binary '\'@key\' is an unknown key because @dynamic_type_property_path is @dynamic_type_property_value (see config schema type @resolved_dynamic_type).','','none'),(10095,_binary '\'@key\' is a required key.','','none'),(10096,_binary '\'@key\' is a required key because @dynamic_type_property_path is @dynamic_type_property_value (see config schema type @resolved_dynamic_type).','','none'),(10097,_binary 'Move in any direction','','11.2.5'),(10098,_binary 'Your comment has been updated.','','none'),(10099,_binary '@id (@label)','','none'),(10100,_binary 'Limit (messages per interval)','','none'),(10101,_binary 'Interval (seconds)','','none'),(10102,_binary 'Ideal when date and time needs to be input by users, like event dates and times','','none'),(10103,_binary 'Date or date and time stored in a readable string format','','none'),(10104,_binary 'Easy to read and understand for humans','','none'),(10105,_binary 'Display both start and end dates','','none'),(10106,_binary 'Display start date only','','none'),(10107,_binary 'Display end date only','','none'),(10108,_binary 'Ideal for storing durations that consist of start and end dates (and times)','','none'),(10109,_binary 'Choose between setting both date and time, or date only, for each duration','','none'),(10110,_binary 'The system automatically validates that the end date (and time) is later than the start, and both fields are completed','','none'),(10111,_binary 'File already locked for writing.','','none'),(10112,_binary 'Bytes (KB, MB, ...)','','none'),(10113,_binary 'For uploading files','','none'),(10114,_binary 'Can be configured with options such as allowed file extensions and maximum upload size','','none'),(10115,_binary 'Temporary file data for could not be written','','none'),(10116,_binary 'Temporary file could not be opened for file upload','','none'),(10117,_binary 'No image toolkit is configured on the site. Check PHP installed extensions or add a contributed toolkit that doesn\'t require a PHP extension. Make sure that at least one valid image toolkit is installed.','','none'),(10118,_binary 'For uploading images','','none'),(10119,_binary 'Allows a user to upload an image with configurable extensions, image dimensions, upload size','','none'),(10120,_binary 'Can be configured with options such as allowed file extensions, maximum upload size and image dimensions minimums/maximums','','none'),(10121,_binary 'Missing file with ID %id.','','none'),(10122,_binary 'The \"@name\" at \"@target_entity_type_id:@target_bundle\" references the \"@entity_type_id:@bundle\" entity type that does not exist.','','none'),(10123,_binary 'For more information, see the <a href=\":href\">online documentation for the Layout Builder Expose All Field Blocks module</a>.','','none'),(10124,_binary 'Layout Builder Expose All Field Blocks','','none'),(10125,_binary 'When enabled, this module exposes all fields for all entity view displays. When disabled, only entity type bundles that have layout builder enabled will have their fields exposed. Enabling this module could significantly decrease performance on sites with a large number of entity types and bundles.','','none'),(10126,_binary 'Could not retrieve the remote URL (@url): %error','','none'),(10127,_binary 'Media Mapping Constraint','Validation','none'),(10128,_binary 'It is not possible to map the source field @source_field_name of a media type.','','none'),(10129,_binary 'Migration messages','','none'),(10130,_binary 'View the migration messages.','','none'),(10131,_binary 'View migration messages','','none'),(10132,_binary 'There are no migration message tables.','','none'),(10133,_binary 'No migration messages available.','','none'),(10134,_binary 'The message table is missing for this migration.','','none'),(10135,_binary 'When there is an error processing a row, the migration system saves the error message but not the source ID(s) of the row. That is why some messages in this table have \'Not available\' in the source ID column(s).','','none'),(10136,_binary 'The upgrade process may log messages about steps that require user action or errors. This page allows you to view these messages','','none'),(10137,_binary 'Review the detailed upgrade log.','','none'),(10138,_binary 'Enter credentials for the database of the Drupal site you want to upgrade, not the new site.','','none'),(10139,_binary 'Check whether there is translated content of these types:','','none'),(10140,_binary 'Possible ID conflicts for translations are not automatically detected in the current version of Drupal. Refer to the <a target=\"_blank\" href=\":id-conflicts-handbook\">Upgrading Drupal handbook</a> for instructions on how to avoid ID conflicts with translated content.','','none'),(10141,_binary '<strong>Install all modules on this new site</strong> that are enabled on the old site. For example, if the old site uses the Book module, then install the Book module on this new site so that the existing data can be imported to it.','','none'),(10142,_binary 'The Navigation module provides a left-aligned, collapsible, vertical sidebar navigation.','','none'),(10143,_binary 'For more information, see the <a href=\":docs\">online documentation for the Navigation module</a>.','','none'),(10144,_binary 'This layout builder tool allows you to configure the blocks in the navigation toolbar.','','none'),(10145,_binary 'Toolbar and Navigation modules are both installed','','none'),(10146,_binary 'The Navigation module is a complete replacement for the Toolbar module and disables its functionality when both modules are installed. If you are planning to continue using Navigation module, you can uninstall the Toolbar module now.','','none'),(10147,_binary 'Navigation Top Bar','','none'),(10148,_binary 'Saved navigation blocks','','none'),(10149,_binary 'Navigation Shortcuts','','none'),(10150,_binary 'Navigation flag','','none'),(10151,_binary 'Values stored are floating-point numbers','','none'),(10152,_binary 'For example, \'Fraction\': 0 => 0, .25 => 1/4, .75 => 3/4, 1 => 1','','none'),(10153,_binary 'Values stored are numbers without decimals','','none'),(10154,_binary 'For example, \'Lifetime in days\': 1 => 1 day, 7 => 1 week, 31 => 1 month','','none'),(10155,_binary 'Values stored are text values','','none'),(10156,_binary 'For example, \'US States\': IL => Illinois, IA => Iowa, IN => Indiana','','none'),(10157,_binary 'Specify the existing path you wish to alias. For example: /node/28, /media/1, /taxonomy/term/1.','','none'),(10158,_binary 'Install the Help module for more information on the sizes attribute.','','none'),(10159,_binary 'This theme requires the listed modules 